ious conclusions to be drawn here."9NOEL: This floor had 30 on light against 26 on dark."4On the dark side, there were only two Zweilous."%On the light side, there were..."ETwo Espeon, two Floette, a Florges, a Chingling, and a Granbull."Too much."2NOEL: 30 on the light side versus 26 on dark."That's a lot."gFrom what we know of previous floors, Espeon is 3, Floette is 3, Florges is 5, and Chingling is 2."6NOEL: This floor had 24 on light, and 21 on dark."�It's easy to figure out Zweilous' value from the previous floor, but even having opened the way, it's not clear from this floor alone what Murkrow or Houndour are worth."#NOEL: 24 on light, 21 on dark."5Everything is new except Zweilous, which was 13."6NOEL: This one was 18 on light versus 24 on dark."MGranbull and Togetic faced off against Houndour, Drifloon and Mandibuzz."1That seemed to be a very strong Mandibuzz..."#NOEL: 18 on light, 24 on dark."7On the light side, Granbull was 11, Togetic was 7."xOn the dark side, Houndour was on the previous floor but the numbers make it impossible to know its value for sure." It should be either 3 or 5.")NOEL: 20 on light versus 31 on dark."/I get the feeling that we're near the end."wAll of the values here are tecnically unknown, but we can infer relativistic properties based on their evolutions."KFor the sake of convenience, I'll list the evolutions we've confirmed:":For the light side, Cleffa and Chingling were both 2."zFor the dark side, Mismagius was 7, Mightyena was 5, Mandibuzz was a whopping 17, Umbreon was 3, and Zweilous was 13."ONOEL: In order to progress, we have to balance the power of the two sides."|Each Pokémon contributes a certain amount of power based on its species, expressed in a prime number between 1 and 20."9Also, neither side can reach a remaining power of 0."`There's no way to see what the immediate power of a side is; only what it is when we enter."6Ask me what the totals of each floor is whenever."UAlso, if you take me to previous floors, I'll probably remember their solutions."Just in case you forget."*NOEL: Sure, I can heal your Pokémon."7NOEL: This place looks so bland without any color."I guess it suits me.">NOEL: It's been a while since I saw a Cleffa like that..."INOEL: It's a good thing these levels don't consider type advantages."<I wonder if they're like Shadow type Pokémon that way."BNOEL: I think there are actually two solutions to this one..."uPrime numbers provide a lot of unique ways of creating sums, but a lot of unsolved problems have come from them."LFor instance, there's one... I think it's called the Golbat Conjecture?"ZThat states that every even number above two is the sum of at least two other primes."jI've been thinking about it as we do this, and every number I check, even through the billions, fits,"/But that still doesn't mean they all will."CI'm sorry I can't tell you the specific power values like Eve."NOEL: This is simple."Not easy."Just simple."ENOEL: The doctor never let us have Gym puzzles at the orphanage."JBut if I had been allowed to have one, maybe this would've been okay."&NOEL: I kind of miss Gym Battles."QThe calculations are imprecise, but that's what makes them more interesting."NTAKA: ...Father, Elena, Corey, Ame... They're all dead because of Meteor."[TAKA: Heather looks exactly like her mother. It's a shame she never got to meet her..."ZTAKA: Maybe it's the swords, but I have a pretty good idea who we're about to meet..."VTAKA: ...It was nice to meet Grandfather. He was nothing like I expected, though."BELIAS: Have I mentioned that I'm uncomfortable around swords?"/Particularly when people point them at me.",ELIAS: Amethyst, Elena... Even Phoenix."J...Would this all have gone differently if I let myself have friends?"2ELIAS: Heather looks so much like her mother."/...It's a shame she never got to meet her."FELIAS: If I had just tried to convince him Sirius was bad news..."+So many people would still be alive..."LIN: wait, hey"can i have a lemonade?"i h