s going to take a long time to repair."'The device was remotely triggered."bAccording to the radio signal, the detonation device had to have been in a fifty foot radius."AThen the culprit is most definitely around here somewhere..."&???: Another victim of the crash?"OQuit your snivelling and go to the back of the line like the rest of them."%Those who cut won't get treated,"6But all who wait will get what help can be given."6Whatever pain you feel, know it was not deserved."???: Can you stop shaking?"PATIENT: Y-yeah, sorry."It just hurts."_And I feel kind of just a little bit panicky after being in, like, an entire trainwreck..."*???: It is an understandable anxiety."0Hold still, and I will give you two tonics."One will calm the pain."One will calm your nerves.""PATIENT: Is that really safe?"???: It is safe."(I know because I created them both."�Neither is suitable to long term use, but if the need were to come up, I would not hesitate to use them on either myself or my daughter."pThe city, too, has decreed that they are beneficial enough to be worth asking me to come here and use them."#Does this belay your concerns?"PATIENT: Y-yeah..."=Sorry, you just kind of give off a scary vibe, you know?"9???: This is not the first time I've been told that."It will not be the last."9I lost my capacity for cheerful expression long ago."It was taken from me."<Those of you who can still smile should enjoy doing so,"+Just so long as it is not in delusion."PATIENT: Um."9???: It seems my stock of painkiller is running low."HNo matter; this last one will be enough for the remaining patients."(HOTSHOT: Wait, that's the last one?"?Shit, no way I'm waiting for it to get used up then. Move!"PATIENT: O-ow, hey!"0HOTSHOT: I'll be taking this, pops. Thanks!"???: Are you hurt worse?"\PATIENT: He shoved me out of the way pretty roughly, but it shouldn't be too much-- ow!"&???: Come. I can still treat you."/???: Trainer, I cannot leave this patient."tIf you have any inkling of goodwill in your body, I ask you to find that crook and recover my medical supplies.";Time is a key factor. Act fast or it will be too late."BHe fled north. That would be as good a place to start as any.";???: Our culprit forfeited the stolen goods after all."%I understand that was your work."It was acceptably done."HYou have both my gratitude, and that of our last remaining patient."$Along with it, an introduction."You may call me Corey."gCOREY: It is regrettable-- the circumstances that required us to gather here to treat the injured."6To reduce the influx, while allowing departure..."+To disrupt a necessary supply chain..."6To remove a lynchpin in the fabric of the city..."eHow many excuses will be used to justify a tragedy which claimed the lives of so many, I wonder?"..."=Incidentally, you were also on that train, were you not?"JAnd yet here you are, standing on the other side of the service line."0Do continue to carry yourself with respect."dThere is much that will require decisive action and strong presence of will in the coming days."-You may take these in aid of your cause."COREY: Until next we meet."#YOUTH: O-ow! Ugh, that stings!"???: Only temporarily."<The wound must be disinfected before it can be dressed."pIt may sting, but it will burn far worse should you ignore the problem, and by neglect, allow it to fester.")If that's what you want, I can stop." YOUTH: N-no, sir. Please..."r???: The transaction of short term pain for long term healing is a difficult one for the young to understand."Hold still."GYou do not have the experience to know why the world has hurt you.",You must trust the adults in your life."GAll too often they are incapable of adequately earning that trust."2This is the tragedy between every generation."'There. The difficult part is done."GNow I'll apply a numbing agent to relieve the pain while you wait."(That should be better already, yes?"YOUTH: Yes, sir..."???: Worth waiting for?"YOUTH: Yes, sir."???: Good."NNow wait a mite lo