NN: Here, of all places, though?"3ADRIENN: Well, let's start from the beginning."+That must be Vulpix, the Fox Pokémon!"It's an Alolan variety."It's a special variety."It's a Kantonian variety."It's a normal variety."Yes"NoIu;␀[["#Oy, this is my house. Git out!"#I guess it is public property."�Y'know, sometimes I do hafta share this place. There's this small-like Pokémon that sometimes comes down here when it's a-rainin'."PANSEAR: P-pan..."GPansear seems to be afraid of the rain... It's too scared to move."'Do you want to rescue the Pansear?"%There was no room for Pansear..."PANSEAR: P-Pan... sear..."PANPOUR: Pan~~"4Panpour seems to be enjoying watching the rain."It seems to want to play!"TEDDIURSA: Ursa!"Teddiursa fled!"Yes"No["&Oh! C'est ma piaule là. Dégage!")On va dire que c'est un lieu public."qTsais, je partage ma piaule en fait. Y a un petit Pokémon qui vient parfois s'planquer ici quand ça pleut."FLAMAJOU: F-fla..."JFlamajou semble avoir peur de la pluie... Il a trop peur pour bouger."%Voulez-vous recueillir Flamajou?"+Il n'y a pas de place pour Flamajou..." FLAMAJOU: F-fla... majou..."FLOTAJOU: Flota~~"3Flotajou a l'air heureux de regarder la pluie."Flotajou veut jouer!"TEDDIURSA: Ursa!"Teddiursa s'enfuit!"Oui"Non;["#Oy, this is my house. Git out!"#I guess it is public property."�Y'know, sometimes I do hafta share this place. There's this small-like Pokémon that sometimes comes down here when it's a-rainin'."PANSEAR: P-pan..."GPansear seems to be afraid of the rain... It's too scared to move."'Do you want to rescue the Pansear?"%There was no room for Pansear..."PANSEAR: P-Pan... sear..."PANPOUR: Pan~~"4Panpour seems to be enjoying watching the rain."It seems to want to play!"TEDDIURSA: Ursa!"Teddiursa fled!"Yes"No0Iu;␀u�[["ESPURR: Esp... ... ... ...")Espurr looks completely traumatized."AEspurr smells the PokéSnax! Espurr snapped back to reality!")Do you want to take Espurr with you?""There was no room for Espurr."ESPURR: ..."8It seems to have gone into shock and won't respond."MINCCINO: Min..."Minccino looks scared."EMinccino smells the PokéSnax! Minccino snapped back to reality!"+Do you want to take Minccino with you?"$There was no room for Minccino."MINCCINO: ..."SWINUB: Swin..."%Swinub is curled up into a ball."-Swinub smells the PokéSnax! It came to!")Do you want to take Swinub with you?""There was no room for Swinub."SWINUB: ..."*It doesn't seem to want to respond..."ARON: Ronron...")Aron is meekly looking at the floor."6Aron smells the PokéSnax! It looks up excitedly!"'Do you want to take Aron with you?" There was no room for Aron."ARON: ..."AIt seems to be looking back at the ground and won't respond."1Hey stranger, you know those online quizzes?"WLike "What's your true soul color?" or "Which Go-Rock Quad member would date you?""RSo I found one of those on this old website for "What Pokémon Type are you?"">Apparently every single type and combination is possible."jI already took it for myself, but I wanna see if other people really get that many different answers."%I'm Normal/Flying, bee-tee-dubs."Do you wanna try it?"gFair warning, it's like 36 questions long because apparently the writer doesn't know when to quit."$But wanna take the quiz anyway?" Wanna take that quiz again?"8Wanna take that "What Pokémon Type are you?" quiz?"Sweet! Okay, let's go."Let's start simple."iWhat's your favorite color?\ch[62,-1, Red, Yellow!, Green, Blue, Orange, Purple, Pink, White, Black]"What kind of weather do you find most appealing? \ch[62,-1, Clear and sunny!, Rain is comforting, A sandstorm would be awesome, Snow is pretty!, A relaxing overcast, I love when it's windy, Rainbows. Rainbows everywhere., I don't have a favorite weather., Hail is super cool!]"3What is your idea of "Success"?\ch[62,-1, Having lots of great friends!, A stable and progressive career, Lots of money, Finding true love, Success is when you stop chasing it, Being famous!, Enlightenment and acquisition of knowledge, Prestige; Reputation; Respectability, Anything as long as you're happy]"�What are you most afraid of?\ch[62,-1, I'm not afraid of anything, Rejection, Bugs are gross!, One specific very uncommon thing..., Losing those close to me, Missing out, Of staying the same forever, Myself, Like I'd tell you!]":Which best describes you?\ch[62,-1, I have friends but I'm still lonely, I'm always trying to run away, Others always misunderstand me, I drive everyone away, I end up regretting a lot of things, I'm not good enough at anything, Most people just ignore me, Others need to get on my level, Everything is pointless.]";How do you feel about relationships?\ch[62,-1, Like I always need to be in one, Who cares?, It would be nice to be cared for..., They're too often just a distraction, I do better alone., They can add a lot to life!, Thanks for reminding me :c, Self-acceptance is more important, I like having someone to look after]"4What's your ideal partner like?\ch[62,-1, Stable and level-headed, Hopeless romantics are cute, Romance is a capitalistic fabrication, I like the bad-ass types!, Rational and supportive, Someone who I can help find their voice, Honest and direct, Dreams big and chases hard, Someone who can keep up with me.]"RWhat are your ideal friends like?\ch[62,-1, Absolutely inseparable, Just around when I need them, Talk to me often but don't cling, We can just hang whenever, Loud and fun; likely to get into trouble!, Just one or two who know everything, I like knowing lots of different people, Ideally? I don't need friends, Always mutually supportive]"\How do those compare to your real friends?\ch[62,- 1, They usually are too chaotic..., We don't see eye-to-eye often, I'm content with my real friends, They don't know how much I miss them, They usually ignore me., My "real friends" dislike me, I love my friends and want to adopt them!, ...What real friends?, I'm usually keeping them together...]">Oh no! A Ninetales' curse has turned you into a Pokémon!"FYou've been cast out of your home and forced to live in the wild."WHow do you pass the time as a Pokémon?\ch[62,-1, Find food and shelter ASAP, I wanna explore!, I'd go look for some friends?, Time to try out my battling skills..., Just sleep I guess, Time to study Pokémon from their world!, Gonna go hunt that Ninetales..., I'll still find a way to be on the computer., There are so many ways to play now!]"2You just saw some other Pokémon in the area!"3How do you react to them?\ch[62,-1, Ignore them., Leave. It's not worth the trouble., Run away!, Just watch from afar, I'd watch but secretly hope they approach..., I'd go and see what's up, I'd introduce myself right away!, Skip the introductions-- let's play!, That depends on exactly what they're doing.]"ASuddenly the wild Pokémon get into a fight with each other!"JIt's your first time seeing a battle from a Pokémon's point of view!"YWhat do you do?\ch[62,-1, Get excited! Let's brawl!, Stay away; it's kind of scary, Consider the ethics of Pokémon battles..., Try to resolve the situation peacefully, Observe and pity the loser, It makes no difference to me anyway, It seems fun! Join in right away!, Wait for a chance to test your own skills, Study their technique to improve]"RAfter one of the Pokémon is knocked out, a human finds it and takes it away."kAfter the harsh battle, another human shows up and immediately captures the Pokémon that defeated it."�As a Pokémon, how do you feel about Trainers? \ch[62,-1, Having to do anything they say is scary, Having the company seems nice!, Pokémon capture must be unethical..., You just have to find the right Trainer., brb gonna go get a trainer rq, I don't need a Trainer to be awesome, The same as I did as a human, Regretting ever having captured Pokémon, I'd love to meet a lifelong companion!]"MYou meet some Pokémon of your same species, and tbh they're kinda cute!"DWhat do you do?\ch[62,-1, I'd introduce myself properly, No introductions; only play!, Keep my distance since I was human..., Maybe we can discuss Pokémon life?, I'd bring them food as a gift!, Just ignore them..., Play a prank as an excuse to talk~, 'Cute' is a shallow judgment. Irrelevant., I don't want to bother them.]"SUh oh! Suddenly a wild Houndoom appears and starts bullying the cute Pokémon!"4What will you do?\ch[62,-1, Tactical retreat!, Jump in and defend them!, Wait patiently for the right moment..., Taunt it away from the other one!, Pretend to be on its side; then strike!, I challenge it to an honest fight, Offer to help the Pokémon first, Not my problem., Hold on! Can't we talk this out?]"=Good news! The Houndoom left the other Pokémon alone..."&...But now it's onto you instead!".What's the plan?!\ch[62,-1, Keep it busy so the other can escape!, Forget it! Go back to the other Pokémon!, Bring it on., I will be the sacrifice..., Work together with the other one!, Intimidate Houndoom into quitting, Calm it down and solve the conflict, Duh-- Run!, Trick it with human knowledge!]"*One way or another, Houndoom is gone."ABut just after you've been attacked, a wild Trainer appears!"7He sees you're weak, and captures you immediately!"How do you feel about captivity?\ch[62,-1, FML., New friend!!!, I just hope he's good., I think I'll miss the wild..., Just let me out of the stupid Pokéball, Company might not be so bad, It's an opportunity to get stronger!, Running away ASAP, Costs and benefits remain to be seen.]"DYour new Trainer, Elliot, decides he wants you to get stronger."�He goes out and challenges the first Trainer he sees, and next thing you know you're facing off against a very strong-looking Greninja!";In fact, it seems to be around 20-30 levels above you!"$What will you do?\ch[62,-1, ...I'll do my best!, Can I just forfeit?, Quit. Bye., Level doesn't matter! Let's fight!!!, I must learn to overcome this difference, I choose to have faith in my Trainer, Ask how many Potions Elliot has..., Perhaps we're being switch-trained?, Elliot's an idiot.]"SUnfortunately, and perhaps predictably, your battle with Greninja goes poorly."RElliot thinks you need to fight some weaker Pokémon to get stronger instead.">The next thing you know, you're up against a baby Skitty."HIt seems to just be fresh out of the egg, let alone hardly a match."'Elliot commands you to go all-out.".What do you do?\ch[62,-1, KO it. Sucks to suck., I refuse to attack!, Attack but as gently as possible, KO it and suffer the guilt, Befriend the Skitty and play instead, Attack Elliot for being dumb, Teach the Skitty to play dead instead, Pretend to attack but miss on purpose, I will do as I am told.]"qElliot finally gets a sense of your power level, and begins to match you against more appropriate opponents."[In a heated battle with a Persian, you score a strong hit, nearly KOing your opponent."`But suddenly, Persian's Slash scores a critical hit, robbing you of an otherwise clean win!"aHow do you feel after the loss?\ch[62,-1, Mad at myself. I let it happen., Pissed at Persian, Indifferent. It happens., I'd feel sorry at first and then get over it, The next Persian I see will feel it., I'll just have to do better next time., Elliot should have accounted for that., I should've been ready for the crit., I feel like getting ice cream!]"YElliot just picked up a brand new TM he wants to teach you to help you get stronger!"It's the TM for Explosion."!How do you feel about that?\ch[62,-1, The Trainer knows best., You're kidding right?, Was this TM ethically reviewed?, Power attacks are nice but..., Clearly Elliot doesn't care, Elliot is denser than lead., I refuse to learn the move!!!, I'm hoping someone will save me..., BOOOOOOM!!!!!]",Elliot just caught a low-level Gothita!"EHe tries her out in a few battles, but she's not doing too well."FIn fact, she can hardly get in one or two hits before being KO'd."BAt a rare break, Gothita asks if she's doing something wrong."What do you tell Gothita?\ch[62,-1, She just needs to evolve, Elliot's just an idiot., She's perfect as is!, Use her emotions as strength, Maybe we can train together!, She needs to work harder, She needs to stop complaining, Everyone starts somewhere., Whatever happens happens.]"QAn Ace Trainer named Brian appears and challenges Elliot to a Double Battle!",It's Elliot's first one, and yours too."6He opens up by sending you out alongside Gothita!">You know Gothita won't survive more than a single attack."What do you do?\ch[62,-1, Put her on back and carry, Keep a positive attitude, Protect Gothita at my own risk!, Whatever I'm told to do., Just KO the enemy first-- duh., Whatever happens will be fine, Stop the fight, Analyze how best to use her, Where's that Explosion TM?]"LFortunately, Elliot realizes Gothita's in trouble and switches her out."FInstead he sends in his very first Pokémon: a high level Luxray!"#It's obvious it outpowers you."-How do you save face?\ch[62,-1, Accept failure with pride, Treat it as a test for myself, Just accept the easy win, Save face? This is Elliot's fault, Put the enemy into the dirt first, Consider it a sacrifice for Gothita, Just laugh it off!, Focus on strategy over power, It's a learning opportunity]"The battle rages on!"BYou and Luxray face off against Brian's Starmie and Skarmory!"yElliot notices they're both weak to Electric attacks, so he commands Luxray to hit them both at once with Discharge!"vLuxray glances at you, but charges up for the hit. Elliot hasn't even considered that you would be attacked also!"How do you feel?\ch[62,-1, Please think of me!!!, Do as you must., I'll get Luxray back later., I feel that my Trainer is dumb., I realize I don't matter., Bracing for impact!, I take the hit but Luxray owes me., Gettin' mad at Luxray and Elliot both, Running. I feel like running.]"IStarmie, Skarmory, and yourself all manage to survive the Discharge."KBoth of them attack Luxray, and now all four Pokémon are really weak!"�Elliot, thinking that Discharge worked well, commands you to use an attack that would hit everyone on the field, KOing Skarmory, Starmie, and Luxray all at once!"jWill you take the kills?\ch[62,-1, A win is a win., I will do it if I'm told to., I won't take my partner down!, I'll attack but I won't like it, Luxray will still have contributed to the win, I'll sincerely apologize to Luxray first, What happens to Luxray isn't my problem, Done deal. It's revenge for the Discharge., Can't we find an enemy-only move instead?]"RLuxray, Starmie, and Skarmory are all knocked out and Elliot wins the battle!"@But now Elliot is mad at you for hurting his prized Luxray!"9He's even talking about releasing you because of it!"9How do you react?\ch[62,-1, Isn't that unfair?!, If it's really what you want..., I'm so sorry! I'll try better!, You TOLD me to do it., Pissed. Go ahead and release me!, You'd be better off without me anyway., Perhaps parting is for the best., Just take Luxray to a Pokémon Center..., Sweet mercy-- let me OUT.]"COn that note, how do you feel about Elliot overall? \ch[62,-1, He has a lot to learn., He's not a bad person but..., He's too immature to function., Kill me now., Maybe I can help him be better!, Elliot is an idiot., I'd rather not be alone still., I hope he trips off the edge of a cliff., He's simply not worth the time.]"nElliot leaves you and Gothita out of your Pokéballs and runs away to take Luxray to the Pokémon Center."$He said he needs time to think."|After being mad at you, and disappointed in Gothita's poor performance, it seems like he might abandon the both of you."-As Elliot leaves, Gothita begins to cry."FWhat do you do?\ch[62,-1, I'm not getting involved here, Reassure her she didn't mess up, Offer to listen to her, Nothing-- it's not my problem, Let's run away with Gothita!, Offer Gothita some choice advice, Talk smack about Elliot to cheer her up!, Encourage her to have faith in herself, I'll cheer for her from a distance]"ZBefore Elliot comes back, you're found instead by Brian, the Ace Trainer from before!"4He recognizes you and takes you to find Elliot.";Elliot has calmed down, and begins talking with Brian."�After a little while, Brian says that he was very impressed with your performance in the battle and offers to trade his Starmie for you!":Elliot thinks it over, and after a while, he accepts!"THow do you feel about the trade?\ch[62,-1, Did I do something wrong?, Better Brian than Elliot., Good for me but bad for Starmie, Excited! But nervous..., Who will look out for Gothita?, New friends! But I hate saying goodbye, If he lost to Elliot is he even better?, Change means good things can happen!, Can't I just be released instead?]"yAfter a few days with Brian, you find that he is more stable and mature than Elliot, but has very different methods."sAll of his Pokémon go through rigorous daily routines of specific repetitions and technique-honing exercises."�For instance, Skarmory must practice its Brave Bird attack by landing the move on the same exact spot of a target 30 times in a row."Brian is very strict about this, what he calls EV Training, and you don't feel like you're making progress with your exercises."eHow do you feel about Brian's training?\ch[62,-1, Send me back to Elliot!, Repetitive. Annoying. Hate it., The work will be worth it in the long run, To do as told is my duty, I refuse to do any of it!, It was fun at first! Now I quit., There needs to be a better way than tedium., I've been waiting for this kind of structure!, I wonder if I deserve this?]"EAfter some time, Brian decides that he's going to take on a Gym."�He sends you out as the glass doors to the Gym's entrance slide open, and tells you that he'll be counting on you in particular for this battle."How do you feel?\ch[62,-1, I'll work hard for the win!, We can only do our best, This is too much pressure..., Happy to strut my stuff!, It's not ALL on me... right?, Let's consider strategies in advance, Show me the victims., This is gonna be fun., I'm eager to prove my usefulness.]"&One ferocious Gym Battle later..."bYou've just barely pulled through with a sliver of health and Brian's last Pokémon standing!"7Brian collapses to the ground in shock and relief."yHe's grateful that he won, but discouraged by the fact that it was so close, and there's still a whole league to go!"lHow would you respond?\ch[62,-1, What matters is you keep learning, The Training worked so far. Keep it up., We can redouble our efforts., I'm not gonna stop getting stronger!, I'm sorry I couldn't do more, I look forward to the next close match, I collapse with him! Tired! Nerves!, Wasn't that Gym Leader super cool?!, Quitting is stupid. Make plans; do better.]"?After everything, what do you miss most about being a human?\ch[62,-1, Making my own decisions, Being able to speak!, Calling the shots in battle, Being a Pokémon is more fun actually, I miss other people., I don't! No responsibilities is great!, Either way is fine with me, Doing whatever I feel like!, The internet.]"%Back to your human self at last!"qWhich of these traits best describes you?\ch[62,-1, Independent/Strong-willed/Confident, Reserved/Timid/High-strung, Self-assured/Independent/Rational, Light-hearted/Playful/Versatile, Energetic/Impulsive/Affectionate, Insecure/Devoted/Unique, Prideful/Tough/Solitary, Isolatory/Mysterious/Reclusive, Free-thinking/Spirited/Stubborn, Intelligent/Analytical/Creative, Optimistic/Inspiring/Kind-hearted, Intellectual/Curious/Withdrawn, Passionate/Ambitious/Quick-tempered, Wise/Confident/Imaginative, Peaceful/Caring/Compassionate, Mischievous/Misunderstood/Humorous, Understanding/Even-tempered/Subdued, Steadfast/Loyal/Tough]"Final question!"�Just for our records to improve this quiz, what is your favorite Type?\ch[62,-1, Normal, Fire, Water, Electric, Grass, Ice, Fighting, Poison, Ground, Flying, Psychic, Bug, Rock, Ghost, Dragon, Dark, Steel, Fairy]"...Whew!"3That took a while, but you made it to the end!"+Okay, let's tally up your results now!".". ."
. . ."And done!"You are a... \v[719] Type!"eYou can see what you scored for each Type on that computer there, or see what your result means."But there you go!"9You know, I happened to find this Gem the other day."3Since it matches you, you may as well take it."fYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "mononormal"."dYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monofire"."eYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monowater"."hYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monoelectric"."eYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monograss"."cYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monoice"."hYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monofighting"."fYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monopoison"."fYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monoground"."fYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monoflying"."gYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monopsychic"."cYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monobug"."dYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monorock"."eYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monoghost"."fYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monodragon"."dYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monodark"."eYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monosteel"."eYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monofairy".")It won't obligate you into anything."{It'll just make it so you'll probably find more Pokémon of that type in specific cases where you might otherwise not."Anyway, take care.";You can come by if you ever wanna take the quiz again.">Well, that's fine. It'll be here if you change your mind.":Or have the time to sit through like forty questions."!Geez, who writes this stuff?"You are a:\n \v[719] Type!"Normal: \v[701]"Fire: \v[702]"Water: \v[703]"Electric: \v[704]"Grass: \v[705]"Ice: \v[706]"Fighting: \v[707]"Poison: \v[708]"Ground: \v[709]"Flying: \v[710]"Psychic: \v[711]"Bug: \v[712]"Rock: \v[713]"Ghost: \v[714]"Dragon: \v[715]"Dark: \v[716]"Steel: \v[717]"Fairy: \v[718]"�Please select a Type.\ch[62,-1, Normal, Fire, Water, Electric, Grass, Ice, Fighting, Poison, Ground, Flying, Psychic, Bug, Rock, Ghost, Dragon, Dark, Steel, Fairy]"CNormal Types are usually light-hearted and easy- going people."@Like everyone else, they have their flaws and insecurities,"�But perhaps uniquely, they're able to accept themselves and others in spite of their flaws, and are experts at making the best of situations both good and bad."3Fire Types are all about passion and ambition."RThey're earnest and active. When they want something, they go for it all-out."bThere's no better go-getter, but Fire Types risk pushing themselves too hard and burning out."tThey're great at getting things done, but when it happens, it's sure to be on their schedule and no one else's."4Water Types are masters of going with the flow."�Balancing cool rationality with a deep understanding of their own and others' emotions, they're adept at understanding all sides of a conflict."�As extremely adaptable individuals, they can adjust to any sort of scenario-- even if it would be unhealthy-- and make it their own."$Electric Types light up a room!"\Energetic, forthright and cheerful, they bring an unrivaled spirit to any conversation."�Their impulsiveness can often lead to things getting out of hand, but their positive nature lends itself to smoothing over conflicts and making a lot of fun memories along the way."6Grass Types tend to put others before themselves."�They go out of their way to help and soothe others, and are great contributors to making the world a more positive, peaceful place."�Despite the fact that their habitual benevolence wins plenty of friends, they can also sometimes be insecure and prone to having doubts."^In reality though, Grass Types are often much more cherished than they will ever realize."?Ice Types are some of the most charming and unique people,"#But seldom do they realize it."qMany Ice Types hide behind a veil of aloofness, often hiding how much they truly worry or care about others."cTheir cool distance serves both to entice others, suggesting an air of mystery and refinement,"�But at the same time, in hiding how much they truly care, they risk pushing others away and missing out on welcome opportunities."0Fighting Types are models of determination."�Understanding that it is not the 100th strike that cracks the stone, but the 99 that came before it, no one is better able to set their mind to a task and stick to it."�Working with a tireless fervor that many others can only dream of, Fighting Types are sure to achieve whatever they pursue with enough time and patience."dPoison Types are prone to resigning themselves to circumstances they don't truly wish to be in."RThey value others above themselves, and may give up on themselves too easily."}In spite of these things, they often don't realize that they make for some of the best and closest friends that can be found."�Without ever realizing their own importance, they serve vital roles in the lives of those around them, all the while slowly building themselves up."-Ground Types are pragmatic and stubborn."|Unphased by traditional notions of what's "right" or "best", Ground Types view life and society from the outside looking in."�They prefer to remain with their ideals regardless of the consequences, which tends to work out well given how firmly rooted in results and effectiveness they often are."-Flying Types are free-spirited dreamers!"Always looking for bigger, better, more exciting things, they aren't necessarily bound to what they """should""" be doing."�Sometimes this gets them in trouble, but some might say Flying Types have an uncanny ability to just narrowly avoid whatever dire consequences would come of their mischief."bMoreover, they have a ton of fun doing whatever it is they do, and always get the last laugh."2Psychic Types are intelligent and analytical."=They value creativity, thoughtfulness and understanding."�They often see the pattern and reasons behind events and circumstances rather than the circumstances themselves, and thus thrive individually and socially."�While they can sometimes miss the forest for the trees and be extraordinarily unique in their own rites, they seem to seldom mind this.".Bug Types are intellectual and reclusive."iThey tend to be introverted, preferring books, games, or the internet to the company of real people."�The result is a surprisngly unique and refined perspective on many subjects, even if they are often unsure of how best to share it."�The best among Bug Types hollow out their own place in the world with like-minded individuals who share their passions and interests in the comforts of mutual respect and curiosity."0Rock Types are unshakably loyal companions."}Great at listening and following directions, those who earn the respect and service of a Rock Type are especially lucky."{Rock Types always stick up for their friends, faithfully serve their communities, and dutifully manage their families."�Despite this, they sometimes prefer to be left to their own devices, or might struggle to tear themselves away from negative people,"�But the burden of loyalty, while not an easy one to bear, is an invaluable and often overlooked cornerstone of society and our friendships."|While Ghost Types may appear intimidating or mean, at the end of the day, they're just practicing their sense of humor."bOften a darker humor, and sometimes at the expense of others, it is seldom truly ill-meaning."�Rather, cavalcades of jokes and pranks are both the sword and shield of a Ghost Type, serving to break the ice and earn favor with others, while also protecting their true, vulnerable selves from scrutiny."�Truly getting to know a Ghost Type beneath the surface can be a challenge in its own right, but should someone be let in, there's a bright and magnetic soul to be found."PDragon Types aren't weighed down by "common sense", rules, or expectations."xAs free-thinkers who read between the lines, they have a wealth of things to offer the world and those around them."|They can be intense and particular, but only because they quickly come to understand in wisdom what many others cannot."�Dragon Types often struggle to make close friends, but when they do attach to people, it is never lightly, always forming an unshakable bond sure to alter each of their lives forevermore."&Dark Types are the most reserved."}They tend to be in conflict with both others around them and themselves, and often prefer to keep their distance as a result."XNevertheless, Dark Types have many hidden strengths, varying from person to person."~Often able to do things others aren't, or with a perspective no one else would have, they can make for invaluable allies."MStill, it is rare that they ever let people too close to their hearts...",Steel Types don't let much get to them."zSteadfast, even-keel, and direct, they know what they want, how they want it, and one way or another, they'll get it."qWhile they can be prone to cynicism or nihilism, they often make reliable comrades and effective colleagues.".Fairy Types are optimistic and inspiring!"}They often strive to be a source of light and goodness in their communities, making for fast friends and strong leaders."~Their much-needed whimsy and creativity can often fill an emptiness where the dusts of routine and melancholy begin to settle."�But for all their goodness, Fairy Types expect the same respect from others as they offer, and if one fails to return it, the backlash can be severe..."Yes"No"All Scores"Result Analysis"Cancel[""PSYSTIGRI: Psy... ... ... ..."1Psystigri a l'air complétement traumatisé."CPsystigri renifle le PokéSnax! Psystigri reprend ses esprits!"-Voulez-vous prendre Psystigri avec vous?"*Il n'y a pas de place pour Psystigri."PSYSTIGRI: ..."ALe Pokémon semble être en état de choc et ne réagit pas."CHINCHIDOU: Chin..." Chinchidou a l'air apeuré."EChinchidou renifle le PokéSnax! Chinchidou reprend ses esprits!".Voulez-vous prendre Chinchidou avec vous?"+Il n'y a pas de place pour Chinchidou."CHINCHIDOU: ..."MARCACRIN: Mar..."0Marcacrin est recroquevillé sur lui même."<Marcacrin a senti le PokéSnack! Il semble intéressé."+Veux-tu prendre le Marcacrin avec toi?"*Il n'y a pas de place pour Marcacrin."MARCACRIN: ..."-On dirait qu'il ne veut pas répondre..."GALEKID: Gale...";Galekid regarde tristement et avec persistance le sol.":Galekid a senti le PokéSnax! Il semble tout excité!"+Voulez-vous prendre Galekid avec vous?")Il n'y a plus de place pour Galekid."GALEKID: ...":On dirait qu'il fixe le sol. Il ne vous remarque pas."(Hé, tu connais ces quizz en ligne?"bDu genre "De quelle couleur est ton aura?" ou "Quel Maître de la Ligue irait bien avec toi?""YJ'en ai trouvé un sur un vieux site qui s'appelle "De quel Type de Pokémon es-tu?""AApparemment, toutes les combinaisons de type sont possibles."rJe l'ai déjà essayé, mais je voudrais voir si on peut vraiment obtenir beaucoup de résultats différents.""J'suis Normal/Vol, si jamais."Tu veux essayer?"lJ'te préviens, il y a genre 36 questions. Apparemment, l'autrice ne sait pas faire des choses simples."!Tu veux essayer quand même?"!Tu veux réessayer le quizz?"?Tu veux essayer le quizz "De quel Type de Pokémon es-tu?""Cool! Ok, c'est parti."On commence en douceur."nQuelle est ta couleur préférée?\ch[62,-1, Rouge, Jaune, Vert, Bleu, Orange, Violet, Rose, Blanc, Noir]"Quelle est ta météo préférée? \ch[62,-1, Un beau ciel bleu!, Je trouve la pluie réconfortante., La tempête de sable ça déchire., La neige!, Un apaisant ciel gris., J'adore le vent., Des arc-en-ciels partout., Je n'ai pas de météo préférée., Je trouve la grêle cool!]"5Comment définirais-tu "la Réussite"?\ch[62,-1, Avoir plein d'amis géniaux!, Une carrière qui avance progressivement, Beaucoup d'argent, Trouver l'amour, C'est quand on arrête de la chercher., Être une star!, Le savoir et la sagesse, Avoir une réputation respectable, Peu importe tant qu'on est heureux]"�De quoi as-tu le plus peur?\ch[62,-1, J'ai peur de rien., Être rejeté., Les insectes!, Un truc très spécifique et très particulier..., Perdre mes proches., J'ai le syndrome FOMO., De ne jamais changer., Moi-même., Je ne dirai rien!]"cQu'est-ce qui te décrit le mieux?\ch[62,-1, J'ai des amis mais je me sens seul, J'essaie toujours de fuir., Les autres ne me comprennent jamais., Je fais fuir tout le monde., Je finis toujours par avoir des regrets., Je ne suis pas doué pour quoi que ce soit., La plupart des gens m'ignorent., Je suis un niveau au-dessus des autres., Rien n'a de sens.]"BQue penses-tu des relations amoureuses?\ch[62,-1, J'ai toujours besoin d'être en couple., Je m'en fous., Ça doit être agréable..., Elles ne sont qu'une distraction., Je suis mieux sans., Elles apportent beaucoup!, Merci de me le rappeler :c, S'accepter soi-même est plus important., J'aime prendre soin de quelqu'un.]"À quoi ressemble ton ou ta partenaire idéal?\ch[62,-1, Stable et équilibré, Les romantiques ont du charme, La romance est une invention capitaliste., J'aime bien les gens qui m'impressionnent!, Raisonnable et solidaire., Quelqu'un que je peux aider à trouver sa voie., Quelqu'un de franc et direct., Avec de l'ambition et de la détermination., Quelqu'un qui peut me supporter.]"oÀ quoi ressemblent tes amis idéaux?\ch[62,-1, Absolument inséparables., Là quand j'ai besoin d'eux., Parle-moi souvent mais t'attache pas., On peut juste glander de temps en temps., Le genre avec qui on fait des conneries!, Un ou deux qui savent tout., J'aime connaître plein de gens différents., J'ai pas besoin d'amis., Qui se soutiennent les uns les autres.]"~Et à quoi ressemblent tes vrais amis?\ch[62,- 1, Ils sont un peu trop désordonnés..., On ne se voit pas souvent en face à face., Je suis satisfait de mes vrais amis., Ils ignorent combien ils me manquent., Ils font comme si j'étais pas là., Mes "vrais amis" ne m'aiment pas., J'adore mes amis et je veux les adopter!, ... Quels vrais amis?, J'essaie de les garder ensemble...]"FOh non! La malédiction d'un Feunard t'a transformé en Pokémon!">Tu n'as plus de chez-toi et tu dois vivre dans la nature."jComment passes-tu le temps en tant que Pokémon?\ch[62,-1, Trouver un abri et à manger et vite, Je pars en exploration!, Et si je chercherai des amis?, Je dois tester mes talents au combat!, À dormir., À étudier les Pokémon depuis leur monde, Je vais retrouver ce Feunard..., Je finirais quand même devant un écran., Tellement de possibilités s'ouvrent!]"6Tu aperçois d'autres Pokémon dans les environs!"Comment réagis-tu?\ch[62,-1, Je les ignore., Je pars. Je ne prends pas le risque., Sauve qui peut!, J'observe de loin., J'espère secrètement qu'ils approchent..., Je m'avance pour voir., Je vais me présenter!, Des camarades pour jouer!, Cela dépend de ce qu'ils font.]">Soudain, un combat s'engage entre deux Pokémon sauvages!"QC'est la première fois que tu vois un combat du point de vue d'un Pokémon!"LQue fais-tu?\ch[62,-1, C'est parti! Baston!, Je reste à l'écart car ça me fait peur., Quid de l'éthique des combats Pokémon?, J'essaie de trouver une issue pacifique., J'observe et plains le perdant., Ça ne change pas grand-chose pour moi., Ça a l'air marrant! J'y vais!, J'attends une occasion., J'étudie leurs techniques.]"RAprès qu'un des Pokémon soit tombé K.O., un humain le trouve et l'emporte."_Quant au Pokémon vainqueur, un autre humain profite qu'il soit affaibli pour le capturer."�En tant que Pokémon, que penses-tu des Dresseurs? \ch[62,-1, Devoir leur obéir est effrayant., Leur compagnie a l'air agréable., La capture de Pokémon est immorale..., Il y a le bon et le mauvais Dresseur., Je vais les faire démissionner., Pas besoin d'un Dresseur pour être génial., La même chose que quand j'étais humain., Je regrette d'avoir capturé des Pokémon., Je rêve d'un compagnon de route!]"RTu rencontre un autre Pokémon de la même espèce, et il est plutôt mignon!"7Que fais-tu?\ch[62,-1, Je me présente poliment., Pas de présentations. On joue!, Je garde mes distances. Je suis humain..., On discute de la vie des Pokémon?, Je lui offre de la nourriture!, Je l'ignore..., Une petite blague et on attaque., 'Mignon' c'est très superficiel., Je ne voudrais pas déranger...]"KOh, oh! Un Démolosse sauvage apparaît et attaque le Pokémon mignon!"9Que faire?\ch[62,-1, Retraite stratégique!, Je me précipite à sa rescousse!, Attendre le bon moment..., Je fais diversion en le provoquant., Faire semblant de l'aider et frapper!, Le défier dans un combat à la loyale., Proposer d'aider le Pokémon., Ce ne sont pas mes affaires., Attendez! On peut discuter?]"=Ouf! Le Démolosse laisse l'autre Pokémon tranquille..."-...Mais maintenant, il s'attaque à toi!".Que fais-tu?!\ch[62,-1, Je le retiens pour que l'autre s'échappe!, Laisse-moi! Retourne vers l'autre!, Amène-toi., Je me sacrifie..., Il faut coopérer avec l'autre!, Je fais fuir le Démolosse en l'intimidant, Je résous calmement le conflit., Je cours pardi!, Je le piège grâce au savoir humain.]":D'une façon ou d'une autre, le Démolosse est parti."BMais juste après son attaque, un Dresseur sauvage apparaît!"5Il profite de ton état et te capture aussitôt!">Que penses-tu de ta captivité?\ch[62,-1, Féchié., Un nouvel ami!!!, J'espère qu'il est doué..., La vie sauvage va me manquer., Faites-moi sortir de cette Pokéball., De la compagnie. C'est pas si mal, C'est une chance de s'améliorer!, Je me tire dès que je peux., Le pour et le contre méritent d'être pesés.]";Ton nouveau Dresseur, Elliot, décide de t'entraîner."~Il défie le premier Dresseur qu'il rencontre, et ni une ni deux, tu te retrouves face à un Amphinobi qui a l'air très fort!"?Il doit être au moins 20 ou 30 niveaux au-dessus du tien!"?Comment réagis-tu?\ch[62,-1, ... Je ferai de mon mieux!, Je peux déclarer forfait?, Je démissionne. Ciao., On se fiche des niveaux! À l'attaque!!, Je cherche un moyen de réduire l'écart., Je choisis d'avoir foi en mon Dresseur, Elliott a combien de Potions?, Il va peut-être me remplacer?, Elliot est un abruti.]"BMalheureusement, mais sans surprise, ton combat se passe mal."KElliot se dit qu'il faut te faire affronter des Pokémon plus faibles."5Ton prochain match t'oppose à un bébé Skitty."DIl sort à peine de l'Œuf, et est complètement sans défense."(Elliot t'ordonne d'y aller à fond."aQu'est-ce que tu fais?\ch[62,-1, Je le mets KO. Pas de pitié., Je refuse d'attaquer!, J'attaque mais doucement., Je le mets KO et je me sens coupable., Je joue avec Skitty et on devient potes., J'attaque cet énorme crétin d'Elliot., J'apprends au Skitty à faire le mort., J'attaque et je fais exprès d'échouer., Je ferai ce qu'on me dit de faire.]"wElliot prend finalement conscience de ton niveau, et commence à te faire affronter des adversaires à ta hauteur."[Au cours d'un combat enflammé contre un Persian, tu es à deux doigts de la victoire."]Quand soudain, Persian lance Tranche, réussit un coup critique, et te vole la victoire!"�Comment te sens-tu après avoir perdu?\ch[62,-1, Énervé contre moi-même. C'est ma faute., Énervé contre Persian., Indifférent. Ça arrive., Je me sens mal au début puis je passe outre., Le prochain Persian que je vois va me le payer., J'aurai juste à faire mieux la prochaine fois., Elliot aurait dû le prévoir, J'aurai dû me préparer au coup critique., Je veux une glace!]"XElliot vient de se procurer une CT qu'il veut t'enseigner pour te rendre plus fort!"C'est la CT Explosion."_Qu'est-ce que tu en penses?\ch[62,-1, C'est lui le Dresseur. Il décide., Tu plaisantes n'est-ce pas?, Quid de l'éthique de cette CT?, La puissance c'est bien mais..., Elliot n'en a clairement rien à faire de moi., Elliot a le QI d'un seau d'eau vide., Je refuse d'apprendre cette CT!!!, J'espère que quelqu'un va venir me sauver..., BOUUUUUM!!!!!]"4Elliott vient de capturer une petite Scrutella!"NIl l'essaie dans quelques combats, mais elle ne s'en sort pas très bien."MEn fait, elle arrive à peine à lancer une attaque avant de tomber K.O."DLors d'un temps mort, Scrutella te demande ce qu'elle fait mal."iQu'est-ce que tu dis à Scrutella?\ch[62,-1, Elle doit juste évoluer., Elliot est juste un idiot., Elle est parfaite comme elle est., Qu'elle utilise ses émotions comme une force., On peut peut-être s'entrainer ensemble!, Elle doit travailler plus dur., Elle doit arrêter de se plaindre., Tout le monde commence quelque part., Ce qui doit arriver arrivera.]"MUn Topdresseur nommé Bryan apparaît et défie Elliot en Combat Double!"1C'est une première pour Elliot et pour toi."=Il décide de vous envoyer en premier, Scrutella et toi!"<Tu sais que Scrutella ne tiendra pas une seule attaque."HQue faire?\ch[62,-1, La mettre derrière et mener le combat., Garder une attitude positive., Protéger Scrutella à mes risques et périls., Ce qu'on m'aura dit de faire., Mettre K.O le Pokémon avant... évidemment., Peu importe., Arrêter le combat., Déterminer en quoi elle peut être utile, Où est la CT Explosion déjà?]"FHeureusement, Elliot réalise la situation et rappelle Scrutella."AÀ sa place, il envoie son tout premier Pokémon: un Luxray!"7Il est clair qu'il est beaucoup plus fort que toi."SComment éviter de faire pâle figure?\ch[62,-1, Garder la tête haute., En faire un test pour moi-même., Accepter la victoire facile., Pâle figure? C'est la décision d'Elliot., Mettre l'adversaire au tapis en premier., Ce sacrifice est pour Scrutella., En rire., La stratégie avant les muscles., C'est une bonne occasion d'apprendre.]"Le combat fait rage!"BLuxray et toi êtes face au Staross et à l'Airmure de Bryan!"zElliot remarque qu'ils sont tous les deux faibles aux attaques Électrik, et ordonne à Luxray d'utiliser Coup d'Jus!"{Luxray te jette un bref coup d'œil, puis charge son attaque. Elliot ne s'est pas rendu compte que tu serais touché aussi!"gComment est-ce que tu te sens?\ch[62,-1, Pense à mon XP!!!, Fais ce que tu as à faire., Je règlerai son compte à Luxray plus tard., Je pense que mon Dresseur est stupide., Je me rends compte que je ne compte pas., PRÊT POUR L'IMPACT!, J'encaisse mais Luxray m'en doit une., S'énerver contre Elliot et Luxray., Je cours je vole peu importe mais je fuis.]">Le Staross, l'Airmure et toi survivez tous au Coup d'Jus."VLes deux attaquent Luxray, et maintenant, tous les Pokémon sont très affaiblis!"�Elliot se dit que le Coup d'Jus a bien marché et t'ordonne d'utiliser une attaque qui touche tout le champ de bataille pour mettre K.O. Staross, Airmure et Luxray du même coup!"uVas-tu attaquer et les mettre K.O?\ch[62,-1, Une victoire est une victoire., Je ferai ce qu'on me dit de faire., Je ne mettrai pas mon partenaire K.O., J'attaque mais ça ne me plaît pas., Luxray aura contribué à la victoire., Je m'excuse envers Luxray d'abord., Luxray n'est pas mon problème., Sur le champ. J'ai pris le Coup d'Jus., Une attaque monocible peut-être?]"OLuxray, Staross et Airmure tombent tous K.O. et Elliot remporte le combat!"KMais maintenant Elliot t'en veut d'avoir blessé son précieux Luxray!"$Il parle même de te relâcher!"iComment réagis-tu?\ch[62,-1, N'est-ce pas injuste?!, Si c'est vraiment ce que tu veux..., Je suis tellement désolé! Je m'améliorerai!, C'est TOI qui m'as dit de le faire., Vas-y! Relâche moi!, Tu seras mieux sans moi dans tous les cas., Se séparer est peut-être la solution., Amène-le juste dans un Centre Pokémon..., Par Arceus... LAISSEZ-MOI PARTIR.]"PAprès ça, que pensez-vous d'Elliot en général? \ch[62,-1, Il a beaucoup à apprendre., Ce n'est pas quelqu'un de mauvais mais..., Il est trop immature., Tuez moi. Maintenant., Peut-être que je peux l'aider!, Elliot est un idiot., Je déteste la solitude., J'espère qu'il va tomber d'une falaise., Il n'en vaut juste pas la peine.]"mElliot vous laisse, Scrutella et toi, hors de vos Pokéballs et court emmener Luxray au Centre Pokémon."0Il a dit qu'il avait besoin de réfléchir."pAprès avoir été déçu de la performance de Scrutella, on dirait qu'il va vous abandonner tous les deux."1Elliot part, et Scrutella se met à pleurer."FQue faire?\ch[62,-1, Je ne m'implique pas dans cette histoire., La rassurer. Elle n'a rien fait de mal., L'écouter., Rien. Ce n'est pas mon problème., S'enfuir avec Scrutella!, Donner des conseils à Scrutella., Descendre Elliot pour lui remonter le moral., Lui redonnner confiance en elle., Je l'encourage mais en silence.]"OAvant qu'Elliot ne revienne, c'est Bryan, le Topdresseur, qui vous trouve!"4Il te reconnaît et t'emmène retrouver Elliot."KCe dernier s'est calmé, et les deux Dresseurs commencent à discuter."zAu bout d'un moment, Bryan déclare que tu l'as beaucoup impressionné, et propose de t'échanger contre son Staross!"0Elliot réfléchit, et finalement, accepte!"�Comment te sens-tu à propos de l'échange?\ch[62,-1, J'ai fait quelque chose de mal?, Mieux vaut Bryan qu'Elliot., C'est bien pour moi mais triste pour Staross., Sous pression mais hâte d'en découdre!, Qui prendra soin de Scrutella?, Chouette! Mais je déteste dire au revoir., Mais il a pas perdu contre Elliot?, Le changement apporte de bonnes choses!, On ne peut pas me relâcher plutôt?]"�Après quelques jours avec Bryan, tu t'aperçois qu'il est plus stable et mature qu'Elliot, mais a des méthodes très différentes."Tous ses Pokémon doivent s'entraîner tous les jours et suivre des programmes rigoureux pour améliorer leurs techniques."vPar exemple, Airmure doit exercer son Rapace en frappant le même emplacement sur une cible trente fois de suite."�Bryan est très strict à ce sujet. Il appelle cela l'entraînement aux EVs. Et tu n'as pas l'impression de progresser avec ces exercices."�Comment te sens-tu après l'entraînement de Bryan?\ch[62,-1, Rendez-moi Elliot!, Répétitif. Ennuyeux. Je hais ça., Le travail paiera plus tard., Mon rôle est de faire ce qu'on me dit., Je refuse de participer à l'entraînement!, C'était marrant... au début., Il faut un autre moyen moins ennuyeux., J'ai toujours voulu cet entraînement!, Est-ce que je mérite vraiment tout ça?]"NQuelques temps plus tard, Bryan décide de relever le défi d'une Arène."uSur le seuil de la porte d'entrée de l'Arène, il te confie qu'il compte sur toi en particulier pour ce combat."RComment tu te sens?\ch[62,-1, Je travaillerai dur pour la victoire!, On fera de notre mieux., C'est trop de pression!, Je vais enfin montrer ma vraie valeur!, Il y a AUSSI les autres... N'est-ce pas??, Prévoyons notre stratégie à l'avance., Montrez-moi mes futures victimes., Ça va être marrant., J'ai hâte de prouver mon utilité.]",Un combat d'Arène féroce plus tard..."WTu t'en es sorti de justesse, et tu es le dernier Pokémon de Bryan encore debout!"9Bryan, exténué et soulagé, s'effondre sur le sol."�Il est content d'avoir gagné, mais découragé d'à quel point c'était serré, et du fait qu'il y a encore toute une Ligue qui l'attend!"iComment est-ce que tu réponds?\ch[62,-1, N'arrête jamais d'apprendre., L'entraînement a fonctionné jusqu'ici., Redoublons d'efforts!, Je ne vais pas m'arrêter de progresser!, Pardon mais je ne peux pas faire plus., J'ai hâte du prochain match épique., Je m'effondre avec lui., Ce Champion était vraiment cool!, Abandonner c'est dommage après tout ça.]"SAprès toute cette aventure, qu'est-ce qui te manque le plus de ta vie d'être humain?\ch[62,-1, Faire mes propres choix., Pouvoir parler., Faire les choix pendant les combats., C'est plus marrant d'être un Pokémon., Les autres gens me manquent., Adieu les responsabilités!, Les deux me conviennent., Faire ce qui me plaît., Internet.]"%Te voilà enfin redevenu humain!"8Quel portrait te décrit le mieux?\ch[62,-1, Assuré/Confiant/Indépendant, Timide/Réservé/Anxieux, Affirmé/Autonome/Raisonnable, Enjoué/Versatile/Frivole, Impulsif/Énergique/Passionnel, Angoissé/Devoué/Unique, Fier/Rude/Solitaire, Mystérieux/Difficile/Exclusif, Rebelle/Libre-penseur/Entêté, Intelligent/Réfléchi/Créatif, Optimiste/Inspirant/Bienveillant, Cérébral/Curieux/Introverti, Passionné/Ambitieux/Emporté, Sage/Sûr/Imaginatif, Paisible/Altruiste/Empathique, Malicieux/Incompris/Drôle, Compréhensif/Constant/Pondéré, Impassible/Loyal/Dur]"Dernière question!"�Pour améliorer ce quizz, peux-tu nous donner ton Type préféré?\ch[62,-1, Normal, Feu, Eau, Électrik, Plante, Glace, Combat, Poison, Sol, Vol, Psy, Insecte, Roche, Spectre, Dragon, Ténèbres, Acier, Fée]"...Pfiou!"2C'était long, mais tu as tenu jusqu'au bout!"&Ok, c'est l'heure des résultats!".". ."
. . ."Et voilà!"Tu es de Type... \v[719]!"oTu peux consulter sur cet écran ton score pour chaque Type, et regarder à quoi correspond ton résultat."Mais voilà!"4D'ailleurs, j'ai trouvé ce Joyau l'autre jour.".Comme il est de ton Type, je te le donne."cTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "mononormal"."aTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monofire"."bTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monowater"."eTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monoelectric"."bTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monograss"."`Tu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monoice"."eTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monofighting"."cTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monopoison"."cTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monoground"."cTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monoflying"."dTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monopsychic"."`Tu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monobug"."aTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monorock"."bTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monoghost"."cTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monodragon"."aTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monodark"."bTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monosteel"."bTu sais, la prochaine fois qu'on te demande un mot de passe, essaie de répondre "monofairy"."/Ça ne t'obligera pas à quoi que ce soit."iÇa augmentera juste tes chances de trouver un Pokémon de ce type dans des situations spécifiques."!Enfin bref, à la prochaine."1Tu peux revenir faire le quiz quand tu veux.":Ok, comme tu veux. Je serai là si tu changes d'avis."EEt si tu as le temps de répondre à presque quarante questions."$Qui écrit ces trucs, sérieux?"#Vous êtes de Type:\n \v[719]!"Normal: \v[701]"Feu: \v[702]"Eau: \v[703]"Électrik: \v[704]"Plante: \v[705]"Glace: \v[706]"Combat: \v[707]"Poison: \v[708]"Sol: \v[709]"Vol: \v[710]"Psy: \v[711]"Insecte: \v[712]"Roche: \v[713]"Spectre: \v[714]"Dragon: \v[715]"Ténèbres: \v[716]"Acier: \v[717]"Fée: \v[718]"�Sélectionnez un Type.\ch[62,-1, Normal, Feu, Eau, Électrik, Plante, Glace, Combat, Poison, Sol, Vol, Psy, Insecte, Roche, Spectre, Dragon, Ténèbres, Acier, Fée]"SLes personnes de Type Normal sont généralement aimables et faciles à vivre."EComme tout un chacun, ils ont leurs défauts et leurs angoisses,"�Mais ce qui fait peut-être leur particularité, c'est leur capacité à les accepter, chez eux et chez les autres, et à tirer le meilleur parti de chaque situation."2Les Type Feu ne sont que passion et ambition."dIls sont motivés et appliqués. Lorsqu'ils veulent quelque chose, ils s'en donnent les moyens."_Ce sont des fonceurs, qui risquent à tout moment le Burn Out, ou de se brûler les ailes."MLes Type Feu obtiennent des résultats, mais pour eux-mêmes avant tout."LLes Type Eau sont passés maîtres dans l'art de nager avec le courant."�Grâce à un subtil équilibre entre une rationnalité froide et une compréhension profonde des émotions de chacun, ils sont aptes à saisir tous les points de vue dans un conflit."�Ondoyants à l'extrême, ils peuvent s'adapter à n'importe quel scénario, fut-il contraire à leur intérêt, et se l'approprier."+Les Type Électrik mettent l'ambiance!"eÉnergiques, francs et guillerets, ils apportent à une conversation une fraîcheur sans pareil."�Leur impulsivité finit parfois par faire dégénérer les choses, mais leur nature optimiste a tendance à délester les conflits pour s'en amuser, et à en faire des mésaventures qu'ils relatent par la suite avec légèreté."ALes Type Plante ont tendance à placer les autres avant eux."�Ils n'hésitent pas à apporter leur aide ou leur soutien, et contribuent de ce fait à rendre le monde plus serein et accueillant."}Malgré leur avenance naturelle qui leur vaut d'avoir beaucoup d'amis, ils peuvent être sujets aux doutes et au stress."fMais en réalité, les Type Plante sont souvent bien plus appréciés qu'ils n'en ont conscience."SLes Type Glace font partie des personnes les plus atypiques et charismatiques,".Bien qu'ils en aient rarement conscience."�Les Type Glace se cachent derrière un voile d'indifférence, dissimulant souvent à quel point ils s'inquiètent ou se soucient vraiment des autres."vLeur distance froide sert à la fois à séduire les autres et à suggérer un air de mystère et de raffinement,"�Mais en même temps, en cachant à quel point ils se sentent concernés, ils risquent de repousser les autres et de passer à côté d'opportunités bienvenues."9Les Type Combat sont des modèles de détermination."�Ils comprennent mieux que personne que ce n'est pas le centième coup qui brise la pierre, mais les quatre-vingt-dix-neuf coups successifs qui l'ont précédé."�Travaillant sans relâche avec une ardeur que les autres leur envient, les Type Combat atteignent leur but à force de temps et de patience."jLes Type Poison ont une fâcheuse tendance à accepter des circonstances qui ne leur conviennent pas."YEn accordant plus de valeur à autrui qu'à eux-mêmes, ils s'oublient trop souvent."�En dépit de cela, ils ne réalisent que rarement qu'ils sont les amis les plus précieux qui soient pour ceux qui ont la chance de les avoir."�En négligeant leur propre importance, ils jouent un rôle vital dans la vie de leur entourage, ce qui contribue lentement à leur épanouissement personnel."0Les Type Sol sont pragmatiques et résolus."xIndifférents aux notions de "bien" ou de "juste", les Type Sol observent le monde et la société de l'extérieur."�Ils restent fidèles à leurs valeurs quelles qu'en soient les conséquences, ce qui, comme elles visent avant tout l'efficacité, a tendance à bien fonctionner pour eux."*Les Type Vol sont des esprits libres!"}Toujours à la recherche de plus grand, plus beau, plus distrayant, ils ne se sentent pas contraints par la notion de devoir."�Ce qui leur vaut parfois des ennuis, mais les Type Vol ont un talent peu commun pour s'extraire de n'importe quel imbroglio et esquiver comme des acrobates les conséquences de leurs forfaits."hQui plus est, ces mésaventures les divertissent grandement, et ils en tirent une joie victorieuse."2Les Type Psy sont intelligents et rationnels."KIls privilégient la réflexion, la compréhension et la créativité."�Ils distinguent les causes et les structures des événements et de leurs circonstances, ce qui leur permet de s'épanouir socialement et individuellement."~Parfois, les arbres leur cachent la forêt, et leurs habitudes les rendent extraordinairement uniques, mais ils n'en ont cure."7Les Type Insecte sont des cérébraux introvertis."iIls ont tendance à préférer la compagnie des livres, des jeux ou d'internet à celle des humains."�Cela se traduit chez eux par un point de vue unique et souvent très documenté sur de nombreux sujets, bien qu'ils ne sachent pas comment le partager."�En s'entourant de pairs qui partagent leurs passions et en se fondant sur le respect mutuel et la curiosité, les Type Insecte se creusent leur nid au sein du monde."6Les Type Roche sont d'une loyauté inébranlable."zGagner le respect et le dévouement d'un Type Roche est une chance, car ils savent écouter et suivre des directives."�Les Type Roche défendent leurs amis, servent leurs communautés, et s'occupent de leurs familles avec application et assiduité."~Néanmoins, il leur arrive de suivre leurs propres ordres, et ont parfois de la peine à se séparer des personnes négatives."�Mais le fardeau de la loyauté, bien qu'il puisse être difficile à porter, est une pierre angulaire de la société dont on sous-estime l'importance."{Les Type Spectre peuvent sembler méchants, ou intimidants, mais ce n'est au bout du compte que leur sens de l'humour."fUn humour souvent sombre, parfois aux dépends d'autrui, mais qui n'a jamais pour but de blesser."�Les vannes et les farces servent aux Type Spectre d'une part à briser la glace pour s'attirer les faveurs des autres, et d'autre part à dissimuler ce qu'ils sont vraiment aux yeux et au jugement de la société."�De fait, pénétrer ce voile opaque et apprendre à connaître un Type Spectre est une épreuve en soi, mais la lumineuse âme qui se trouve à l'intérieur en vaut la chandelle."cLes Types Dragon ne sont pas plombés par le bon sens, les règles ou les attentes des autres."�Leur liberté de penser leur permet de lire entre les lignes. Ils ont tellement à offrir au monde et à ceux qui les entourent."�Leur manière d'agir est intense et particulière grâce à leur sagesse et leur faculté à comprendre ce que les autres ne peuvent pas."�Les Types Dragon ont souvent du mal à se faire des amis proches mais quand ils s'attachent à quelqu'un, ce n'est jamais à moitié et forment un lien indestructible avec la personne."3Les Types Ténèbres sont les plus réservés."tIls ont tendance à être en conflit avec les autres et eux-mêmes, et préfèrent donc garder leurs distances."eNéanmoins, les Types Ténèbres ont plein d'atouts cachés, changeant d'une personne à l'autre"�Souvent capables de faire ce que d'autres ne peuvent pas, ou avec une perspective différente, ils peuvent faire des alliés inestimables."RMais, ça reste très rare qu'ils laissent des gens entrer dans leur cœur..."<Les Types Acier ne laissent presque rien les atteindre."�Fermes, intangibles et francs, ils savent ce qu'ils veulent, comment ils le veulent et d'une façon ou d'une autre ils l'auront."�Bien qu'ils puissent être cyniques et nihilistes, ils sont souvent les camarades sur qui on peut compter et des collègues efficaces."2Les Types Fée sont optimistes et inspirants!"�Ils font généralement tout leur possible pour être une source de bonheur et de bien-être pour les gens autour d'eux, faisant d'eux de personnes sociables et populaires."�Leur fantaisie et leur créativité peut souvent combler les vides et routines de la vie qui se mettent petit à petit en place."�Mais malgré toute leur bonté, ils attendent souvent la même chose des autres et le retour de bâton leur fait très mal lors de grosses déceptions."Oui"Non"Tous les scores"Analyse des résultats"Annuler;["ESPURR: Esp... ... ... ...")Espurr looks completely traumatized."AEspurr smells the PokéSnax! Espurr snapped back to reality!")Do you want to take Espurr with you?""There was no room for Espurr."ESPURR: ..."8It seems to have gone into shock and won't respond."MINCCINO: Min..."Minccino looks scared."EMinccino smells the PokéSnax! Minccino snapped back to reality!"+Do you want to take Minccino with you?"$There was no room for Minccino."MINCCINO: ..."SWINUB: Swin..."%Swinub is curled up into a ball."-Swinub smells the PokéSnax! It came to!")Do you want to take Swinub with you?""There was no room for Swinub."SWINUB: ..."*It doesn't seem to want to respond..."ARON: Ronron...")Aron is meekly looking at the floor."6Aron smells the PokéSnax! It looks up excitedly!"'Do you want to take Aron with you?" There was no room for Aron."ARON: ..."AIt seems to be looking back at the ground and won't respond."1Hey stranger, you know those online quizzes?"WLike "What's your true soul color?" or "Which Go-Rock Quad member would date you?""RSo I found one of those on this old website for "What Pokémon Type are you?"">Apparently every single type and combination is possible."jI already took it for myself, but I wanna see if other people really get that many different answers."%I'm Normal/Flying, bee-tee-dubs."Do you wanna try it?"gFair warning, it's like 36 questions long because apparently the writer doesn't know when to quit."$But wanna take the quiz anyway?" Wanna take that quiz again?"8Wanna take that "What Pokémon Type are you?" quiz?"Sweet! Okay, let's go."Let's start simple."iWhat's your favorite color?\ch[62,-1, Red, Yellow!, Green, Blue, Orange, Purple, Pink, White, Black]"What kind of weather do you find most appealing? \ch[62,-1, Clear and sunny!, Rain is comforting, A sandstorm would be awesome, Snow is pretty!, A relaxing overcast, I love when it's windy, Rainbows. Rainbows everywhere., I don't have a favorite weather., Hail is super cool!]"3What is your idea of "Success"?\ch[62,-1, Having lots of great friends!, A stable and progressive career, Lots of money, Finding true love, Success is when you stop chasing it, Being famous!, Enlightenment and acquisition of knowledge, Prestige; Reputation; Respectability, Anything as long as you're happy]"�What are you most afraid of?\ch[62,-1, I'm not afraid of anything, Rejection, Bugs are gross!, One specific very uncommon thing..., Losing those close to me, Missing out, Of staying the same forever, Myself, Like I'd tell you!]":Which best describes you?\ch[62,-1, I have friends but I'm still lonely, I'm always trying to run away, Others always misunderstand me, I drive everyone away, I end up regretting a lot of things, I'm not good enough at anything, Most people just ignore me, Others need to get on my level, Everything is pointless.]";How do you feel about relationships?\ch[62,-1, Like I always need to be in one, Who cares?, It would be nice to be cared for..., They're too often just a distraction, I do better alone., They can add a lot to life!, Thanks for reminding me :c, Self-acceptance is more important, I like having someone to look after]"4What's your ideal partner like?\ch[62,-1, Stable and level-headed, Hopeless romantics are cute, Romance is a capitalistic fabrication, I like the bad-ass types!, Rational and supportive, Someone who I can help find their voice, Honest and direct, Dreams big and chases hard, Someone who can keep up with me.]"RWhat are your ideal friends like?\ch[62,-1, Absolutely inseparable, Just around when I need them, Talk to me often but don't cling, We can just hang whenever, Loud and fun; likely to get into trouble!, Just one or two who know everything, I like knowing lots of different people, Ideally? I don't need friends, Always mutually supportive]"\How do those compare to your real friends?\ch[62,- 1, They usually are too chaotic..., We don't see eye-to-eye often, I'm content with my real friends, They don't know how much I miss them, They usually ignore me., My "real friends" dislike me, I love my friends and want to adopt them!, ...What real friends?, I'm usually keeping them together...]">Oh no! A Ninetales' curse has turned you into a Pokémon!"FYou've been cast out of your home and forced to live in the wild."WHow do you pass the time as a Pokémon?\ch[62,-1, Find food and shelter ASAP, I wanna explore!, I'd go look for some friends?, Time to try out my battling skills..., Just sleep I guess, Time to study Pokémon from their world!, Gonna go hunt that Ninetales..., I'll still find a way to be on the computer., There are so many ways to play now!]"2You just saw some other Pokémon in the area!"3How do you react to them?\ch[62,-1, Ignore them., Leave. It's not worth the trouble., Run away!, Just watch from afar, I'd watch but secretly hope they approach..., I'd go and see what's up, I'd introduce myself right away!, Skip the introductions-- let's play!, That depends on exactly what they're doing.]"ASuddenly the wild Pokémon get into a fight with each other!"JIt's your first time seeing a battle from a Pokémon's point of view!"YWhat do you do?\ch[62,-1, Get excited! Let's brawl!, Stay away; it's kind of scary, Consider the ethics of Pokémon battles..., Try to resolve the situation peacefully, Observe and pity the loser, It makes no difference to me anyway, It seems fun! Join in right away!, Wait for a chance to test your own skills, Study their technique to improve]"RAfter one of the Pokémon is knocked out, a human finds it and takes it away."kAfter the harsh battle, another human shows up and immediately captures the Pokémon that defeated it."�As a Pokémon, how do you feel about Trainers? \ch[62,-1, Having to do anything they say is scary, Having the company seems nice!, Pokémon capture must be unethical..., You just have to find the right Trainer., brb gonna go get a trainer rq, I don't need a Trainer to be awesome, The same as I did as a human, Regretting ever having captured Pokémon, I'd love to meet a lifelong companion!]"MYou meet some Pokémon of your same species, and tbh they're kinda cute!"DWhat do you do?\ch[62,-1, I'd introduce myself properly, No introductions; only play!, Keep my distance since I was human..., Maybe we can discuss Pokémon life?, I'd bring them food as a gift!, Just ignore them..., Play a prank as an excuse to talk~, 'Cute' is a shallow judgment. Irrelevant., I don't want to bother them.]"SUh oh! Suddenly a wild Houndoom appears and starts bullying the cute Pokémon!"4What will you do?\ch[62,-1, Tactical retreat!, Jump in and defend them!, Wait patiently for the right moment..., Taunt it away from the other one!, Pretend to be on its side; then strike!, I challenge it to an honest fight, Offer to help the Pokémon first, Not my problem., Hold on! Can't we talk this out?]"=Good news! The Houndoom left the other Pokémon alone..."&...But now it's onto you instead!".What's the plan?!\ch[62,-1, Keep it busy so the other can escape!, Forget it! Go back to the other Pokémon!, Bring it on., I will be the sacrifice..., Work together with the other one!, Intimidate Houndoom into quitting, Calm it down and solve the conflict, Duh-- Run!, Trick it with human knowledge!]"*One way or another, Houndoom is gone."ABut just after you've been attacked, a wild Trainer appears!"7He sees you're weak, and captures you immediately!"How do you feel about captivity?\ch[62,-1, FML., New friend!!!, I just hope he's good., I think I'll miss the wild..., Just let me out of the stupid Pokéball, Company might not be so bad, It's an opportunity to get stronger!, Running away ASAP, Costs and benefits remain to be seen.]"DYour new Trainer, Elliot, decides he wants you to get stronger."�He goes out and challenges the first Trainer he sees, and next thing you know you're facing off against a very strong-looking Greninja!";In fact, it seems to be around 20-30 levels above you!"$What will you do?\ch[62,-1, ...I'll do my best!, Can I just forfeit?, Quit. Bye., Level doesn't matter! Let's fight!!!, I must learn to overcome this difference, I choose to have faith in my Trainer, Ask how many Potions Elliot has..., Perhaps we're being switch-trained?, Elliot's an idiot.]"SUnfortunately, and perhaps predictably, your battle with Greninja goes poorly."RElliot thinks you need to fight some weaker Pokémon to get stronger instead.">The next thing you know, you're up against a baby Skitty."HIt seems to just be fresh out of the egg, let alone hardly a match."'Elliot commands you to go all-out.".What do you do?\ch[62,-1, KO it. Sucks to suck., I refuse to attack!, Attack but as gently as possible, KO it and suffer the guilt, Befriend the Skitty and play instead, Attack Elliot for being dumb, Teach the Skitty to play dead instead, Pretend to attack but miss on purpose, I will do as I am told.]"qElliot finally gets a sense of your power level, and begins to match you against more appropriate opponents."[In a heated battle with a Persian, you score a strong hit, nearly KOing your opponent."`But suddenly, Persian's Slash scores a critical hit, robbing you of an otherwise clean win!"aHow do you feel after the loss?\ch[62,-1, Mad at myself. I let it happen., Pissed at Persian, Indifferent. It happens., I'd feel sorry at first and then get over it, The next Persian I see will feel it., I'll just have to do better next time., Elliot should have accounted for that., I should've been ready for the crit., I feel like getting ice cream!]"YElliot just picked up a brand new TM he wants to teach you to help you get stronger!"It's the TM for Explosion."!How do you feel about that?\ch[62,-1, The Trainer knows best., You're kidding right?, Was this TM ethically reviewed?, Power attacks are nice but..., Clearly Elliot doesn't care, Elliot is denser than lead., I refuse to learn the move!!!, I'm hoping someone will save me..., BOOOOOOM!!!!!]",Elliot just caught a low-level Gothita!"EHe tries her out in a few battles, but she's not doing too well."FIn fact, she can hardly get in one or two hits before being KO'd."BAt a rare break, Gothita asks if she's doing something wrong."What do you tell Gothita?\ch[62,-1, She just needs to evolve, Elliot's just an idiot., She's perfect as is!, Use her emotions as strength, Maybe we can train together!, She needs to work harder, She needs to stop complaining, Everyone starts somewhere., Whatever happens happens.]"QAn Ace Trainer named Brian appears and challenges Elliot to a Double Battle!",It's Elliot's first one, and yours too."6He opens up by sending you out alongside Gothita!">You know Gothita won't survive more than a single attack."What do you do?\ch[62,-1, Put her on back and carry, Keep a positive attitude, Protect Gothita at my own risk!, Whatever I'm told to do., Just KO the enemy first-- duh., Whatever happens will be fine, Stop the fight, Analyze how best to use her, Where's that Explosion TM?]"LFortunately, Elliot realizes Gothita's in trouble and switches her out."FInstead he sends in his very first Pokémon: a high level Luxray!"#It's obvious it outpowers you."-How do you save face?\ch[62,-1, Accept failure with pride, Treat it as a test for myself, Just accept the easy win, Save face? This is Elliot's fault, Put the enemy into the dirt first, Consider it a sacrifice for Gothita, Just laugh it off!, Focus on strategy over power, It's a learning opportunity]"The battle rages on!"BYou and Luxray face off against Brian's Starmie and Skarmory!"yElliot notices they're both weak to Electric attacks, so he commands Luxray to hit them both at once with Discharge!"vLuxray glances at you, but charges up for the hit. Elliot hasn't even considered that you would be attacked also!"How do you feel?\ch[62,-1, Please think of me!!!, Do as you must., I'll get Luxray back later., I feel that my Trainer is dumb., I realize I don't matter., Bracing for impact!, I take the hit but Luxray owes me., Gettin' mad at Luxray and Elliot both, Running. I feel like running.]"IStarmie, Skarmory, and yourself all manage to survive the Discharge."KBoth of them attack Luxray, and now all four Pokémon are really weak!"�Elliot, thinking that Discharge worked well, commands you to use an attack that would hit everyone on the field, KOing Skarmory, Starmie, and Luxray all at once!"jWill you take the kills?\ch[62,-1, A win is a win., I will do it if I'm told to., I won't take my partner down!, I'll attack but I won't like it, Luxray will still have contributed to the win, I'll sincerely apologize to Luxray first, What happens to Luxray isn't my problem, Done deal. It's revenge for the Discharge., Can't we find an enemy-only move instead?]"RLuxray, Starmie, and Skarmory are all knocked out and Elliot wins the battle!"@But now Elliot is mad at you for hurting his prized Luxray!"9He's even talking about releasing you because of it!"9How do you react?\ch[62,-1, Isn't that unfair?!, If it's really what you want..., I'm so sorry! I'll try better!, You TOLD me to do it., Pissed. Go ahead and release me!, You'd be better off without me anyway., Perhaps parting is for the best., Just take Luxray to a Pokémon Center..., Sweet mercy-- let me OUT.]"COn that note, how do you feel about Elliot overall? \ch[62,-1, He has a lot to learn., He's not a bad person but..., He's too immature to function., Kill me now., Maybe I can help him be better!, Elliot is an idiot., I'd rather not be alone still., I hope he trips off the edge of a cliff., He's simply not worth the time.]"nElliot leaves you and Gothita out of your Pokéballs and runs away to take Luxray to the Pokémon Center."$He said he needs time to think."|After being mad at you, and disappointed in Gothita's poor performance, it seems like he might abandon the both of you."-As Elliot leaves, Gothita begins to cry."FWhat do you do?\ch[62,-1, I'm not getting involved here, Reassure her she didn't mess up, Offer to listen to her, Nothing-- it's not my problem, Let's run away with Gothita!, Offer Gothita some choice advice, Talk smack about Elliot to cheer her up!, Encourage her to have faith in herself, I'll cheer for her from a distance]"ZBefore Elliot comes back, you're found instead by Brian, the Ace Trainer from before!"4He recognizes you and takes you to find Elliot.";Elliot has calmed down, and begins talking with Brian."�After a little while, Brian says that he was very impressed with your performance in the battle and offers to trade his Starmie for you!":Elliot thinks it over, and after a while, he accepts!"THow do you feel about the trade?\ch[62,-1, Did I do something wrong?, Better Brian than Elliot., Good for me but bad for Starmie, Excited! But nervous..., Who will look out for Gothita?, New friends! But I hate saying goodbye, If he lost to Elliot is he even better?, Change means good things can happen!, Can't I just be released instead?]"yAfter a few days with Brian, you find that he is more stable and mature than Elliot, but has very different methods."sAll of his Pokémon go through rigorous daily routines of specific repetitions and technique-honing exercises."�For instance, Skarmory must practice its Brave Bird attack by landing the move on the same exact spot of a target 30 times in a row."Brian is very strict about this, what he calls EV Training, and you don't feel like you're making progress with your exercises."eHow do you feel about Brian's training?\ch[62,-1, Send me back to Elliot!, Repetitive. Annoying. Hate it., The work will be worth it in the long run, To do as told is my duty, I refuse to do any of it!, It was fun at first! Now I quit., There needs to be a better way than tedium., I've been waiting for this kind of structure!, I wonder if I deserve this?]"EAfter some time, Brian decides that he's going to take on a Gym."�He sends you out as the glass doors to the Gym's entrance slide open, and tells you that he'll be counting on you in particular for this battle."How do you feel?\ch[62,-1, I'll work hard for the win!, We can only do our best, This is too much pressure..., Happy to strut my stuff!, It's not ALL on me... right?, Let's consider strategies in advance, Show me the victims., This is gonna be fun., I'm eager to prove my usefulness.]"&One ferocious Gym Battle later..."bYou've just barely pulled through with a sliver of health and Brian's last Pokémon standing!"7Brian collapses to the ground in shock and relief."yHe's grateful that he won, but discouraged by the fact that it was so close, and there's still a whole league to go!"lHow would you respond?\ch[62,-1, What matters is you keep learning, The Training worked so far. Keep it up., We can redouble our efforts., I'm not gonna stop getting stronger!, I'm sorry I couldn't do more, I look forward to the next close match, I collapse with him! Tired! Nerves!, Wasn't that Gym Leader super cool?!, Quitting is stupid. Make plans; do better.]"?After everything, what do you miss most about being a human?\ch[62,-1, Making my own decisions, Being able to speak!, Calling the shots in battle, Being a Pokémon is more fun actually, I miss other people., I don't! No responsibilities is great!, Either way is fine with me, Doing whatever I feel like!, The internet.]"%Back to your human self at last!"qWhich of these traits best describes you?\ch[62,-1, Independent/Strong-willed/Confident, Reserved/Timid/High-strung, Self-assured/Independent/Rational, Light-hearted/Playful/Versatile, Energetic/Impulsive/Affectionate, Insecure/Devoted/Unique, Prideful/Tough/Solitary, Isolatory/Mysterious/Reclusive, Free-thinking/Spirited/Stubborn, Intelligent/Analytical/Creative, Optimistic/Inspiring/Kind-hearted, Intellectual/Curious/Withdrawn, Passionate/Ambitious/Quick-tempered, Wise/Confident/Imaginative, Peaceful/Caring/Compassionate, Mischievous/Misunderstood/Humorous, Understanding/Even-tempered/Subdued, Steadfast/Loyal/Tough]"Final question!"�Just for our records to improve this quiz, what is your favorite Type?\ch[62,-1, Normal, Fire, Water, Electric, Grass, Ice, Fighting, Poison, Ground, Flying, Psychic, Bug, Rock, Ghost, Dragon, Dark, Steel, Fairy]"...Whew!"3That took a while, but you made it to the end!"+Okay, let's tally up your results now!".". ."
. . ."And done!"You are a... \v[719] Type!"eYou can see what you scored for each Type on that computer there, or see what your result means."But there you go!"9You know, I happened to find this Gem the other day."3Since it matches you, you may as well take it."fYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "mononormal"."dYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monofire"."eYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monowater"."hYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monoelectric"."eYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monograss"."cYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monoice"."hYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monofighting"."fYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monopoison"."fYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monoground"."fYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monoflying"."gYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monopsychic"."cYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monobug"."dYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monorock"."eYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monoghost"."fYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monodragon"."dYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monodark"."eYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monosteel"."eYou know, the next time someone asks you for a password, you could try telling them "monofairy".")It won't obligate you into anything."{It'll just make it so you'll probably find more Pokémon of that type in specific cases where you might otherwise not."Anyway, take care.";You can come by if you ever wanna take the quiz again.">Well, that's fine. It'll be here if you change your mind.":Or have the time to sit through like forty questions."!Geez, who writes this stuff?"You are a:\n \v[719] Type!"Normal: \v[701]"Fire: \v[702]"Water: \v[703]"Electric: \v[704]"Grass: \v[705]"Ice: \v[706]"Fighting: \v[707]"Poison: \v[708]"Ground: \v[709]"Flying: \v[710]"Psychic: \v[711]"Bug: \v[712]"Rock: \v[713]"Ghost: \v[714]"Dragon: \v[715]"Dark: \v[716]"Steel: \v[717]"Fairy: \v[718]"�Please select a Type.\ch[62,-1, Normal, Fire, Water, Electric, Grass, Ice, Fighting, Poison, Ground, Flying, Psychic, Bug, Rock, Ghost, Dragon, Dark, Steel, Fairy]"CNormal Types are usually light-hearted and easy- going people."@Like everyone else, they have their flaws and insecurities,"�But perhaps uniquely, they're able to accept themselves and others in spite of their flaws, and are experts at making the best of situations both good and bad."3Fire Types are all about passion and ambition."RThey're earnest and active. When they want something, they go for it all-out."bThere's no better go-getter, but Fire Types risk pushing themselves too hard and burning out."tThey're great at getting things done, but when it happens, it's sure to be on their schedule and no one else's."4Water Types are masters of going with the flow."�Balancing cool rationality with a deep understanding of their own and others' emotions, they're adept at understanding all sides of a conflict."�As extremely adaptable individuals, they can adjust to any sort of scenario-- even if it would be unhealthy-- and make it their own."$Electric Types light up a room!"\Energetic, forthright and cheerful, they bring an unrivaled spirit to any conversation."�Their impulsiveness can often lead to things getting out of hand, but their positive nature lends itself to smoothing over conflicts and making a lot of fun memories along the way."6Grass Types tend to put others before themselves."�They go out of their way to help and soothe others, and are great contributors to making the world a more positive, peaceful place."�Despite the fact that their habitual benevolence wins plenty of friends, they can also sometimes be insecure and prone to having doubts."^In reality though, Grass Types are often much more cherished than they will ever realize."?Ice Types are some of the most charming and unique people,"#But seldom do they realize it."qMany Ice Types hide behind a veil of aloofness, often hiding how much they truly worry or care about others."cTheir cool distance serves both to entice others, suggesting an air of mystery and refinement,"�But at the same time, in hiding how much they truly care, they risk pushing others away and missing out on welcome opportunities."0Fighting Types are models of determination."�Understanding that it is not the 100th strike that cracks the stone, but the 99 that came before it, no one is better able to set their mind to a task and stick to it."�Working with a tireless fervor that many others can only dream of, Fighting Types are sure to achieve whatever they pursue with enough time and patience."dPoison Types are prone to resigning themselves to circumstances they don't truly wish to be in."RThey value others above themselves, and may give up on themselves too easily."}In spite of these things, they often don't realize that they make for some of the best and closest friends that can be found."�Without ever realizing their own importance, they serve vital roles in the lives of those around them, all the while slowly building themselves up."-Ground Types are pragmatic and stubborn."|Unphased by traditional notions of what's "right" or "best", Ground Types view life and society from the outside looking in."�They prefer to remain with their ideals regardless of the consequences, which tends to work out well given how firmly rooted in results and effectiveness they often are."-Flying Types are free-spirited dreamers!"Always looking for bigger, better, more exciting things, they aren't necessarily bound to what they """should""" be doing."�Sometimes this gets them in trouble, but some might say Flying Types have an uncanny ability to just narrowly avoid whatever dire consequences would come of their mischief."bMoreover, they have a ton of fun doing whatever it is they do, and always get the last laugh."2Psychic Types are intelligent and analytical."=They value creativity, thoughtfulness and understanding."�They often see the pattern and reasons behind events and circumstances rather than the circumstances themselves, and thus thrive individually and socially."�While they can sometimes miss the forest for the trees and be extraordinarily unique in their own rites, they seem to seldom mind this.".Bug Types are intellectual and reclusive."iThey tend to be introverted, preferring books, games, or the internet to the company of real people."�The result is a surprisngly unique and refined perspective on many subjects, even if they are often unsure of how best to share it."�The best among Bug Types hollow out their own place in the world with like-minded individuals who share their passions and interests in the comforts of mutual respect and curiosity."0Rock Types are unshakably loyal companions."}Great at listening and following directions, those who earn the respect and service of a Rock Type are especially lucky."{Rock Types always stick up for their friends, faithfully serve their communities, and dutifully manage their families."�Despite this, they sometimes prefer to be left to their own devices, or might struggle to tear themselves away from negative people,"�But the burden of loyalty, while not an easy one to bear, is an invaluable and often overlooked cornerstone of society and our friendships."|While Ghost Types may appear intimidating or mean, at the end of the day, they're just practicing their sense of humor."bOften a darker humor, and sometimes at the expense of others, it is seldom truly ill-meaning."�Rather, cavalcades of jokes and pranks are both the sword and shield of a Ghost Type, serving to break the ice and earn favor with others, while also protecting their true, vulnerable selves from scrutiny."�Truly getting to know a Ghost Type beneath the surface can be a challenge in its own right, but should someone be let in, there's a bright and magnetic soul to be found."PDragon Types aren't weighed down by "common sense", rules, or expectations."xAs free-thinkers who read between the lines, they have a wealth of things to offer the world and those around them."|They can be intense and particular, but only because they quickly come to understand in wisdom what many others cannot."�Dragon Types often struggle to make close friends, but when they do attach to people, it is never lightly, always forming an unshakable bond sure to alter each of their lives forevermore."&Dark Types are the most reserved."}They tend to be in conflict with both others around them and themselves, and often prefer to keep their distance as a result."XNevertheless, Dark Types have many hidden strengths, varying from person to person."~Often able to do things others aren't, or with a perspective no one else would have, they can make for invaluable allies."MStill, it is rare that they ever let people too close to their hearts...",Steel Types don't let much get to them."zSteadfast, even-keel, and direct, they know what they want, how they want it, and one way or another, they'll get it."qWhile they can be prone to cynicism or nihilism, they often make reliable comrades and effective colleagues.".Fairy Types are optimistic and inspiring!"}They often strive to be a source of light and goodness in their communities, making for fast friends and strong leaders."~Their much-needed whimsy and creativity can often fill an emptiness where the dusts of routine and melancholy begin to settle."�But for all their goodness, Fairy Types expect the same respect from others as they offer, and if one fails to return it, the backlash can be severe..."Yes"No"All Scores"Result Analysis"CancelIu;␀[["W-whismur..."3Whismur is drawn to the PokéSnax in your bag!"Whis! Whiswhis, whismur!""The hungry Pokémon attacked!"*Good day. I am the owner of this lot."4I'm looking for a tenant to rent this space to."BIf you find anyone in need of a place to stay, do refer them.")This place is great, nice find, pal!"]Not that I have any furniture to move in, but I'm sure I'll find a way home before long."�Look, I really appreciate you helping me out here. I wanna give you something. Go ahead, take it. 'S a buddy of mine, but it'll be cool to you."4Take good care of it, all right? Yourself, too!["Chuchmur...";Chuchmur est attiré par le PokéSnack dans votre sac!"Chuch! Chuchuch, chuchmur!"!Le Pokémon affamé attaque!"2Bonjour. Je suis le propriétaire de ce lieu."0Je cherche quelqu'un à qui louer mon bien."YSi vous trouvez quelqu'un qui cherche un endroit où rester, veuillez l'en informer."3Cet appartement est pas mal! Bonne trouvaille!"~J'ai pas vraiment d'affaires pour m'installer, mais je suis sûr que je trouverai un moyen de rentrer chez moi très bientôt."�J'apprécie beaucoup ce que tu as fait pour moi. Je veux te donner quelque chose. Allez, prends-le! C'est un ami à moi. Ça me fait plaisir."<Prends-en bien soin, hein? Et prends soin de toi aussi!;["W-whismur..."3Whismur is drawn to the PokéSnax in your bag!"Whis! Whiswhis, whismur!""The hungry Pokémon attacked!"*Good day. I am the owner of this lot."4I'm looking for a tenant to rent this space to."BIf you find anyone in need of a place to stay, do refer them.")This place is great, nice find, pal!"]Not that I have any furniture to move in, but I'm sure I'll find a way 