rs."XDamage report complete! It seems peripheral structures were only damaged minimally.".So this wasn't an accident. Good to know."eYeah. The blast-type was a fairly controlled radius. It's usually used for municipal demolition."#The Stairway looks terrible...";I mean, even worse than it was before it was blown up."KSuch gorgeous, pristine water flowing in from the Carnelian Mountains."cThis waterfall feeds the Azurine Lake, which means all this water is going to be contaminated."bWelcome, come one, come all for the grand unveiling of Silph Co.'s most fabulous new product!",It's the best thing since indoor bread!"5The most convenient thing since sliced plumbing!"CLadies and gentlemen, may I present to you-- the "Link Stone"!"sAre you tired of having to find potentially untrustworthy Trainers to trade your Pokémon with to evolve them?"dAre you as heartbroken as your Pokémon is when it has to be traded away from you just to grow?"Your worries are over!"QThe Link Stone can force a Pokémon to evolve while never leaving your care!"SThe remarkable scientists of Silph Co. have produced this marvelous new Stone,"YInfused with the very energy emitted in a real trade that causes Pokémon to evolve!"PThis Link Stone will be hitting stores soon, but you all are a lucky bunch."iRight here, right now, you can get a prototype edition fully-functional Link Stone for just $10,000!"0\GBe the first to try it! What do you say?!"&There you go! One happy customer!"3I'm afraid you can't afford this! Anyone else?"6Suit yourself. Who wants to try it? Don't be shy!"BLook for the Link Stone at the Obsidia Department Store soon!"?FERN: Man, these bitch-ass cops won't even let us through."2Yeah, there was a terrorist threat. I get it."GBut they should be accepting help from the people to deal with it."VIf they could do it on their own, this wouldn't have happened in the first place."MThey're too tripped up on their own power and policies to even see that."=That right there is why the bad guys 