w immediately."Thank you."AOfficer, stand by. I'll have new orders for you momentarily."OFFICER: Yes, sir."/CHIEF: Good luck. I do hope you find them."?CHIEF: Two have returned now. But three are still missing."8CHIEF: You found one! But we're still missing four."\CHIEF: Three are back! Are things finally starting to look up? Well, there's still two.".CHIEF: Ah! There's only one more to find!"TCHIEF: By Jove, kid, you've done it! You found our entire missing police force!"DWell, there is the matter of the officer who died in service..."*You found his Growlithe, did you not?"�Like in many other regions, all of our officers are issued Growlithe as partner Pokémon. But now that its Trainer is gone, that Growlithe..."wI would feel it an insult to the memory of my former officer to simply give that Growlithe to another new recruit."�It may be difficult to understand, but if you would, please feel free to take Growlithe with you. You were the one to find it after all."/And after everything you've done for us...")Consider it a token of appreciation."HYou're now an honorary member of the Reborn City Police Department!"�CHIEF: It may be difficult to understand, but if you would, please feel free to take Growlithe with you. You were the one to find it after all."TAnd after everything you've done for us... Consider it a token of appreciation."TCHIEF: Back in full force, the Reborn City Police Department is ready to serve!" CHIEF: Greetings, civilian!"NWith everyone's help and new volunteers, our force is back at full power!"FIf anything is troubling you, please don't hesitate to inform us."MWe are committed to keeping this city a peaceful place once and for all!"HAhh, so you're interested in that "Corin-Rouge" character, are you?"(He's a confounding one, to be sure."�He is a flashy individual, but skilled at hiding and get- aways, so we've tracked much of his movement, though never been able to catch him."jNow that we've got many other obstacles out of the way, we've already begun to turn a focus onto him."OIf you'd like to take vanguard in the operation, it would be a great help!"Here's the situation:"JWe've received an increasing number of reports about his whereabouts."`That is, the numbers are so fast-increasing, it puts him in three different places at once!"uThe reports all came in around the same time, but for wildly different places. I'd like you to investigate them."2First, he was sighted around Malchous Forest."FA moment later, we heard he was on a small islet in Azurine Lake."]Finally, an officer reportedly saw him around the same time at Sunset Circle in Peridot."iMost of our officers are still occupied on the multitude of other tasks, so I shall leave it to you!".CHIEF: Good to see you again, old friend!"YThanks to your efforts, the Reborn City Police Department is back at full operation!"dIf you'd like to take vanguard in the operation, I'm sure we could catch him in no time at all!"rMost of our officers are still occupied on the multitude of other tasks, so I shall entrust this task to you."!CHIEF: Here's the situation:"KWe've received an increasing number of reports about his where-abouts.";Please investigate the areas and try to apprehend him!""CHIEF: Well? How has it gone?"3Hrm, so the three sightings were all decoys..."That crafty Corin..."$So the clues you gathered were:".Find him in the place where mists settle!".Find him in a place where Trainers fight!"2And "Find him buried in a pocket of peonies!""6How cryptic... Can you crack this caper, Trainer?"&I leave it in your capable hands."5What?! The Corin at the riddle was a decoy too?!"That sneaky Seviper..."7So one of the suspected clones was the real Corin!"]The one at Malchous Forest, the one at Sunset Circle, and the one around Azurine Lake..."eIf he was trying to buy time, he would probably choose the place that had the best escape route."You have to hurry, \PN!"-CHIEF: Any news on the Corin-Rouge case?"..."'So he was able to flee the city..."'I see. Then it's out of our hands.".Well, don't feel too bad about it, sport."!You did well in finding him."WAnd one way or another, he's gone, so he won't be hurting anyone here for a while."/Still... I suspect he won't stray too far."qHe knows this area like the back of his hand, meaning he'll probably come back after laying low for a while.")Considering the direction he took..."/There might still be a chance to find him."6Of course, the one most suited to the job is you."EJust make sure to drag him back here so we can lock the lout up!"Ah, I know!"eIf you're going to chase him north into the Tourmaline Desert, maybe these can help protect you." CHIEF: Good luck out there!"6CHIEF: I suspect Corin-Rouge won't stray too far."CHIEF: Ho, there!"@That knave Corin-Rouge seems to have had a change of heart!"=He just showed up one day and held out his hands for us!"9Didn't speak a word or even make direct eye contact.":I don't suppose you know anything about all that, eh?"GROWLITHE: Grrowrrr..."GROWLITHE: Growrithe!"}Let's see... If I remember right, we had two officers stationed in Jasper, and three in Beryl, all of whom went missing."!So that's everything. Right."'Let's get this city back on track."*Thanks for helping me out back there!"6OFFICER: Hey, you see the guy across the counter?"pHe's been feeling really down ever since Team Meteor stole his Growlithe. I wanna do something to help him."lI know the Chief won't give him the spare Growlithe that we had, but I think there's a way around that."NWould you be willing to breed that Growlithe and give me one of the Eggs?"6OFFICER: No, no. It's a lot to ask, I understand."+OFFICER: You'll really give it to him?"LThank you so much! I'm sure this will really make a difference for him!"]Say, I picked up an abandoned Egg a while ago and I've been holding onto it for a while."QCouldn't tell you what'll come of it, but why don't you take that in return?"4\PN traded the GROWLITHE EGG for a MYSTERY EGG!"KOFFICER: ...Huh, doesn't this 