 was just the excuse he used to keep himself locked up."KRather than being strong, isn't it better to learn to care for others?"0He was as weak and scared as any other kid."$If only he knew how to show it."HEATHER: So it's settled!"0That's the kind of heroine I'm going to be!"CAny old clown in a suit can punch a villain and call it a day,"6But who are the ones practicing true compassion?!"4That's a job only a magical wind maiden can do!Iu;␀�X[[�"R...So my roommate said she was gonna convert our place into a streamer house."5Naturally, I thought she meant online streaming."+In retrospect, this was foolish of me."Sandy, what the hell..."[Welcome! This is the meeting place of Reborn's Geography Club! Fascinating, is it not?"UWelcome! This is the meeting place of Reborn's History Club! Isn't it wonderful?"7Hello! Would you like to hear about the Opal Ward?"�The Opal Ward is right in the heart of Reborn City! It's one of the busiest wards, often bustling with Trainers and pedestrians alike!"}Opal Bridge, the walkway between the lower-level of the ward and the Obsidia Ward in itself, is a renowned battling location!"XNew Trainers show up there for challenges all the time, so always be on your guard!"�Of course, should you need to heal, simply stroll down to the Grand Hall! One of the largest buildings in Reborn, and the only one in Opal!"oThe Grand Hall has its own center, mart, and is generally a hub for the Reborn League. 'Tis a great place!":Hello! Would you like to hear about the Obsidia Ward?"�The Obsidia Ward is Reborn's largest ward, oftentimes considered in two separate halves, the main and south area, and North Obsidia."�Of course, we're in North Obsidia now, but the two halves have even been cut off from each other after the recent earthquakes. Oh my!"�After all, underneath the Obsidia Ward is a network of railway tunnels. When the earthquakes hit, the hollow foundation gave way!"Not only is the tunnel unusable, but much of the ward was destroyed, including the HQ of Reborn's largest company, Yureyu!"bWhile North Obsidia features the massive Grand Stairway, a monument leading outside the city,"Central Obsidia is now the prime commercial district. There are salons, shops, and even a beautiful park all along Main Street!"7Hello! Would you like to hear about the Onyx Ward?"�The Onyx Ward is one of the finest residential wards in the city. This may perhaps be because of its close location to the Onyx Trainers' School!"More than just a school, it also doubles as a Reborn League Gym! Young Trainers of all kinds flock there for their own reasons!"oBetween that and the Onyx Arcade, the Onyx Ward is one of the most youthful and lively places in the city!":Hello! Would you like to hear about the Peridot Ward?"~The Peridot Ward is the second largest in the city! More than any other, however, it's also primarily an industrial ward."iFactories and warehouses line its shores of Azurine Lake... Many lower-income people live there too!"lUnfortunately, as a result, the Peridot Ward has become notorious for homelessness and gang activity..."�On a lighter note, the Power Plant and Reborn League Gym is also located there, not far from the Peridot Station, the best way in and out of Reborn!"9Hello! Would you like to hear about the Jasper Ward?"aBordering the peaceful Malchous Forest, the Jasper Ward is a very moderate residential area."bMany families of middle class live there- or... I should correct, did until quite recently..."iWith the recent overexpansion of the Malchous Forest, Jasper has become somewhat of a ruin, sadly..."8Hello! Would you like to hear about the Lapis Ward?":The Lapis Ward is one of the highest-class in Reborn!"~Perhaps rivaled only by the Onyx Ward, it's an ideal place for a family, with some of the lowest crime rates in the city!"IIt's also one of the few locations unaffected by recent disasters..."qMost notable in the Lapis Ward are a Reborn League Gym and Dr. Connal's Orphanage. You can hardly miss them!"8Hello! Would you like to hear about the Beryl Ward?"ZBordering the Rhodochrine Jungle, the Beryl Ward is among the larger wards in Reborn."�Although the recent disaster has spelled an end for much of its residence, Beryl was formerly a very unique middle-class community."pIt also held a reputation of being one of the sightseeing places in the city, as it is the highest-up ward!"^It offers great views of the Tourmaline Desert, Reborn City, and even the Azurine Region!"8Hello! Would you like to hear about the Coral Ward?"rThe Coral Ward is the smallest ward of Reborn, tucked into the corner of the Azurine Lake near South Obsidia."�Its main attraction has been its port! Coral is normally a very lively location full of hard workers and tourists traveling the lake!"dUnfortunately, thanks to the recent water quality, there's been little need to go down there..."?Interested in learning about Reborn's geography! Splendid!"~I'll give you one quick tip! Often times we refer to places, for instance the Azurine Region, just so, with the word 'Region'."�While it may be confusing to some, this use of the word 'Region' varies from that of places like the Hoenn Region, Kanto Region, or Reborn Region."|When we talk about regions here, think of them more as sub-regions, as they are all places within the greater Reborn Region!">Hello! Would you like to hear about the Chrysolia Region?"]Much of Chrysolia is an old forest, formerly connecting Reborn City and the Orre Region!"zOther landmarks include the quaint Spinel Town, and the Tanzan Mountain area, a network of sprawing trails and caves!"<Hello! Would you like to hear about the Azurine Region?"BThe Azurine Region lies across Azurine Lake from Reborn City!"�Full of beaches and mountains, it's quite an empty place, speaking in terms of the locals. In fact, there's only one settlement there!"|On the Apophyll Beach, there is a small Academy! Sometimes Trainers who wish not to study in the city will go there instead."^There is also an island not far off, known as Azurine Island. Little is known about it..."vFinally, a massive volcano, known as Pyrous Mountain, towers above the area, shedding a layer of ash across it..."AHello! Would you like to hear about the Byxbysion Wasteland?"~The Byxbysion Wasteland is a treacherous jumble of debris that surrounds the entire southern border of the Reborn Region."TThose who venture far out into it seldom return, so little is known about it..."tBut whispers of discovered ruins and objects suggest perhaps there was once something else beneath the filth..."\Something from a story since passed and forgotten... Orre it could simply be a rumor..."?Hello! Would you like to hear about the Aventurine Region?"LThe Aventurine Region lies just north of here, through the Grand Gates!"�On the whole, it's one of the most beautiful places in Reborn, with lush forests, rich peaks, and even a special crystal valley..."�Also around are the Celestinine River, the famous Agate Circus, and Agate City with a history older than it belies... As well as a mysterious castle..."?Hello! Would you like to hear about the Tourmaline Desert?"^The Tourmaline Desert reaches for miles, bordering the northern end of the Reborn Region!"�Many newcomers travel via train across the desert from very far away. What those Trainers don't know is the desert's mysterious history!"kThe train tracks have had to been rebuilt several times, thanks to a multitude of strange accidents..."]As a result, a strange scrapyard of train parts rests out in the middle of the desert..."|Sometimes, it even stands in the shadow of an enormous tower... But as soon as you blink- the tower vanishes! How curious..."=Hello! Would you like to hear about the Carnelia Region?"�The Carnelia Region is home to the twin cities of Calcenon and Labradorra! They rest in the valley of some of the tallest mountains in Reborn!"�Though all topped with icy peaks, the largest by far is Ametrine Mountain! It overshadows even the most important Charous Mountain..."1...where the Reborn League Champion waits..."
Uh..."#Oh, yes, I'm the Move Deleter.",I can make Pokémon forget their moves.""Would you like me to do that?")Which Pokémon should forget a move?"=Come again if there are moves that need to be forgotten."(What? No Egg should know any moves."6What? I can't make Shadow Pokémon forget a move.")\v[3] seems to know only one move..."$Which move should be forgotten?"6Hm! \v[3]'s \v[4]? That move should be forgotten?"It worked to perfection!"*\v[3] has forgotten \v[4] completely."COREY: ..."...Zor..."ZORUA: Zorrrrrrrrrrr!"ARC: Knock knock, Dad."You've got company.".DAD: Oh, my boy, it's so good to see you!"Come in, come in!"ARC: ...Seriously, Dad?"This place is a mess."<DAD: Ahh, I've been so busy lately, you know how it is?"ARC: I do know how it is."Do better.")ARC: Sorry, \PN, just give me a sec."Make yourself at home.":DAD: Aren't you going to introduce me to your friend?"&ARC: Right, so, Dad, this is \PN."He's the Champion."She's the Champion."They're the Champion."DAD: The Champion?!"$You are running in high places!"<You did not tell me you were meeting with the Champion!"+ARC: There's a lot I haven't told you." Stuff was busy for a while."1But, that's part of why I wanted to drop by.".Say "Hi" to Mom, let you know I'm safe..."Everything's good."&DAD: That is very good to hear..."=ARC: Also, Jay said you were asking him for money again."PDAD: Ohhhhh no, no no no, I told your brother not to bother you with that--"ARC: Dad,"HDAD: You don't have to worry about it, you've done enough already--"ARC: Dad, listen."'If you need money, you come to me."Not him,"Me."Understand?"4DAD: Yes, yes, yes, it was just a minor thing--"0ARC: Even for minor things, you come to me."-He needs to be free to stand on his own."Are we clear?"DAD: Yes, yes, yes..."We are clear."ARC: Good." ARC: Here's for this month."LThere's a little extra, because Mom mentioned something about the sink."$DAD: Oh... Yes, yes, thank you."/I-- I don't know what we'd do without you."ARC: I know."How's Mom?"DAD: The usual..."Same as usual."KShe's sleeping right now, but I'm sure she won't mind if you say "Hi"."ARC: I'll do that."ARC: Come with me."Sorry about that." ARC: She's had a hard time.".I won't bore you with the details, but..."-This is how she spends most of her time."#ARC: I just wanted you to see."GLike I said, we gotta work hard to take care of those close to us."ARC: Hey, Mom."We've got a visitor."IARC: So... we took care of the situation I told you about last time."Or, \PN did."7Now it's about clean up and getting back on track."3I've been working with a group of guys lately."LUsed to be called the Magma Gang, but they're putting that behind them."KUsed to be called the Aqua Gang, but they're putting that behind them."They're a good bunch."Spirited."hSo, we ran across this urban camper the other day, and he didn't wanna move, because of course not."�There was the usual argument about shelters, but then one of the guys brought up, "Who actually owns the space he's camping on?""!Who's permission do we need?"PSo we did some digging, and you wouldn't believe who it turned out to be..."Yes"No[�"V...Ma coloc' a dit qu'elle voulait faire passer un max de courant dans la maison."GJe pensais, naturellement, qu'elle voulait parler d'électricité."&Avec le recul, j'ai été naïve."Sandy, franchement..."gBienvenue! C'est le lieu de rendez-vous du Club de Géographie de Reborn! Fascinant, n'est-ce pas?"dBienvenue! C'est le lieu de rendez-vous du Club d'Histoire de Reborn! n'est-ce pas merveilleux?"EBonjour! Voudriez-vous des renseignements sur le Quartier Opale?"�Le Quartier Opale est au cœur de Reborn! C’est l’un de ses quartiers lesplus actifs, fourmillant de monde – y compris de nombreux Dresseurs!"�Le Pont Opale, le passage entre la partie basse du quartier du même nom et le Quartier Obsidienne, est connu pour les combats de Pokémon qu’on peut y faire."lDe nouveaux Dresseurs en quête de défis s’y pressent continuellement, soyez-y donc toujours prêts."�Bien sûr, si vous voulez soigner vos Pokémon, le Grand Hall est à deux pas! C’est l’un des plus grands bâtiments de Reborn, et le plus notable du Quartier Opale!"�Le Grand Hall possède son propre Centre Pokémon et ses propres boutiques, et est plus généralement un point de rencontre pour les participants à la Ligue de Reborn. C’est un endroit extraordinaire!"PBonjour! Voudriez-vous avoir des renseignements sur le Quartier Obsidienne?"�Le Quartier Obsdienne est le plus grand quartier de la ville de Reborn, souvent considéré comme deux quartiers réunis, la zone principale et Sud, et la zone Nord."�Bien sûr, nous sommes à Obsidienne Nord ici, mais les deux quartiers ont été séparées par les terribles séismes. Rendez-vous compte!"�Après tout, les souterrains du Quartier Obsidienne sont un réseau de métro souterrain. Quand les séismes sont survenus, toutes les fondations se sont affaissées!"�Non seulement le tunnel est inutilisable, mais la plupart du quartier a été détruit, dont le siège social de la plus grande entreprise de Reborn, Yureyu!"iAlors qu'Obsidienne Nord comprend le Grand Escalier, un monument qui mène à la sortie de la ville."�Obsidienne Centrale est aujourd'hui la principale zone commerciale. Il y a des salons, des magasins, et même un magnifique parc le long de la Grande Rue!"JBonjour! Voudriez-vous avoir des renseignements sur le Quartier Onyx?"�Le Quartier Onyx est l'un des quartiers résidentiels les plus modernes de la ville. C'est probablement parce que sa proximité avec l'École des Dresseurs d'Onyx!"�Plus qu'une école, c'est aussi une Arène de la Ligue de Reborn! Des Dresseurs de toute sorte se retrouvent ici pour différentes raisons!"iEntre ça et le Casino d'Onyx, le Quartier Onyx est le quartier jeune et le plus animé de la ville!"HBonjour! Voudriez-vous des renseignements sur le Quartier Péridot?"*Le Quartier Péridot est le deuxième plus grand quartier de la ville! Il est aussi principalement une zone industrielle."�Les usines et les entrepôts s'alignent sur les bordures du Lac Azurrine... Les classes les plus populaires vivent ici également."nMalheusement, cela a eu pour conséquence de faire de Péridot le quartier des sans-abris et des gangs..."�Pour terminer sur une note plus lègèren la Centrale et l'Arène sont aussi là-bas, non loin de la Gare Bellevue, l'entrée et la sortie de Reborn!"EBonjour! Voudriez-vous des renseignements sur le Quartier Jaspe?"sBordant l'apaisante Forêt Mauverte, le Quartier Jaspe est une zone résidentiellle pour les classes moyennes."jBeaucoup de familles vivent ici- ou... devrais-je plutôt dire, vivaient jusqu'à très récemment..."rAvec la récente surexpansion de la Forêt Mauverte, Jaspe est malheureusement devenu un quartier en ruine..."JBonjour! Voudriez-vous des informations sur le Quartier Lapis-Lazuli?"=Le Quartier Lapis-Lazuli est le quartier chic de Reborn!"�Seulement rivalisé par le Quartier Onyx, c'est l'endroit idéal pour les familles, avec un taux de crime très bas par rapport à la ville!"RC'est aussi l'un des rares endroits épargnés par les récents désastres..."�Les lieux remarquables dans le Quartier Lapis-Lazuli sont l'Arène et l'Orphelinat du Dr. Connal. Vous pouvez difficilement les manquer!"DBonjour! Voulez-vous des renseignements sur le Quartier Béryl?"XC’est l’un des plus grands quartiers de Reborn. Il jouxte la Jungle Rhodocrine."�Avant la catastrophe récente qui l’a vidé de la plupart de ses habitants, le Quartier Béryl était un lieu de vie privilégié pour les classes moyennes."zCe quartier, étant le plus élevé de Reborn, est réputé pour le point de vue qu’il offre sur la ville entière."~De là, on peut avoir un excellent panorama sur la ville entière, le Désert de Tourmaline, et même la Région Azurine!"LBonjour! Voudriez-vous avoir des renseignements sur le Quartier Corail?"zLe Quartier Corail est le plus petit quartier de la ville, situé dans le coin du Lac Azurine près d'Obsidienne Sud."�Sa principale attraction est son port! Corail est en temps normal un lieu très animé, tant par les travailleurs que par les touristes!"nMalheureusement, à cause de la qualité de l'eau actuelle, il y a peu de raisons de se rendre là-bas..."6La géographie de Reborn t'intéresse? Splendide!"�Je vais te donner une petite astuce! Nous utilisons souvent le mot "région" pour désigner certains endroits comme la Région d'Azurine."�Cela peut être un peu perturbant. En fait, c'est un sens du mot "Région" un peu différent de celui de Région d'Hoenn, Région de Kanto ou Région de Reborn."Quand nous parlons de ces régions, ce sont plus des sous-régions, qui font toutes partie de la grande Région de Reborn!"HBonjour! Voudriez-vous des renseignements sur la Région Chrysolia?"oChrysolia est notamment recouverte d'une ancienne forêt, qui relie la ville de Reborn et la Région Orre!"Certains points notables sont le Village Spinelle, et la Montagne Tanzan, véritable réseau de grottes et de souterrains."FBonjour! Voudriez-vous des renseignements sur la Région Azurine?"_La Région Azurine est de l'autre côté du Lac Azurine par rapport à la ville de Reborn."Pleins de plages et de montagnes, c'est un endroit plutôt désertique. À vrai dire, il n'y a qu'un seul village là-bas!"�Sur la Plage d'Apophylle, il y a une petite Académie! Parfois, les Dresseurs qui souhaitent ne pas étudier en ville se rendent là-bas à la place!"lIl y a aussi une île tout près, appelée l'Île Azurine. Il y a peu de choses connues à son sujet..."zEnfin, ce volcan massif, connu sous le nom de Mont Pyros, surplombe la zone et la recouvre d'une couche de cendres..."GBonjour! Voudriez-vous des informations sur le Crassier Byxbysion?"lLe Crassier Byxbysion est un méli-mélo insidieux de débris qui couvrent l'ensemble du Sud de Reborn."fCeux qui s'y enfoncent en reviennent rarement, alors il y a peu d'informations sur cet endroit..."}Mais les rumeurs parlent de ruines et d'objets qui suggèrent qu'il y avait autrefois quelque chose sous toute cette saleté."`Quelque chose sur des temps passés et oubliés... Mais c'est sûrement juste une rumeur..."OBonjour! Voudriez-vous avoir des renseignements sur la Région Aventurine?"\La Région Aventurine se situe juste au Nord d'ici, juste derrière les Grandes Portes!"�Dans l'ensemble, c'est l'une des plus belles régions de Reborn, avec ses forêts luxuriantes, sa faune riche, et même une vallée de cristaux..."�La région est bordée par la Rivière Célestine, le célèbre Cirque d'Agate et Agate, une ville d'histoire... Il y a aussi un mystérieux château..."OBonjour! Voudriez-vous avoir des renseignements sur le Désert Tourmaline?"_Le Désert Tourmaline s'étend sur des kilomètres et borde sur la Région Nord de Reborn!"�Beaucoup de nouveaux arrivants viennent de très loin et traversent le désert en train. Ce que ces Dresseurs ne savent pas, c'est que le désert regorge de mystères!"gLes rails du train ont du être reconstruits de nombreuses fois, à cause d'accidents étranges..."TDu fait, une décharge de restes de train s'est formée au milieu de désert..."�Parfois, l'ombre d'une énorme tour recouvre la décharge... Mais en un battement de cils, la tour disparaît! Tellement bizarre..."HBonjour! Voudriez-vous des renseignements sur la Région Carnélia?"�La Région Carnélia comporte les villes jumelles Calcinéon et Labradorra! Elles surplombent la vallée des plus grandes montagnes de Reborn!"�Même si elles sont plus petites que les sommets glacés, notamment la Montagne Amétrine qui est encore plus plus grande que le Mont Chaorite lui-même."X...Mont Chaorite qui est l'endroit où le Maître de la Ligue de Reborn patiente..."Euh...";Ha, oui, c'est vrai. Je suis l'Effaceur de Capacités."9Je peux faire oublier aux Pokémon leurs capacités."!Voudrais-tu que je le fasse?"2Quel Pokémon voudrait oublier une capacité?"CReviens si tu as des capacités qui devraient être oubliées."1Quoi? Un Œuf ne connaît pas de capacités."6What? I can't make Shadow Pokémon forget a move."0\v[3] ne connaît qu'une seule capacité..."0Quelle capacité dois-je lui faire oublier?"AHmm! \v[4] de \v[3]? Cette capacité devrait être oubliée?"%Cela a marché à la perfection!")\v[3] a complètement oublié \v[4]."COREY: ..."...Zor..."ZORUA: Zorrrrrrrrrrr!"ARC: Knock knock, Dad."You've got company.".DAD: Oh, my boy, it's so good to see you!"Come in, come in!"ARC: ...Seriously, Dad?"This place is a mess."<DAD: Ahh, I've been so busy lately, you know how it is?"ARC: I do know how it is."Do better.")ARC: Sorry, \PN, just give me a sec."Make yourself at home.":DAD: Aren't you going to introduce me to your friend?"&ARC: Right, so, Dad, this is \PN."He's the Champion."She's the Champion."They're the Champion."DAD: The Champion?!"$You are running in high places!"<You did not tell me you were meeting with the Champion!"+ARC: There's a lot I haven't told you." Stuff was busy for a while."1But, that's part of why I wanted to drop by.".Say "Hi" to Mom, let you know I'm safe..."Everything's good."&DAD: That is very good to hear..."=ARC: Also, Jay said you were asking him for money again."PDAD: Ohhhhh no, no no no, I told your brother not to bother you with that--"ARC: Dad,"HDAD: You don't have to worry about it, you've done enough already--"ARC: Dad, listen."'If you need money, you come to me."Not him,"Me."C'est clair?"4DAD: Yes, yes, yes, it was just a minor thing--"0ARC: Even for minor things, you come to me."-He needs to be free to stand on his own."Are we clear?"DAD: Yes, yes, yes..."We are clear."ARC: Bien." ARC: Here's for this month."LThere's a little extra, because Mom mentioned something about the sink."$DAD: Oh... Yes, yes, thank you."/I-- I don't know what we'd do without you."ARC: I know."Comment va Maman?"DAD: The usual..."Same as usual."KShe's sleeping right now, but I'm sure she won't mind if you say "Hi"."ARC: I'll do that."ARC: Come with me."Désolé pour ça." ARC: She's had a hard time.".I won't bore you with the details, but..."-This is how she spends most of her time."#ARC: I just wanted you to see."GLike I said, we gotta work hard to take care of those close to us."ARC: Hey, Mom."We've got a visitor."IARC: So... we took care of the situation I told you about last time."Or, \PN did."7Now it's about clean up and getting back on track."3I've been working with a group of guys lately."LUsed to be called the Magma Gang, but they're putting that behind them."KUsed to be called the Aqua Gang, but they're putting that behind them."They're a good bunch."Spirited."hSo, we ran across this urban camper the other day, and he didn't wanna move, because of course not."�There was the usual argument about shelters, but then one of the guys brought up, "Who actually owns the space he's camping on?""!Who's permission do we need?"PSo we did some digging, and you wouldn't believe who it turned out to be..."Oui"Non;[�"R...So my roommate said she was gonna convert our place into a streamer house."5Naturally, I thought she meant online streaming."+In retrospect, this was foolish of me."Sandy, what the hell..."[Welcome! This is the meeting place of Reborn's Geography Club! Fascinating, is it not?"UWelcome! This is the meeting place of Reborn's History Club! Isn't it wonderful?"7Hello! Would you like to hear about the Opal Ward?"�The Opal Ward is right in the heart of Reborn City! It's one of the busiest wards, often bustling with Trainers and pedestrians alike!"}Opal Bridge, the walkway between the lower-level of the ward and the Obsidia Ward in itself, is a renowned battling location!"XNew Trainers show up there for challenges all the time, so always be on your guard!"�Of course, should you need to heal, simply stroll down to the Grand Hall! One of the largest buildings in Reborn, and the only one in Opal!"oThe Grand Hall has its own center, mart, and is generally a hub for the Reborn League. 'Tis a great place!":Hello! Would you like to hear about the Obsidia Ward?"�The Obsidia Ward is Reborn's largest ward, oftentimes considered in two separate halves, the main and south area, and North Obsidia."�Of course, we're in North Obsidia now, but the two halves have even been cut off from each other after the recent earthquakes. Oh my!"�After all, underneath the Obsidia Ward is a network of railway tunnels. When the earthquakes hit, the hollow foundation gave way!"Not only is the tunnel unusable, but much of the ward was destroyed, including the HQ of Reborn's largest company, Yureyu!"bWhile North Obsidia features the massive Grand Stairway, a monument leading outside the city,"Central Obsidia is now the prime commercial district. There are salons, shops, and even a beautiful park all along Main Street!"7Hello! Would you like to hear about the Onyx Ward?"�The Onyx Ward is one of the finest residential wards in the city. This may perhaps be because of its close location to the Onyx Trainers' School!"More than just a school, it also doubles as a Reborn League Gym! Young Trainers of all kinds flock there for their own reasons!"oBetween that and the Onyx Arcade, the Onyx Ward is one of the most youthful and lively places in the city!":Hello! Would you like to hear about the Peridot Ward?"~The Peridot Ward is the second largest in the city! More than any other, however, it's also primarily an industrial ward."iFactories and warehouses line its shores of Azurine Lake... Many lower-income people live there too!"lUnfortunately, as a result, the Peridot Ward has become notorious for homelessness and gang activity..."�On a lighter note, the Power Plant and Reborn League Gym is also located there, not far from the Peridot Station, the best way in and out of Reborn!"9Hello! Would you like to hear about the Jasper Ward?"aBordering the peaceful Malchous Forest, the Jasper Ward is a very moderate residential area."bMany families of middle class live there- or... I should correct, did until quite recently..."iWith the recent overexpansion of the Malchous Forest, Jasper has become somewhat of a ruin, sadly..."8Hello! Would you like to hear about the Lapis Ward?":The Lapis Ward is one of the highest-class in Reborn!"~Perhaps rivaled only by the Onyx Ward, it's an ideal place for a family, with some of the lowest crime rates in the city!"IIt's also one of the few locations unaffected by recent disasters..."qMost notable in the Lapis Ward are a Reborn League Gym and Dr. Connal's Orphanage. You can hardly miss them!"8Hello! Would you like to hear about the Beryl Ward?"ZBordering the Rhodochrine Jungle, the Beryl Ward is among the larger wards in Reborn."�Although the recent disaster has spelled an end for much of its residence, Beryl was formerly a very unique middle-class community."pIt also held a reputation of being one of the sightseeing places in the city, as it is the highest-up ward!"^It offers great views of the Tourmaline Desert, Reborn City, and even the Azurine Region!"8Hello! Would you like to hear about the Coral Ward?"rThe Coral Ward is the smallest ward of Reborn, tucked into the corner of the Azurine Lake near South Obsidia."�Its main attraction has been its port! Coral is normally a very lively location full of hard workers and tourists traveling the lake!"dUnfortunately, thanks to the recent water quality, there's been little need to go down there..."?Interested in learning about Reborn's geography! Splendid!"~I'll give you one quick tip! Often times we refer to places, for instance the Azurine Region, just so, with the word 'Region'."�While it may be confusing to some, this use of the word 'Region' varies from that of places like the Hoenn Region, Kanto Region, or Reborn Region."|When we talk about regions here, think of them more as sub-regions, as they are all places within the greater Reborn Region!">Hello! Would you like to hear about the Chrysolia Region?"]Much of Chrysolia is an old forest, formerly connecting Reborn City and the Orre Region!"zOther landmarks include the quaint Spinel Town, and the Tanzan Mountain area, a network of sprawing trails and caves!"<Hello! Would you like to hear about the Azurine Region?"BThe Azurine Region lies across Azurine Lake from Reborn City!"�Full of beaches and mountains, it's quite an empty place, speaking in terms of the locals. In fact, there's only one settlement there!"|On the Apophyll Beach, there is a small Academy! Sometimes Trainers who wish not to study in the city will go there instead."^There is also an island not far off, known as Azurine Island. Little is known about it..."vFinally, a massive volcano, known as Pyrous Mountain, towers above the area, shedding a layer of ash across it..."AHello! Would you like to hear about the Byxbysion Wasteland?"~The Byxbysion Wasteland is a treacherous jumble of debris that surrounds the entire southern border of the Reborn Region."TThose who venture far out into it seldom return, so little is known about it..."tBut whispers of discovered ruins and objects suggest perhaps there was once something else beneath the filth..."\Something from a story since passed and forgotten... Orre it could simply be a rumor..."?Hello! Would you like to hear about the Aventurine Region?"LThe Aventurine Region lies just north of here, through the Grand Gates!"�On the whole, it's one of the most beautiful places in Reborn, with lush forests, rich peaks, and even a special crystal valley..."�Also around are the Celestinine River, the famous Agate Circus, and Agate City with a history older than it belies... As well as a mysterious castle..."?Hello! Would you like to hear about the Tourmaline Desert?"^The Tourmaline Desert reaches for miles, bordering the northern end of the Reborn Region!"�Many newcomers travel via train across the desert from very far away. What those Trainers don't know is the desert's mysterious history!"kThe train tracks have had to been rebuilt several times, thanks to a multitude of strange accidents..."]As a result, a strange scrapyard of train parts rests out in the middle of the desert..."|Sometimes, it even stands in the shadow of an enormous tower... But as soon as you blink- the tower vanishes! How curious..."=Hello! Would you like to hear about the Carnelia Region?"�The Carnelia Region is home to the twin cities of Calcenon and Labradorra! They rest in the valley of some of the tallest mountains in Reborn!"�Though all topped with icy peaks, the largest by far is Ametrine Mountain! It overshadows even the most important Charous Mountain..."1...where the Reborn League Champion waits..."
