t have to work."Just let me be in peace."�CRAUDBURRY: Miserable lout, PATHETIC inventory, if this is really all you've got, you ought to be ashamed of your scruffy-rumped self!"=Don't call again until you have something worth my time!"CRAUDBURRY: Oh, it's you."RI shoulda known I'd see low-life scum like you lollygagging around down here."kDon't look at me, criminal swine, you aren't worth my breath! Drivelling mucus with every step... Bah!"7ARCHER: Quite the mouth that one has, doesn't she?"6MAXWELL: You gonna let her talk to you like that?"cARCHER: Perhaps unfortunately, the street-savvy aren't the only ones with influence down here."�There's always people like Craudburry. She pretends to be such an upstanding citizen, but she just plays the streets down here with her wealth."dYou recall the Pokémon we stole from her, yes? That was one she purchased illegally down here."2That's why I had no regrets in targeting her."WNonetheless, her attitude is insufferable. Yet, no one down here stands up to her."1After all, they dare not risk her patronage."xI'm thinking, though, perhaps we might better everyone's lives down here if we, how do you say, teach her a lesson?"4If you're interested, find me around her house."NMAXWELL: I'll tell you what, that broad has way too much power down here."}This is supposed to be place for the strong to survive, not for some rich bitch to order everyone around as she pleases."SBut that's just it. Money casts a powerful curse. And she gets what she wants."$Like stolen Pokémon. You know?"]That's why I tried to take it back from her before. She didn't even play fair to get it."YMost people don't dare stand up to someone like her-- they might lose their squeeze."But us? We're different."AKnow what I mean? I think we oughta teach that one a lesson."<Come find me around her house. We'll settle this score."For, you know, glory."FHey, stranger. Is there something I can do you for-- er, for you?"1I might be able to teach you a thing or two~"JRole Play? Yeah, I get asked for that all the time. One Purple Shard?")Sorry, sugar, I don't work for free."=Thank you kindly. Come again... if you know what I mean~"3Oh, how sweet of you! Three Blue Shards, yeah?"@Electroweb, a shocking choice! Three Green Shards for that~"�Sky Attack? I mean, I know some people feel a high afterwards, but... How about you give me two Red Shards and we call it square." See you around, sweetheart."+Lickitung waits anxiously in the cage."KTRADER: You want Lickitung? I'll give it to you for seven Blue Shards."You gonna take it?"!Gracious. Thing's all yours."DOh, man. I like what I'm seein'. You? You look like fresh meat."7Ugh, I was the one who got chewed up and spit out."7Lesson learned, don't judge the book by its cover."Buy somethin'!".This stuff is worth tons, I'm tellin' ya!"@RAZZY: Hey! What's up! You gettin' hype on the "level-ups"?"Huh, why not?"-Ohhh, you came here looking for someone."2You'll totally find her! You can do anything!"Actually, waitasecond..."UI didn't see a girl, but there was this weird guy wanderin' around a moment ago."7I think he was going up towards the watering hole."&Y'wanna see if you can catch him?"7RAZZY: Aqua Gang can accomplish anything together!"9RAZZY: Together, we can fix this city-- or break it!":RAZZY: So Archer wants us to split up and get jobs..."Okay! I can dig it!"hI've never worked before, and I couldn't begin to guess how to write a resume, but I'll do my best!"*But what kind of place should I work?"CMmm, I wanna work somewhere that's really upbeat and exciting!"*And it should have lots of good food!"Also, I hope it's nearby!"_I still live with my parents, and it's not like they'd let me go out of the city for work.";Plus, if it's a short walk, that's even easier for me!"5Wait, does something that convenient even exist?"7ARCHER: We hadn't seen you around in a while, \PN."5I was beginning to worry something had happened."TAlthough, even if you're here now, there's probably still a lot that's gone on."-Everything's changed, except 7th Street."SBut that just goes to show you this place wasn't as safe as we thought it was."PThe Aqua Gang has kept busy too, but not with our usual method of business."UFrom the beginning, this operation was just an underhanded way to fix this city."WWhen this city started fixing itself, of course I had the other guys get involved."[Then, somewhere between purses and picks, and mortar and bricks, I realized something."Even if we fix this city,"Nothing will fix us."We're a crime rate."jWe're a pattern of habits that pull each other into backwards lifestyles with shallow justifications."+I've decided to disband the Aqua Gang."0Unfortunately, I know it's not that simple."�Studies show that recidivism among gang members is particularly high unless they have adequate alternative social and economic structures."cIn other words, nothing's going to change unless these guys have somewhere else to go instead."(For instance, if they got new jobs."@That could cover both halves of their needs fairly cleanly."@I've already talked about all of this with them, of course."2Predictably, they're not taking it seriously."ZI'll continue to try and get through to them. In the meantime, I have a task for you."�They don't really have the motivation for normal work, but if you could find something that would interest each of them, that might change."�What I want you to do is talk to everyone, figure out what kind of place they might want to work, and bring them an application from that place."9It's not like they'll ask for an application though."LYou'll probably have to be direct about it. Use it from your inventory."You understand, right?"ECome talk to me once you've got everyone else set on their path."�ARCHER: What I want you to do is talk to everyone, figure out what kind of place they might want to work, and bring them an application from that place."=ARCHER: So you were able to find something for everyone?"That's a relief."(Then I guess I'm the only one left."FIt's true that I could just as well go out and search for myself,"YBut perhaps you've found something in your search for the others that might suit me?"BMy strengths lie in team coordination, research and analysis."HThese are fairly marketable skills, so I hope something matches up."+Makuhita stares blankly from the cage."KTRADER: You want Makuhita? I'll give it to you for three Green Shards."Locked."eDude... The Butterfree are soooo like lackadaisical. They totally just morphed into that beam..."$Aha, yah, wha? What's going on?"Duuuuuuude..."???: Hm."!MAXWELL: \PN! There you are!")We've been looking all over for you!"7Feels like it's been ages. You've been doing good?"<We've been doing more good than you would even believe."Racking up that glory!"�But no, I'm serious! Some of the guys were like, boohoo and whatever about pitching in with the city restoration, but we got a lot done!"UI think it's eye-opening, to be able to look at something, point to it, and say,"That, right there."I did that.""That was a difference I made.",It's what we've been chasing all along."It's a legacy, you know?"'That's why I've decided something."$I'm breaking up the Magma Gang."I don't have any regrets."7For how the city was before, it was our best play."FBut with how things are going now, it'd just be weighing us down.">We have a chance to rebuild this city from the ground up!"MIt's not just the stones we lay the foundation for, but the spirits too!"OBut if they stay cooped up in places like these, they'll never learn that."=7th Street is the only place that hasn't changed at all."Not one bit!"Isn't that weird?""Something feels off about it."7That's how I know the other path is the right one!"hIn order to get the other guys to understand how to shape a future we can hold dear, what do we do?"VI think a lot of them don't have the confidence or skills for that kind of thing."JThat's why it'd be best to start with a small commitment, like a job."