s! Who wants another?!"QLooks like you do NOT have the goods! Swing and a miss, but try again later!".Selling Ability Capsules! Who wants 'em!?"'You a new face around here? Scram!"(Uh, aite. Go in peace, or whatever."?Mate, 'm not here looking for trouble. Leave me be, aight?"8My friend! Why don't you see what I can do for you?"(Hey, ain't it my favorite customer!"@You recognize your friend in the Pokémon trading business?"iThings struck a sour note after you swept my last stock and I got the fuzz on my tail for some time."6But you know how I roll. They can't keep me down!"WAnd a guy's gotta pull Shards somehow, so here I am, now in the teachin' business."$Nothin' wrong with that, right?"1So, why don't you see what I can do for you?"4I can teach your crew some of this kinda stuff."NKnock Off? With a price of only 8 Red Shards, it's practically a rip off!"DHey, you may be my favorite customer, but this isn't a charity!"1You gotta have the Shards to learn the arts!"Always a pleasure!"EFor just 7 Purple Shards, this Iron Head is practically a Steel!"DGiga Drain brings the pain! For 6 Green Shards, it's your gain!"JThis may be Liquidation, but there ain't no sale, kid! 6 Blue Shards!"I'll be seeing you around!"@Dude. You new around here? I don't think I seen you before."6LOL, I'm just messin' with you man. How are you?!"JIt's been a while! Man, remember last time we dropped Candy together?"0...Wait, you mean you really don't know me?".Shit dude, you're not with them, are you?"<I don't trust you. I never seen you around here before.":You're obviously a cop in disguise! Get away from me!"%Abra sits patiently in the cage."HTRADER: You want Abra? I'll give it to you for eight Purple Shards."-Still nothing? Doesn't anywhere have it?">Oh, sorry. You can go ahead; I'm not in line or anything."3Even a place like this won't sell what I need."�My husband is seriously ill. I've been looking all over for anything that might cure him, and I heard a rumour about a certain herb, but I can't find it anywhere."aNot that I'm surprised. It's rare to find someone willing to cut off... Oh, well, nevermind."LThat plant you have... That wouldn't happen to be Oddishweed, would it?"Really?"YI almost hate to ask, but would you be willing to give me that? It's for my husband."$\PN handed over the Oddishweed."*This really is it! Thank you so much!"CI was beginning to lose hope I would ever be able to find any."bOh, I wish I could repay you somehow... Oh, actually, I suppose you must be a Trainer, right?"VI've been breeding some Pokémon lately, and I have an extra egg. Do you want it?"\PN got the egg!"2Take care of that, okay? And thank you again!"HWell, I suppose that's your right... But where else will I find it?">Oh, sorry. You can go ahead, I'm not in line or anything."�My husband is seriously ill... I've been looking all over for anything that might cure him, and I heard a rumour about a certain herb, but I can't find it anywhere..."`Not that I'm surprised. It's rare to find someone willing to cut off-- Oh, well, nevermind."3Anyway... I suppose I'll check again tomorrow."DEFACTO: Well met, \PN."1Do tell, how do you find business down here?"~Personally, I manage to make a pretty penny, but it can be a veritable struggle to reason with some of these lesser merchants."pSee, the economy down here-- as with any underworld market-- works on a separate axis of supply and demand."KOne singular substance reigns supreme here: "Rare Candy". Heard of it?"�Well, perhaps it is best that someone like you never does. For many of these fellows, however, they are already too addicted to the "level up"."8Incidentally, do you know how "Rare Candy" is made?"�By distilling the synthetic compounds of other items-- specifically Crystal Shards and Heart Scales-- one is left with a highly reactive substance."eCombined with the traditional medicinal Pokémon Rare Candy, a violent psychoactive is produced."gBut, as such, it is these ingredients which are in high demand down here: Shards and Heart Scales."XThus, it is extremely beneficial for those able to gather these resources to do so."This is where I come in!"]I have a brand new product that can help the crafty geologist maximize their efficiency."1Blast Powder is a unique reactive substance."�When placed on certain kinds of damaged rock-- the glowing sediment I'm sure you've seen-- it will allow previously harvested spots to become lucrative."3In short, it allows you to mine a stone twice.""That established... Buy some!"8DEFACTO: You return! Come to buy more Blast Powder?"VBREAK: Oh, \PN! Do stay a moment, I have an amazing discovery to regale you with!"WAlthough this is 7th Street, some find it more like a 7th Heaven. Do you know why?"COh, I shall tell you. It's because they're out of their minds!"Literally~"8Do tell, do tell, have you ever tried "Rare Candy"?"FOh, I suspect you haven't-- it's not what you feed your Pokémon."/This is a very special kind of "level up"."6But I will tell you the ingredients of the thing!"SUGAR!"SPICE!"And EVERYTHING NICE!"Just kidding."�Actually it's the benzoylmethylecgonine dust and crystal-isomerized piperonyl acetone embedded in Heart Scales and crystal Shards."lThen you stick that in a normal Rare Candy and you'll be partyin' it up, down, sideways AND diagonally."HAnyway, it turns out Heart Scales and Shards are useful to collect."3Not always easy though! They play hard to get."*By hiding in hard things, like rocks."0Sure, you can mine some out, but then what?"xI'll tell you what! Then you take some Blast Powder and blow up the base of the rock so you can mine even MORE out!"LThen you sell them and become king of the world! Or queen. Or whatever.";Anyway yes, Blast Powder! Mine things twice! Buy some!"ABREAK: Blast Powder! More fun than exploding chocolate cake!"Merry mining~!""DEFACTO: You're back at last!";Might I interest you in a fresh stock of Blast Powder?"�Oh, please refrain from invoking any of that platitudinous job-seeking discourse that the boss has been so intent on spouting off."cAs his analytical holiness refuses to acknowledge, I am already gainfully employed right here."'As such, why not indulge yourself?"gDEFACTO: Admittedly, it might have been a boon to be in a slightly more intellectual line of work."�Knowledge is the seat of personal growth, but aside from which downcast countenaces are the most likely customers, there's little to be learned here."YBut that anything like that would exist in this city is a far cry. I'm content here."9BREAK: \PN! My old friend and most valued customer~!"FListen! We've got a problemo in the gang and his name is Maxwell."QBut the way he's talking about breaking us up, we oughta call him Maxunwell!";Ohoh, don't look at me like that. It's spine-tingling."pMore seriously, I can't think of a job better suited to my talents than synthesizing benzoylmethylecgonine."0Most people can't even pronounce that word."It's a gift."�I suppose I am familiar with a variety of chemical, herbal and questionably legal substances that might be handy to those with bizarre interests..."BBut really, no one these days likes to think outside the box.",So we might as well just blow stuff up!"fRemember, if it doesn't seem like a good idea, that just means you're not using enough sparklers."A secret switch!"Press it?"Who wouldn't?"Better not..."MI don't know why my boyfriend insists on selling down here all the time."!All these men are so creepy."+Roggenrola waits morosely in the cage."KTRADER: You want Roggenrola? I'll give it to you for three Red Shards."#Excuse me, very sorry, pardon!"(...\PN's "Rare Candy" went missing!"MHello! Care to introduce your Pokémon to one of our special techniques?"What suits your fancy?"4Water Pulse is gonna run you three Blue Shards.""Come back when you've got it."Perfect."4Last Resort is gonna run you two Purple Shards."4Super Fang is gonna run you three Green Shards."2Shock Wave is gonna run you three Red Shards."Any time, kid.",Bro, you got any "Rare Candy" to spare?"'Heh... 'Spare Candy'. That's good.""Hey, you got a problem, bud?!"8You think I steal from you? I ain't steal from you!"3If you gotta problem, let's go! You wanna go?!"Fuck, dude.">What the hell, dude. You can have your shit back, christ.":Fuck me, you looked like an easy pick, too... Dammit."#Stow it, I'll leave you alone.".Ditto swivels back and forth in the cage."HTRADER: You want Ditto? I'll give it to you for eight Green Shards."--POKÉMON PSYCHOLOGY--"	Hey."I remember you."?You were the one who saved me when I was trapped in Beryl."0Well, what am I doing in a place like this?"BDon't worry, I'm still with the police. I'm here on business."LYou're that Trainer who's been taking down Team Meteor and such, right?"CNice work. I think I can trust you, so I'll tell you a secret."(I'm actually with the police force."BThe truth is, we've known about this place for quite a while."hThere was some debate on if we should step in during the city restoration, and that may yet happen."WBut for the time being, the chief's orders are just to monitor and leave it alone.",I can sort of guess what he's thinking."gIf the people here think the police don't know about this place, they'll keep their business here."jThis way we can keep watching them, collect evidence, and be able to nail them when it really counts."/If we were to pull a bust here, then what?"{After a while they'd find some other cranny we don't know about to do their dirty work in, and we'll lose control that way.""So, you can leave this to us."8We'll make sure this place doesn't fester too much."1Take care. Reborn's got a lot riding on you."Welcome to my little shop!"1All these Pokémon are straight up for sale,"1Provided you got the Shards for 'em, anyway."4I got a strict confidentiality what-not policy:"EI ain't tell where I get 'em, and I ain't tell where I sell 'em."JThat means you can be sure any deals we strike are completely secure." Look around, why don't you!"%Looks like I'm sold out for now."<I'll be sure and get a new stock in one way or another."?You Aqua punks still struttin' around like you're so cool?"#Hmph. Not like it matters now."|Please, your blank stare is piercing into my soul. I cannot possibly exist under the pressure of your black-pixel eyes."UHello! Are you prepared to be amazed by the amazing moves of the Move Magician?!"nSplendid! Just say the word and Paras-to Change-o! Your Pokémon can learn one of these splendid attacks!"`Tricks! My specialty. For two purple shards, I'll show you how you confound your opponents!"ABut don't you have Shards? I need enough to pay back Agate--"gI mean... If I don't have Shards, I won't have enough mana to teach your Pokémon! Yes, that's it!"MAbra! Kadbra! And Alomomola! Your Pokémon is now one move more amazing!"fAh yes, I can see it clearly now! Your Pokémon will learn Defog for the price of two Red Shards!"{Laser Focus, is it? It won't even take an ounce of focus for me to pass that on! Just give me one Blue Shard and it's done!"iThe classic switcharooni! For one Green Shard, you too will make skills move in the blink of an eye!"7Dude, you wanna give me some cash? I need a fix..."lSome people was worried that the fuzz would bust this place up if it was found during the construction."Hah! We show 'em."*Incompetent police don't have a clue!"F7th Street is the one place that won't change! This is OUR world!"JEven in its death-- I will show you the true POWER of the Magma Gang!"You are strong indeed."6Hoo-hah. I bow to a strength greater than my own."'Vanillite waits sadly in the cage."MTRADER: You want Vanillite? I'll give it to you for three Purple Shards."1Headbutt is gonna run you three Blue Shards."1Bounce is gonna run you three Purple Shards."2Heal Bell is gonna run you four Green Shards."0Bug Bite is gonna run you three Red Shards."*ARC: Hey. \PN, right? Come over here.".ARC: You remember me? From the Nightclub."gLook, I've been keeping my eye on this place for a while. There's something fishy about it, yanno."oAnd I've seen you buy from this guy a few times, yeah? But you don't seem like his typical customer to me."???: Hey, you. Come here."{Who are you? I've been keeping my eye on this place for a while, but you don't seem like this guy's typical customer to me."\PN, huh?"aWell, I'm Arclight- DJ Arclight, to be specific. I run the Nightclub up in the Obsidia Ward."&You can just call me Arc. Anyway."YI'm pretty sure that these Pokémon he's selling are stolen, and I ain't about that."_Most of his customers don't care a thing about Pokémon. They usually end up abusing them."�If these Pokémon really are stolen, it's probably hopeless to find their original owners, but, I figure at least we can get them to a good place."3And I'm thinkin' you might be that good place."�So I'll tell you what, \PN, I'm gonna leave it to you to buy up the rest of these guys. He won't sell to me; I've raised hell here in the past."MAnd once we've cleaned his stock, then I'll bust in and clean his clock."CMake sure this guy gets shut down for good. Sound like a plan?"I'm countin' on you."ARC: Yo. \PN."�If these Pokémon really are stolen, it might not be practical to find their original owners, but, I figure at least we can get them to a good place."&Huh, you already did it? Not bad." Looks like you did it, huh?"wI owe you one, for sure. I can rest a bit easier knowing that those Pokémon will be taken care of no matter what."FIt might not be a bad idea to hang onto them just in case though."�As for that guy... I won't do anything out in the open. But let me put it this way-- Next time you're around here, don't expect to see him again."1Anyway, here's a little 'thank you' from me." Do what you will with that."<If you ever get into the Nightclub, hit me up for sure!"NIHIL: Sup."5I see you took your time in making it down here."3This has been our squeeze for quite some time.".Surprised I didn't see you 'round before."$Hm, you're looking for someone?"