rceus' Call"\nRead?";"Our Father, fallen from heaven,\nHonored be thy name,"-Your kingdom, born,\nThis world, forlorn":The New World shall become thy heaven." -- Arceus 7-1"%"Charge of the Faithful"\n Read?"8So be it the duty of all, human and Pokémon alike:"RBestow light upon thy brethren; give sight to the blind and life to the lost."EArceus shall grant thee favour in the New World." -- Arceus 12-3""Light's End"\n Read?")"So kind was light to show us mercy,"*That in its shade we festered heresy."*Twixt three stones, each shaded void,"-Six pillars shone, their truth deployed:"$Emerald, Crimson, Violet, Gold,""Azure and Ivory seal as told."/Take heed of its prison, o ye foolish men,"1For the blackest beast lies at light's end.""'The notebook has no title. \nRead?"5Place faith in the Lord, and so shall he in you."=Place animosity upon the Lord, and so shall he upon you."hThis lesson is not an easy one to learn. Some will never fully grasp it. Many will only pretend to."QToday, I would like to share with you the story of how I came to learn this."?I was born to the purpose of Arceus, but I was born blind."}Growing up as a boy with no sight in a world like this is no easy task, but of course, I learned to take care of myself."@For some time, that was the only thing I could be proud of."�My family was an old one, back from the days when Reborn City was no more than a village around a crater, both of which are since lost underground."^When first Arceus' birthplace crashed upon our world, one family set about enshrining it."WThey would protect it from the world, so that its purity might remain ever intact."#This was their life's calling." And this was not my family."\Mine came years later, and, finding light in their purpose, swore to serve that family."ESo it came to be that each generation of my house served theirs."aUntil it came to me, a defective blind child, who would do more harm than good as a servant."OThe man to whom I should have been sworn was born some ten years after me."We know him as Solaris."hHe was a raucous youth, never quite satisfied with his life's charge of protecting an old monument."zAs I understand, for most of his life he resented this purpose, lashing out, as many of the young do, against Arceus."%I could understand his feelings."QWhy, I asked myself, if Arceus is so great, should he have made me this way?"7Why did I have to suffer? Why did I have to serve?"FAs it turned out, Solaris would be the one to show me the answer."�A failed vassal, I dared not approach him, and though our fathers were close, mine never allowed me to see the young master as I was growing up."NIt was not until I was well into a miserable adulthood that we first met."#Solaris knew of me, of course."�He knew my family was due by lineage to serve his, and he had heard of the blind man, whom others had deemed unfit for his presence."1And, as he did with all things, he rebelled."He offered his hand to me.")I took it with an oath of servitude."4This was not a chance I should have been given."OSo, I pushed myself as hard as I could to try and have value to my master."/But both of us were lordless, lawless men."YHe had no purpose to serve but fighting his own, and we found common ground therein."4Nevertheless, Arceus would reach us eventually."_For many years, Solaris questioned, 'Just what does the meteor need to be protected from?'"9It was already locked up with the four crystal keys."7And who would want to defile some old rock anyway?"zThis was a lesson he learned the hard way, when his parents were both killed by an assailant seeking those very keys."QThe young master was too late to save them, but just in time to avenge them."sSo he bludgeoned the man who had claimed the keys until his arms were too battered to hold on to them anymore,"7And until his lips were too loose to keep secrets."*Why?!', Solaris cried, over and over."The assailant would tell him rumours he had never believed, of a great power locked within the meteor, lying dormant for years."PWhether it was true or not, the thief believed it, and so he grasped at it."&Why?!', Solaris continued to cry."�And so he said, on and on until daybreak, thrashing against the culprit's body for long after there was any soul still there to know it."7He was no longer asking anyone other than himself."1Why had he refused to listen to his parents?"1Why had he not seen the danger they were in?" Why could he not save them?"CAnd believing that he had led to the death of his own parents,"FFor the first time, he strode forward to meet his life's purpose."/The Lord will punish those who lack faith."6This is what is to be learned from Solaris' tale."3My own awakening came a number of years later."TWhen my master walked the path of the Lord, so naturally did I have to as well."TI would follow my friend, but in regards to faith, my service was half-hearted."ASolaris recognized this, and one day confronted me about it."After some discussion, he offered the Emerald Key he should have himself vanguarded with his life, in return for my faith."PHe wished for me not just to serve him, but to personally share his burden."_I accepted this, and resolved to place every ounce of my trust in the Lord, and my friend."�When I awoke the next morning, the key still clutched tightly against my chest, I was assaulted by a phenomenon I had never experienced before."}Lights, dazzling colors, shapes so blurred I could scarcely recognize the forms I was so used to navigating around otherwise."Sight."^There are no words to describe the feeling of seeing my master's face for the first time."#Or that of seeing my own face."`That of finally being able to really understand what words like 'golden' and 'light' meant."fBefore, they were just dreams, but I knew that the Lord-- and my trust in him-- had made it real."0The Lord will reward those with true faith."'It has been many years since then."gI am constantly assaulted with sorrow and worry for the sake of my daughter, and for his son both."HI do not wish them to receive any such punishment as my friend did."JI wish them both all the blessings of the Lord they have turned from.""I fear, too, for each of you."9Though less so, than for each of the heretics above."UThe city's miserable state is no doubt a result of its divergence from the Lord."Therefore, I implore you,"Please, trust in Arceus."-Please, guide others to trust in Arceus.";Under the Lord's light, may we all see bright futures."Thank you.""+\PN obtained Field Effect Read-Out 29!"&Info on Holy Field now available!"#LUNA: Well met once more, \PN.":I, as well, had come to see what the matter was here."pLoath as I am to admit due to long-tarnished memories, this place is one I'm yet beholden to in other ways."MI should not like to see it fall to total ruin; silence is quite enough."/And yet, I find this door is closed to me."DWhatever wonders remain beyond it, they are not mine to access."This is quite new to me."/But here you are, an answer to a question."mUnfiltering and unfaltering, may you find you fill your role as effectively as always you thus far have."aLUNA: I suspect we'll both soon see just for what reasons I am unable to join you this time."LUNA: Well, then.";It would appear the matter has decided itself settled."vAnd be it a twist of the mind, or a twist of time, I believe I have some inkling of what transpired beyond there."8A memory came to me not too long after you entered."BI find myself unsure as to whether or not it was mine before."TAKA: Oh, \PN?"=I heard a noise coming from here, but if it's just you--"
