ad-Out 23!" Info on Cave now available!["2\PN obtient la Notice d'Effets de Terrain 23!":Les infos sur la Caverne sont maintenant disponibles!;["+\PN obtained Field Effect Read-Out 23!" Info on Cave now available!Iu;␀�![[G"XWelcome to Critical Capture! Specialty balls to make sure you get that third shake!" Good luck, and have a ball!"RI'm disappointed they don't have Dusk and Level Balls. I guess they sold out?"=Hum. The craftsmanship on these balls is somewhat cheap."�Sorry to nitpick; I used to be a ball designer myself, so it irks me to see these factory made-in-Kalos balls not being quite up to snuff."-Hmm? You say you found a corrupted ball?"2Well, what'd I tell you? It's not surprising."�Actually, it can happen for a few reasons. A defect is one option, but if a ball is damaged and not maintained, it can cause data loss."Here, let me see it?"#Mmm. Right, so see this crack?"RIt was probably dropped from a long way up or something. That doesn't matter."�The problem is, if some debris gets through the exterior into the circuits, then it can distort the electric transmission, and then-- well, this happens."`It might not be impossible to fix, but you're honestly better off just buying another ball."^DESIGNER: You're determined to fix this ball? It probably won't be usable no matter what."HThere is the chance that a Pokémon was inside at one point, but..."�Well, when inside Poké Balls, lifeforce data of Pokémon is converted to a digital format. Meaning the Pokémon itself can corrupt as well."FWhatever this originally was before, it's probably Missingno now."EMissingno can't be caught or tamed, so there's no point to that."+Are you sure you still want to fix it?"DESIGNER: I see."eI have an old diagnostic kit with me, let me see if I can detect any lingering data in the ball."..."......"........."1Mm... The data corruption is already at 96%."?This is probably useless, but let's see what we can use..."Ah, Magnet Powder."wThat will be small enough to 