e, did you?"!I am not Corin-Rouge at all!"'Or was it someone else you chased?":The real Corin-Rouge would never be caught so easily!"cHowever! If you are able to defeat me, I'll give you a hint as to where the real one might be!"*Interesting, very interesting! Bravo!"Ah, so that's it, is it?"TFine! As promised, I'll give you a hint for where to find the true Corin-Rouge!".Find him in the place where mists settle!"#That's all you'll get from me!"NAs promised, I'll give you a hint for where to find the true Corin-Rouge!"(...Aha, you're still staring at me."You know, don't you?"&CORIN-ROUGE: What a pity, though."HI have dreamt of our reunion much since I first laid eyes upon you."And how could I not?"LEven so, never once did I dream that my farewell would come so quickly."&I see the confusion in your eyes."But do not weep, darling.">Even when I am gone, my thoughts will always be with you."So,"?Remember me kindly, as I shall you, until my final breath."$You've worked so hard, and now?"3It's all for nothing, because you're too late."BI've bought just enough time for my train to finally come in."FLORINIA: So, I am..."Confused."JULIA: Okay, we can help!"!What are you confused about?"}FLORINIA: ...So I asked if you might have any ideas to help me get out, meet people, and stay in touch with my feelings."JULIA: Mhm!"YFLORINIA: And so, you said you were going to find an environmental activism group..."BJULIA: Because it seems like the type of thing you'd be into!"1FLORINIA: ...Because I train Grass Types...?""JULIA: And also you're smart!"&Environmental science is a thing!"EFLORINIA: ...But this is an activism group; not a science group."JULIA: Close enough!"LFLORINIA: ...So you got us in contact with Sandy, who had us meet here."SANDY: Oh, that's me!"Yes, I did do that!"FLORINIA: ..."$Where is the rest of the group?"2JULIA: You know, I hadn't thought about that!"Let's ask the expert--"Sandy, what do you think?",SANDY: Well, Julia, I'm glad you asked!"See, the thing is,"*I think I got the meeting time wrong?")I think it was actually an hour ago."But that's okay!"6Because it's ALWAYS time to save the environment.""JULIA: And there you have it!"(SANDY: No use sweating the details!"DI mean, psh, even the environment gets things wrong sometimes--"It's no big deal."�FLORINIA: On the contrary, when the environment gets things wrong it tends to have severe implications for global economic and agricultural conditions..."SANDY: Ooh, that's good!"-I'll write that down for our next rally!"<JULIA: See, you're environmentally science-ing already!"0FLORINIA: I think that's just common sense?"1JULIA: But you know what's not common sense?"Feeeeeeeeeeeeelings!"DThis was supposed to be an expedition of your emotions, right?!"<So maybe the real climate we should be concerned about,"Is your emotional climate!"RSANDY: No, we should definitely be deeply concerned about the actual climate."JULIA: That too!!!"(FLORINIA: ...I'm grateful, I think."YEven if it was a pointless outing with a missed group, chosen for arbitrary reasons,"3I'm glad that I could be here with all of you."...Oh, I--"I'm... crying?"
Ah..."Mosswater Market"You Snooze, You Moves-"6The chillest move tutoring service on the block.""Duuuude, what's up?"?Heyy, don't take it personally, I just call everyone dude.",You here for some of our special moves?")Tell you what, dude, they're a trip."%Yo, you wanna try some of these?"VHeyyy, dankest move in the game. Or rankest. Either way it's 6 Blue Shards, dude."BYooo, dude, you ain't got the price we said. That ain't cool."6Huh? Oh, yeah, I gotta give it the move too, huh."$No problem. There you go, dude."LWoahhh, intense, aren't you? But Dragon Pulse is uhh, six Green Shards."WGotta wonder what kinda grass this thing'd make... Oh, but it's six Purple Shards."?That's seven Red Shards, but hey, no harm, no foul, right?"Sweet, dude."Greetings, Trainer."eI can tell you're well-traveled. I have special moves I can teach to your Pokémon, for a price."3Do you have any Pokémon that can learn these?"_Powerful, but difficult to use well, like many things in life. It costs three Blue Shards."?Excuse me, but I don't think you can pay the price for it.".Always a pleasure to pass on what I know."9Destructive, but effective. It costs 3 Green Shards."bTake care not to get caught in it, Trainer. I'd be devestated. But the price is 3 Red Shards."IExtreme power comes at an extreme price. Namely, nine Purple Shards."+I will be waiting for your next visit."wThis place already offers a lot I couldn't find elsewhere, but I hear there are still some vendors getting set up."ELet's check back in the future to see what else they get for us!"{Ehh? I wanted to get moves to show off at school, but what are these shard-things and where is anyone supposed to get them?";They can't really expect us to start mining, can they?"Well, that's not good."\I tried to do a technical analysis of this building to learn something about it, but..."+I think it printed out the wrong data."
