se basic principles!""And that's the whole problem!"XAfter all the build up and all the expectations and hopes that were pinned on me..."0I still will never be able to be like Kiki!"STUDENT: ..."PIERCE: ..."GPIERCE: I shouldn't need to be reminded of these basic principles!"'VICTORIA: In the way only I can...">Managing the academy alone was always an impossible task,"But Reborn City as well?"LThere's no possible way I can be expected to lead both of them at once!"�KIKI: It is the nature of those precious few among us who truly care to pick up more responsibilities than we are able to uphold."�There is much to be said there, for personal boundaries, for managing the weight of these burdens, and prioritizing them in whichever way will saddle us with the fewest regrets."6But those are not concerns of the present moment."LFor now, it is enough to simply acknowledge that these struggles exist."KThey are there now, and for better or worse, they will be there later."|But their presence does not have to obstruct you from enjoying the benefits of a peaceful mental state in the meantime."BLACKBELT: ..."1VICTORIA: Hey, what were you saying before?!"*You have to lead Reborn and Apophyll?"Who even are you?"BLACKBELT: ......"-VICTORIA: Excuse me? I'm talking to you!"BLACKBELT: ........."VICTORIA: Tch, fine!"Priorities are all well and good, but we still only have twenty-four hours a day and a finite number of days in our lives!"hEven Kiki, for all her focus on wellness, couldn't outlast her expiration in any way that mattered!"QKIKI: The physical clock ticks at the same speed for everyone; this is true."3And we none of us can prevent our varied ends."FBut your mind does not subscribe to the speed of the second hand."XThe clock is a tool measuring the rotation of planets; not the passing of thoughts."|Our mental states can do much to affect the rate at which our time passes, both in the moment and in our longer term health."�By calming oneself and putting the mind int