Oh..."(I never thought I'd make it here...",I guess I'm not so worthless after all."�Listen up! The most important thing isn't power, it isn't courage, and it isn't even having friends! The only thing that matters is that you can rely on ME."&An old area map is posted here..."3...But it doesn't seem to be accurate anymore.Iu;␀PA[[�"Locked."@TAKA: When you're ready, you should give Celebi that water."?But remember to stock up on items and stuff, just in case."TTAKA: \PN? I didn't expect to see you again. I just figured you'd leave, and..."6I mean, go stand at the mountain's peak, I guess?"*Isn't that what Champions usually do?"iIt's... good to see you again, though. I've not really spoken to anyone since... y'know, everything."&I was just up here... reflecting."VDid you know there used to be a temple to Arceus here before they built a League?"%Father mentioned it a few times."BHis father ran it, so he spent a lot of time here as a kid..."8It was already gone by the time I was born, though."*And he only mentioned it a few times."0He didn't like talking about his parents..."They must've been intense.",Probably best I never got to meet them."I doubt Fath--"F... I doubt Solaris would even want them to see how I turned out."QTAKA: Wait a minute, that Pokémon over there, the one just staring at us...")That's Celebi, a Legendary Pokémon!"2It looks pretty rough though, like it's sick?"+We need to help it; we can't let it..."@Too many bad things have happened on this mountain already."But why did it come here?"UI know a bit about Legendary Pokémon, but only what I read in Father's books..."lApparently Grandfather was an expert on medicine and Legendary Pokémon, and we kept some of his books."TAKA: ...Wait."+Celebi can travel through time, right?"8It's in the right place, just a few decades late..."(Uh, here, maybe try giving it this?"aMaybe this will give it just enough energy to travel through back to where it needs to be..."=Oh but, maybe make sure you stock up on items and stuff?"cIt's probably in a hurry to get to the past, I doubt it'll wait after you give it the water..."2But knowing your luck it'll probably be fine!"mA quick jaunt into the past with no complications, and you befriend a Legendary Pokémon in the process."NKnowing my luck, I'd probably just get eaten by a Tyrantrum or something."7ELIAS: Water should temporarily rejuvenate Celebi."QPerhaps too much so-- be prepared to leave as soon as you give it the water.".ELIAS: Prosperitas, Pax Pacis, Obsequium."OA gleaming gate to the New World appears before me, and out steps my Lord."LThe miracle of my sight was more than enough, but you grace me further,"4Performing another miracle before my very eyes."VWhile I'm sure you already knew this, you have caught me at a time of reflection."RToday, I am not here as a member of the Elite Four, but instead as a pilgrim."IBefore there was a Pokémon League here, there was instead a temple.")I spent much time there in my youth."?Even if the temple is gone, this place feels... important."Sacred, even."ELIAS: Errare humanum est."#My deepest apologies, my Lord."\I got so caught up in my reminiscence that I did not see the reason you have come here."'Celebi, the Time Travel Pokémon--"I have read much about it."HIt does not look as lustrous as the diagrams would suggest, though."!ELIAS: Ah, of course, I see."$This is a test of my knowledge."*I shall inspect the Pokémon at once." ELIAS: You poor creature...";It must have been very strenuous to make it even here."9ELIAS: I'm sorry. This is beyond my ability to heal."�The Relic Stone would surely be able to help in this matter, however, last I heard, you had traveled to the New World to locate it?"?But you are here with Celebi, and no Relic Stone in sight."[ELIAS: I understand, my Lord; you wish for me to solve this problem without its power.".Allow me a moment to consider my options."*I apologize profusely for this delay."QELIAS: Of course, this is a brilliant test you have devised for me, my Lord!"^You arrived here when I was reflecting on the old temple, with a Pokémon in need of aid."JSpecifically, a Pokémon that can travel through time, but not space."oI lack the knowledge to heal Celebi without the Relic Stone, but Father Taube, the keeper of the temple..."/Nobody knew more about Legendary Pokémon."*My Lord, please accept this offering."ELIAS: Aqua Pura.";Legendary it may be, but Celebi is still a Grass Type."ESome water should give it enough energy for a trip through time."TI'm sure you already are aware, but-- be prepared before you give it the water."gI doubt an injured Pokémon will waste any time trying to get to where it thinks it can be healed."TThere appears to be something nearby that the sickly Pokémon wants you to see."+Do you want to give Celebi more water?"I\PN gently poured a second bottle of water over the sickly Pokémon.":Celebi still looks weak, but gets a glint in its eye.",Your surroundings start to fade away..."LCelebi looks like it will wait until you're ready to give it the water."�If only a former terrorist had given you a bottle of water like five seconds ago to use in this exact situation but, alas, you have no water."TAKA: Hey, \PN?"-You just spaced out for a second, there.">I mean, that's a mood. I just had the weirdest deja vu..."DAnyway, just give Celebi that water when you're ready, I guess."-ELIAS: My Lord, is everything all right?"I assume you felt it too?"XI just had the strangest sense of familiarity with these events, for some reason..."oAh, not that you would find yourself affected by being in the presence of a Pokémon with power over time."1You must have been waiting for me to adjust."9I am, as always, humbled by how considerate you are."LI'm sure Celebi will be ready for you as soon as you give it the water."+\PN obtained Field Effect Read-Out 35!"%Info on New World now available!"-HARDY: You're in the nick o' time, mate."/I just wiped to this thing like a dumbass."ABut it's softened up and does