ay with!"and that someone else...":don't say it's \v[571] or something stupid like that!"(obviously it was me the whole time!"	huh?"Obut only a crazy girl would waste time talking to her own toy like this..."oh wait, heeheeheehee...")why trying to fight me is useless???"?because if you beat me, then what's gonna happen to you???" no one to play with, uh oh!"*guess the game's over, gotta go home!"$and no one wants it to be over."7if you really did, you'd just walk away right now."but you won't!"@eyes glazed over, mouth open, "what is she even saying????""Ryou only want the game to end when someone ELSE is responsible for it, right?"<these are just words you decided to sit through, right?"Suntil the next time you actually are prompted to do something for real, right?"fine, if you insist!"1if you really want to end the game so badly!"4we can still play with arceus a whole lot more!"huh??????"LIN: really??????"arceus????"0don't tell me i messed with you too much..."hey..."wake up?"(you're supposed to be a god, right?"Gyou were supposed to make it so we wouldn't be sad anymore, right?">we were supposed to make a world where we could be happy,"Uwhere nobody forgot about us, or scared us, or made us do things we didn't want," you can do that, can't you?"9so why are you making our own toy turn against us???"stop it, okay?"that's NOT fun anymore."Eif we're going to play this game, then you NEED to listen to me."Kwe were supposed to be the only ones who understood each other, RIGHT?"Kotherwise, what was the point of making a world just for ourselves????"8so just LISTEN and BEHAVE and it'll be okay, RIGHT?")you're mine, and you always will be."and i'm yours."Gand we take care of each other like people are SUPPOSED to, RIGHT?"#we'll always have each other--"forever,"right?"LIN: oh."so that's how you felt..."then..."$you're just like me, after all."LIN: hahhh?"that's it???"-you came all this way just to lose here."that is truly, remarkably,"STUPID."ahahhahaha!"@after anna's speech and everything, you just go and lose???"wowowowowowowow""but it just goes to show you,"Aafter all the time anna and i both put in to raise you up..."a useless toy like you..."...isn't needed by anyone.Iu;␀gp[["AMARIA: Oh, it's you!"II heard you eloped with Lin, but you decided to come back after all?"That's amazing."6You're here to help out with this now too, right?"Here, look."/These tablets are just covered in braille."aI was originally going to try and deal with this myself since it's right by my house, but..."CTrying to translate this much text manually is just useless..."EI've been here for a while already and hardly made any progress."4Frankly, I'm about ready to throw in the towel."XI think our best bet is to find someone who's already familiar with braille, but..."~The only person I've heard of who was blind was the old guy in the Elite 4, and no one's heard from him since Lin disappeared."HWe'll probably have to find someone else, but I have no idea who..."VI don't suppose you know anyone else who might be able to translate this, do you?"*For now, I think I'll just head back."HMaybe I'll see if there's something else Tania and I can help with."Bye for now~"AMARIA: Oh, you're back."-Julia told me you had eloped with Tania.".I told her that wasn't a very funny joke."/Here to clean up the mess you left behind?"9I guess you haven't really changed at all, have you?"CAMARIA: Well, I'll just leave this in your ever-capable hands."MI thought I'd go see what the trouble was, being on my doorstep and all,"IBut all that seems to be here are these big tablets full of braille."2As for trying to translate all that manually?"No thanks."QYou'd probably be better off just finding someone who can read it naturally."{The only blind person I've heard of was the old guy in the Elite 4, and no one's heard from him since Lin disappeared."/You'll probably have to find someone else."Good luck~"6Maybe I'll see you around the Nightclub sometime."AMARIA: Or maybe not."!DANIELLE: My, what kept you?"DI've more or less just about finished going over the whole bit."_Fortunately for you, this does translate to our language after all. Isn't that convenient?"YNow, there is the matter of how to go about acting on the information listed here..."|You see, that tablet over there describes how in order to open the way forward, an actor must perform a certain ritual."FAnd this tablet here lists the actions necessary for said ritual."<And while I could simply tell you what's listed here..."�Don't you think it's a bit dehumanizing to go about fetching a disabled person just for the sake of serving as a tool of transliteration?"I suppose you wouldn't."TBut I, for one, am discontent to play a passive, intermediary role in all this."'So, here's what we're going to do."9I trust you are familiar with the game "Simon Says"?"�DANIELLE: You say that, but the last time I translated for someone, they said they knew it and then forgot the entire point of the game."PIf I don't specifically say "Simon Says", you don't do the thing, remember."ABut if you get that, then you get where I'm going with this."TDANIELLE: Truly? Goodness, some folks are even more sheltered than I'd thought."1Fret not. I shall kindly explain it for you."YIn "Simon Says," players are given a list of instructions one at a time by a leader."bIf the instruction is preceded by the phrase "Simon says," then each player is to perform it."MIf it is not preceded by that phrase, players are expected to ignore it."jIf a player fails to do something Simon said, or does do something Simon did not say, then they lose."@Simple enough, isn't it? Even a child could win flawlessly."NSo, we will play this game as I read you the instructions for the ritual."iSurely you, a perfectly-sighted person, can't possibly fail something as rudimentary as this, right?"6Now, talk to me again when you're ready to begin."!DANIELLE: Care to try again?"XOr has this simple set of instructions proven just ever too much for you to handle?"$DANIELLE: Shall we get started?"^After all, I do so love tormenting people with games-- I mean, playing games with people."DANIELLE: Lovely."DNow go stand over there, in that middle area. Then we'll begin."1DANIELLE: No need to be nervous or anything.")I'm only here to judge and mock you."DANIELLE: ...What?""DANIELLE: Messed up, did you?"At least you know it."+From the top, then, when you're ready."BDANIELLE: What, is a little children's game too much for you?"CI know I'm not exactly being nice here-- that would be boring."=But if you realllllly want, I can just solve it for you."DANIELLE: Disappointing."%But it's not as if I won't help."9Stand back then, I'll take care of it in an instant."PDANIELLE: Your commitment to letting me bully you is sincerely appreciated."?But the timing is messed up now, so let's go from the top.".DANIELLE: Oh, so it wasn't all poppycock."Color me surprised."kWell, I don't expect you to thank me, and I have no intention of congratulating you, so run along now."ADANIELLE: Don't worry; I don't intend to disappear just yet."[After all, I've gotten the impression that this won't be the last time you'll need me."FAnd I'm sure you would just hate to miss out on our little games."Kzzzzzztttt--"&The Pokémon fled further inward!"KSmall bumps cover the tablet from side to side in distinct patterns..."-DANIELLE: So there were more, after all."aOf course, I already knew that, but I wouldn't want to rob you of your feeling of discovery." Never say I'm not generous."@Now, step back. I'll read this and tell you when I'm ready."DANIELLE: Another, right?""What would you do without me?"JNow, stand aside and be useless for a moment again while I read this."DANIELLE: And again."7Any more of these and I should start charging you."I won't-- but I could."1So you'd better be nice to me, or something."&Anyway, you know the drill. Move."&DANIELLE: All right, I've got it."Ready when you are."*DANIELLE: No