n't that convenient?"YNow, there is the matter of how to go about acting on the information listed here..."|You see, that tablet over there describes how in order to open the way forward, an actor must perform a certain ritual."FAnd this tablet here lists the actions necessary for said ritual."<And while I could simply tell you what's listed here..."�Don't you think it's a bit dehumanizing to go about fetching a disabled person just for the sake of serving as a tool of transliteration?"I suppose you wouldn't."TBut I, for one, am discontent to play a passive, intermediary role in all this."'So, here's what we're going to do."9I trust you are familiar with the game "Simon Says"?"�DANIELLE: You say that, but the last time I translated for someone, they said they knew it and then forgot the entire point of the game."PIf I don't specifically say "Simon Says", you don't do the thing, remember."ABut if you get that, then you get where I'm going with this."TDANIELLE: Truly? Goodness, some folks are even more sheltered than I'd thought."1Fret not. I shall kindly explain it for you."YIn "Simon Says," players are given a list of instructions one at a time by a leader."bIf the instruction is preceded by the phrase "Simon says," then each player is to perform it."MIf it is not preceded by that phrase, players are expected to ignore it."jIf a player fails to do something Simon said, or does do something Simon did not say, then they lose."@Simple enough, isn't it? Even a child could win flawlessly."NSo, we will play this game as I read you the instructions for the ritual."iSurely you, a perfectly-sighted person, can't possibly fail something as rudimentary as this, right?"6Now, talk to me again when you're ready to begin."!DANIELLE: Care to try again?"XOr has this simple set of instructions proven just ever too much for you to handle?"$DANIELLE: Shall we get started?"^After all, I do so love tormenting people with games-- I mean, playing games with people."DANIELLE: Lovely."DN