verything I can to help."!ELIAS: My apologies again..."?I panicked and just said the first name that came to mind."&Please forgive this lie, my Lord."ELIAS: The Relic Stone..."=Unfortunately, it is similarly inaccessible in our time."RHowever, we possessed no alternative, so I am overjoyed to hear you have one."UI presume this will be most effective if Celebi meditates on its own for a time?"TAUBE: Exactly, yes."I apologize for the wait."9Like you no doubt are, I am quite eager to get home."KBut it is important to see this through; Celebi came here for our aid."+ELIAS: It is no burden to wait for us."yI would be honored to read some of the texts you have here, in case there are some the Order was unable to preserve?"DTAUBE: By all means, you are welcome to read whatever you wish."RAh, and the entrance is just back there, Celebi. I hope you find it peaceful."MTAUBE: However, while you are of course free to look through my texts..."LI must admit, I couldn't help but notice you both have Pokémon on you."�Between my responsibilities with the Order and the changes at home, the only person I can ever find the time to battle is Joseph."&Who, naturally, I'm no match for."\How can a humble priest compete with a man that traveled to Orre to conquer Mt. Battle?"NAnd given we have time to kill... Would one of you two care for a battle?"ELIAS: Joseph... Hazel?"I have heard the name.")Your servant, if I recall correctly?":TAUBE: Ah, I see you've been studying Order doctrine."<Yes, I suppose the traditions dictate he is my servant."pBut, even if he is too proud to admit it, as far as I'm concerned, he's nothing short of my closest friend."Interesting, I see."UTAUBE: I'm sure my newborn and his young Elias will get along just as well, too."0As I said, do either of you wish to battle?"ELIAS: Newborn...?"Ah, congratulations..."QI apologize; I do not quite feel up to battling at this particular moment..."4But Arc is a far better trainer than I, anyway."GHe has bested me, and 