er hygiene is important!"or so the adults say."(they're really out of control, huh?"Yes"NoIu;␀�F[[�"6BENNETT: Our mark has gotten quite cozy up there."@SERRA: I don't think there's any way to reach it, is there?"-BENNETT: Reaching it would be pointless."+It would just run away again anyway...""We need a different approach.">SERRA: Between the three of us, maybe we could corner it."5BENNETT: This place must've been used as a camp."/Look, among the stones-- a stirring spoon."+SERRA: Aren't we still in a New World?"4BENNETT: Considering the ecology, I assume not."dThe generated world must have connected to both Victory Road and this previously isolated cave."�This camp was probably left behind by a hiker sometime ago, suggesting that it's impractical-- rather than impossible-- to get here by foot."JSERRA: Well that's nice, but it doesn't exactly help us with Victini."$BENNETT: No, I believe it does."/This camp has seen a healthy share of use."gAnd between this lush environment and the water below, I suspect there's no shortage of food here."jRather than desperately chasing after Victini, let's do our best to make ourselves worth approaching."1SERRA: You're going to lure it in with food?"1BENNETT: It's the choicest course of action."oIn a worst case scenario, we can all enjoy a nice meal together ourselves and come up with an alternative."SERRA: ...Oh, fine."<If we can find a pot, I'm sure I can whip something up."MYou don't get to be a single mother without learning to improvise a bit."\BENNETT: Our hiker left his spoon behind... With any luck, he'll have left his pot too."LMother, would you mind searching for that, or something equally usable?"#SERRA: That can't be sanitary."SBut if and when I find it, I suppose the lake down there looks clean enough..."HBENNETT: I hear curries are quite popular with Pokémon in Galar..."<\PN, would you mind helping me gather some ingredients?"dConsidering the ecology here, I think most everything we need could be found in this very cave."WI have a rough list for what to look for. Talk to me when you're ready to hear it."�BENNETT: I already had a chance to look around the area a bit, and I think I have a pretty good idea of what's available for us to use."1I believe our main course tonight will be..."'Spiced Apple Galarian-style Curry."BENNETT: How is it going?"eBENNETT: Regarding the ingredients, I can give you a general idea for where they might be found."jFor the apples-- both types-- I can see them both on the lower floor from here. Just above the water."vThe Rage Powder plants are directly across from me as well-- it looks as if those are on the lower level as well."?The Pecha Berry you'll find in the care of a wild Wurmple."�Wurmple frequently collect them, since it just so happens that the specific nutrients within Pecha Berries are perfect for creating beautiful cocoons, and--"7...Er, I suppose you don't care about the details."�Anyway, Wurmple characteristically inhabit a certain type of tree-- and I just so happen to recognize a grove of it on the west side of this level."`The Stick-- which really should just be called a leek-- will be maintained by a Farfetch'd."�I saw one flying about earlier-- but in this case, you'll have better luck searching for items on the ground rather than from wild Farfetch'd."6I suspect it will have been left in a high place."fThe Balm Mushroom will grow somewhere with lower light-- close to the ground, probably in a cave."ZBerry Juice is created naturally by Shuckle, and so you will always find it with one."mShuckle habitually hide under breaking rocks, and I suspect that this is the perfect habitat for them..."WLook for smashable rocks, and you will find a Shuckle-- and thus, the Berry Juice."#That's everything that's left."3Feel free to ask again if you need a reminder."�BENNETT: I mentioned getting the Pecha Berries from Headbutt trees-- but more specifically, it'll be commonly held by the Wurmple living in those trees."kI know most Trainers don't just happen to have a Pokémon with Headbutt on them at all times though..."[If you need, I think I can prompt one of your Pokémon to learn the move here and now."Should we see about it?"BENNETT: Good luck."9BENNETT: From this point, we'll need \v[614] things:"*One Sweet Apple, for the main course.")...And I see you have it. Good work."-One Tart Apple, for substance and depth."(...And you've gotten it. Well done."-One Balm Mushroom, for a second texture." You've got that. Excellent."TOne Pecha Berry, for the signature sweetness. Check the Headbutt trees for one.",You have the Pecha Berry. Im-pecha-ble."...Sorry. Anyway..."-Berry Juice, for sweetness and thinning.")You have the Berry Juice. Wonderful."gA Farfetch'd's Stick. This leek will sauté into a perfect start, and the ends are a good garnish."<I see you have a Stick... Leek. Whatever. I'll take it."tRage Powder. Properly treated, this powder stops having adverse effects and starts being a wonderful spice mix."1And you've got it. Expectably reliable work."...That should be it."qIf you want some hints on where to find everything, feel free to ask. I have a general idea for most things."&BENNETT: You got everything then."#Fantastic work as always, \PN."HSERRA: One pot of questionable cleanliness, ready to go as ordered."=BENNETT: We were fortunate to find everything we needed.",Let's hope our fortune carries forward."2SERRA: I guess I'll get started with cooking."What all did you find?"GBENNETT: Everything we need for Galarian-style Spiced Apple Curry."SERRA: Curry! In a cave!"4Shall I prepare the other four courses as well?"BENNETT: ...No,"4In fact, why don't you leave the cooking to me?":SERRA: Oh, please. What would you know about cooking?"MYou've never prepared so much as microwaveable Hot Pokétt for yourself.""BENNETT: Not under your roof."MBut I've learned much in my time away, including how to care for myself."3I would enjoy a chance to demonstrate as much."3SERRA: Well... We could try to do it together."As equals?"BENNETT: As equals, then."(Would you mind skinning the apples?"&Volcarona can get the fire going."4\PN, you've done enough. Have a seat and relax.")The rest of this meal will be on us."0A hole in the ground shoots directly below."
Jump?"/SERRA: Well, it should be done any minute."UBENNETT: Nearly. I'll sprinkle it with the rest of the powder for an extra kick."0And garnish with the greens, and... voilà."GSERRA: Your presentation is certainly better than mine ever was..."dBENNETT: They say presentation is half the appeal. I'm sure you would know that from your work.";But it is not the half that matters. How is the taste?"SERRA: ..."'For cave-made curry, it's not bad."QBENNETT: Sweet and spicy is a classic mix. The key is balancing it properly."VSERRA: In fact, if you told me this was from the Spyce, I might even believe you."HBENNETT: Your praise is appreciated. As was your help in making it."That goes for both of you.")BENNETT: Hello up there, little one."Interested in a bite?"!There's plenty to go around."+BENNETT: See, there's nothing to fear."!Here, allow me to serve you."OBENNETT: Well, someone certainly seems to be energetic after their dinner."TSERRA: Is this the part where our wholesome family meal devolves into violence?"%BENNETT: Sporting violence only."FI do believe our little friend here is ready to burn some energy."5\PN, this is usually your prerogative, isn't it?".SERRA: You're just handing it off to \PN?";Didn't you pick up Fire types for your Elite position?"�BENNETT: My priority here was just making sure Anomalies were contained, and this little guy doesn't seem to be attached to one."5There will be other opportunities for me anyway.")The floor is yours as you wish, \PN."#BENNETT: This one's all yours."?I'm sure you can give it an appropriately enjoyable fight."BENNETT: So that's that."3SERRA: Well, I appreciate you having me along.""Even if I didn't do anything."kBENNETT: You did help with the kitchenware and cooking. There's no need to put your own efforts aside."<Equals includes treating yourself with respect as well."SERRA: ...Oh,"JWell, that's not a lesson I should have to learn from my own child..."<... But from someone who's my equal, I guess it's okay.":BENNETT: Everyone needs a reminder from time to time."For now, shall we be off?"SERRA: I think so."qI have a long night of staring into the middle distance and contemplating my own flawed perspective planned.";BENNETT: As long as you're contemplating improving it.".\PN, would you like to walk back with us?" BENNETT: Then let's be off."@BENNETT: I can't blame you for wanting to look around more."NThis is really quite an interesting environment we've stumbled onto here."qI'd be interested in learning exactly how the local ecosystem maintains temperature and stability despite..."[Uh, well, not to bore you... Let's just say "I think it's neat," and leave it at that."Until next time, \PN.">SERRA: So now we've got dinner, and a show to go with it."FThis is almost better than most of the actual dates I've been on."%VICTINI: Ti-ti-ti-ti-ti-ti-ni!!!"Check Ingredients"
