y don't want to, we can always trade now!"<Are you sure you don't want a moment to meet and greet?"CHIEF: Just as well!">It'll be a long trip-- go on and socialize while you can!"3CHIEF: Hrm... If you're sure, it's no problem!"=CHIEF: Have you made all the rounds you want to already?"CHIEF: Very good!"Let's trade off then."GI'll keep an eye on the guests-- you can keep an eye on the goods."RBetween us, not a soul on board will have so much as a chance to swipe these!"Then I'll be off."'CHIEF: Take good care of the orbs!"YI'll check in again in a bit-- perhaps even bring you something from the snack cart!"Until then!"0The engine car is off limits to passengers."Locked."CRAUDBURRY: YOU."#What are YOU doing here, hmmm?"ACome to ruin the relaxing getaway of a kind, elderly woman?!"[How DARE you even consider violating the sanctity of this train with your PUTRESCENCE!" So much for the dining car!"iThey'd better decontaminate every square inch of this place after inviting GUTTER TRASH like YOU in!"Get away from me at once!"0My poor nose can only take so much at once."�CRAUDBURRY: Are you naturally this insufferable or is it just your mission to make your presence as OFFENSIVE as humanly possible?"Begone!"SANDY: Oh, hi \PN!"&Are you surprised to see me here?">It's true that I decided field work wasn't for me, but...""Desk jobs are just so boring!"MDo you know how tiring is to just sit there and organize papers all day?"eWaiting for the next Certified Cool Person to walk up and take the crazy jobs you're doling out?"3It's like-- why aren't I out there doing that?"WBut I KNOW why I'm not out there doing that-- it's because a Miltank pooped on me!"9But am I to live my life cowering in fear from one--"Heh, COW-ering..."...What was I saying?"�Anyway, I couldn't take the pressure of mentally ping-ponging between wanting to get outside more and wanting to hide inside forever,"\So now I'm here on a moving train going in the opposite direction from all my problems!"$Funny how life works, isn't it?"^SANDY: Hey, you don't think that there's Miltank in wherever this train is going, do you?"JOHN: \PN.""Curious to run into you here."<Rest assured, I harbor no particular resentment to you,"VEven if your actions have resulted in the deaths of several of my past employers."..."FOn second thought, I may have some slight resentment towards you,"JBut you may be relieved that I intend to deal with it professionally."Good day."JOHN: I said "Good day.""!EUSTACE: Greetings, peasant."9Make yourself useful and fetch me a drink, will you?"9Some kind of juice, I believe, would suit my palate."Be forewarned though-- present me with Leppa Juice and I shall forcibly eject you from the train while it is still moving."{Grepa Juice neither-- I don't know what else they put in that stuff, but it surely wasn't meant for human consumption."tAnd you will hold the Oran Juice as well. It is unsuitable for all occasions except the blandest of breakfasts."Hop to it, garçon."FWe can't all stand around all day with stupid looks on our faces."EUSTACE: Garçon?" Where is my juice, garçon?"'The service here is truly abysmal."4JULIA: \PN, I thought that was you who went by!"(What a coincidence seeing you here!"JI was invited for a trip abroad by someone, and would you believe it?"I got stood up!"Me!",Imagine a cheerleader getting stood up!"RI hope the guy recently realized he was gay, or else I want an explanation!!!"xAnd if he did realize he's gay, then I hope he's very happy with his life choices and finds a wonderful husband!!!!"CBut not if the husband would've been interested in me instead!"=It's a pity-- he seemed like such a sweet-talker, too..."But no matter!"*I'm making the best of the situation!"SAnd I've met a fine gentleman in his absence, and we are having a lovely time,"+So there, Mr.Stander-Upper! Take that!"-JULIA: Maybe he just missed the train..."`I almost got on the wrong one-- but I blame him for telling me which it was so last minute!"Mrrgrgrr..."/MAXWELL: \PN. Funny running into you here."lI was just heading out on this train for a change of pace, when I met this lovely lady across from me--"JULIA: Ohstopityou~"#No, I'm kidding-- keep going--"8MAXWELL: For you, baby, I can keep going all night.".But let's take things slow, how about it?"�Anyway, regardless of whatever history we have, I do hope you wouldn't ruin a personal outing just for the sake of some petty past drama."IMy boys are back at the ranch-- you'll get no trouble from our gang."Take care."ARCHER: Ah, \PN."9I understand you're acquainted with my date tonight."�I was just heading out on some business-- which I would ask for your discretion with regards to, lest I mention your own involvement--"VWhen I encountered this young treasure who had been abandoned by some lesser man."EI feel it is only just not to let her mourn her rejection alone."(JULIA: Forget whoever that guy was!"!Tell me more about yourself!"(ARCHER: Naturally, all in due time."OWe have an entire voyage ahead of us to get to know each other, after all."DIn any case, I would appreciate if you granted us some privacy."NYou'll find no unsavory business from me on this ride-- you have my word.""MAXWELL: Until we meet again."%ARCHER: Some space, if you will?"KHow are we supposed to enjoy a moment between the two of us otherwise?"?MAXWELL: My date appears to have pulled a vanishing act..."ARCHER: Curious."Just where did she go...?"DMAXWELL: Well, it seems like we're on opposite sides again, hm?")But I'm innocent as innocent can be."What've you got to ask me?"JMAXWELL: You know, I don't think there's a point in denying this one."wEither of the orbs has power enough that could give me the edge I need to bring the Magma Gang back to full glory."%That's just a no-brainer, right?"II'd just be making myself look more suspicious if I lied about that.",MAXWELL: I'd love to give you an alibi."-I was sitting right here the whole time."1Didn't move an inch, like a good little boy.