're hungry again."..."Ugh... Okay, look..."3I'm a fair man, so I can strike you a bargain."�My Aipom clearly has an eye for a snack, and I certainly can't be bothered searching this dreary dystopia to satiate its... exquisite tastes."So, Trainer..."iYou find some Nanab Berries for my Aipom; say... three of them, and I'll show you the way back home."Sound fair?"?It better, because I doubt you're getting home without me."+I'll be waiting just a bit further up."5To be honest, Trainer... you've got me thinking."+What I saw was quite peculiar, really."cYou’re not quite the Trainer we need, but at the very least... you’ve raised my curiosity."Hmph..."The name's Shiv."And yours?"Your name is... Lin?"$Hah! What kind of name is Lin?!";It sounds like something you just made up on the spot."AHonestly, the longer I talk to you, the stranger you become."-Hmph... Maybe you really do belong here."Anyway... uh, Lin..."NLook, I said I’d let you leave, and I’m certainly a man of my word..."NHowever, before you go, I want a first-hand experience of how you battle."*Doesn’t sound too difficult, right?"-After those three battles you endured..."$How tough can little old me be?"+Well, I’d ask what your choice is...")But obviously, you don’t have one."XLet me know when you’ve prepared yourself, and we’ll get this show on the road.""And please, don’t dawdle..."<You took long enough to do everything else around here."8SHIV: I’m glad you took the time to prepare, Lin."9But to be honest... I don’t know why you bothered."5It won’t make any difference in the slightest."1After all... this dream isn’t yours alone."Well, color me surprised."<SHIV: Well... that certainly wasn't supposed to happen."CEveryone finds themselves surprised at one point or another..."Even me."No matter."RAs I said before, any amount of preparation wouldn't matter in the slightest.",You have your tricks... and I have mi\^"NSHIV: Okay, so perhaps the scales were somewhat tipped out of your favor."'But I suppose 