e a structure like the rest of us..."HCould've even left out the lights if that's really what she's into."Well, whatever."JFor starters, why don't we try activating the crystals one at a time?"CWith just that mirror, we should be able to get two right now."SSERRA: That second mirror panel appeared when you activated that orb of light."0Looks like there's gonna be more to this..."JWith that second mirror, the lower left crystal should now be usable."D...But since each time you fire the lights, they seem to reset."RSo, you might need to find a way to activate more than one crystal at a time."3That purple crystal might be the key for that."[It doesn't reset like the others, and it can be activated when the light is in motion."VIt also seems to interact with the outline shapes left behind around the mirrors?"{If we put all these pieces together as best we can, I think we can use it to bounce the light off of the same mirror twice."1That bottom right crystal is also reachable."5It might behoove us to see what effect that has."*SERRA: Another one on the table, huh?" Makes it easier, I suppose."LI noticed that door above lights up whenever you activate each crystal."BI suspect by the end we'll have to light up all four at once."IMaybe those strange lights left behind by the mirrors are the key..."$SERRA: Looks like it went well."We're ready to go as well."$And we'll be behaving, correct?"kLUNA: One could argue that 'behaving' encompasses an infinite number of actions one might undertake..."9But your meaning is understood and kindly respected,"ASo long as our choices are understood and respected in turn."nELIAS: I suppose this is the part where we each go around and restate what we've learned from the ordeal?"Very well."dI understand that, whatever revelations I may have, it is far from my place to play missionary."kTo impose personal beliefs onto others, even for their perceived benefit, is indeed a lack of respect."OI must trust that my daughter knows what she needs t