ing care of others is very helpful to yourself."^And Amaria here has recently started doing the same, getting some houseplants of her own!"XAMARIA: Yeah, my place was feeling a little empty, so I got a plant to liven it up!"UAnd one turned into two, and two turned into three, and three turned into ten..."'I mean, you guys get it, I'm sure."9Anyway, that's actually what I wanted to talk about."ZOne of my plants has an infestation, you see, and I don't know what to do about it..."LAURA: Oh, how awful!"%BENNETT: ...Infestation of what?"wAMARIA: I'm not certain, but they're tiny and when I tried to water the plant the other day, I got a little shock?"!BENNETT: Sounds like Joltik."ADon't worry, they're a lot less of a problem than you think.",I mean, the plant is probably done for."[But taking care of a few hundred Joltik is remarkably easy, and they're very friendly."First you need--"HOh, actually, you'll need protectors for any of your power outlets."SThey're small enough to get inside and chew on wires, that can be a problem..."\Any exposed wiring is an issue really. If your computer is higher end, you might need--"LAURA: Bennett!";She was asking about the plant, not all of the Joltik."xI understand your excitement, but you should remember what people asked for help with when you're giving your help."BENNETT: Oh, right."*Sorry, Amaria. I got ahead of myself."Laura can take this one.";AMARIA: Oh, it's okay, I understand getting excited..."PLAURA: Right, well, Joltik are actually not a problem for the plant at all!"HIn fact, the small electric charge they give off encourages growth!"WAnd they aren't actually interested in eating the plant, they just want the water."7So you need to make sure to water the plant extra."FOh, while they pose no danger to the plant, there is some to you."/You'll need to water from a safe distance,";Make sure the plant is nowhere near any electronics..."7Make sure no people or Pokémon touch the plant..."8If you need to repot, wear heavy p