to ame?"sure, hold on."okay, sure!"Dfull disclosure, i really have no idea what to talk about here."{i'm writing this on new year's eve so you're just going to be getting whatever stray thoughts come into my head today."5take your pick. \ch[62,-1,who u,devving,lessons]"Ftake your pick. \ch[62,-1,who u,devving,lessons, likes, dislikes]"Mtake your pick. \ch[62,-1,who u, devving, lessons, likes, dislikes, ame]"im cass",look, i never know what to say to this."5here, i'll add some more options to the chatbox."ah yes."!back when i was a smol child"at the wee age of 21"7i hit up ame and was like "hey you want some help""/and ame was like "yeah do some animations""Li had played reborn twice and liked it enough to come back to it later."Ji like helping out with things that have potential and need the help." but god i hated animations."�the animation editor worked in a legal sense. if you consulted the dictionary definition of "functional" you would likely deduce that the editor qualified as such."(but working with it was a bad time."i made one animation.":now i genuinely don't remember what i did after that."nlife was rough. i ended up clicking with ame really well and moved in with her at the end of that summer."7i did a lot of uncategorizable dev work for a bit."�i think the most notable thing i did was filesize reduction. e17 was the largest episode of reborn and i'm doing my best to keep it that way."tafter that i got into teambuilding. most of the nightclub content was done by me. it's why i have an NPC there."Lit would've been... about three years ago by the time this is released."ki've gotten a bit better at teambuilding since then! just in case some of the teams seem a bit crusty."�later that year we put out e18.2. that was technically my first release! it was just a small update to the AI to put out some fixes."Vafter that was when i started putting effort into getting the game to run better."hbefore this, i had some minor experience with scripting. i generally didn't like working with code."Sthen perry showed up with a script that evaluated the performance of the code.""i took that and went to town."Uregular readers of my devblog posts will recall the optimization o'clock series."�i spent an absolute shitload of time combing through the scripts, running the profiler, making changes, re-running the profiler, noting differences, making changes, re-rerunning the profiler..."Aas weird as it may sound, it was a life-changing experience."�i think i'm probably known more generally as a coder these days. which is weird! if you told me before my optimization binge that my primary role on the team was going to be as a scripter, I'd have laughed really hard before tossing you out of my office."(metaphorical office)"@it got me to realize that, hey, maybe coding wasn't so bad!"#and now i'm really good at it!"?hell, the optimization binge practically changed fangames."bif this isn't your first fangame, you've probably felt the impact of this without knowing it."nthe biggest effect was probably that it kicked off a series of events that led to making MKXP mainstream."8i don't know if you happened to use the old engine."it sucked."@it ran badly for everyone no matter what hardware you used."3it was in desperate, dire need of improvement."Fif you've never experienced it then i consider that a good thing."Bit also opened up the development of the main fangame engine."_you've probably experienced something based on my code modifications without realizing it."+and, well, i guess now we're at today!"3i help out with a number of different games..."%i've made a fuckload of teams..."destroyed the code..."and now here we are!"wso if you're playing this game, or rejuv, or some other game, and noticing that it's running smooth like butter..."i'm glad i could help!"+look at you picking the cheesy option."Ahopefully you also picked them in order so this has context!"'man i'm bad at talking about this."reborn's changed my life.".....god that's SO cheesy."/i think it's making me lactose intolerant."Oi said that i was in a bad place when i first got involved in development."Ci could really use a change of environment, change of scenery."reborn's where i got that."`it kinda got off to a rocky start. i was in a social circle that was... not the healthiest."Hbut then i got out of that. made new friends, worked on new things."%i've come a long way since then!"*people don't take fangames seriously."Je comprends."7but that doesn't mean that they aren't meaningful."�i've met a lot of cool people, i've worked on a project that other people enjoy, i've acquired a lot of new skills, and i've (hopefully!) helped out other people in the process."=i don't want to say that there's a "lesson" from this..."&but keep yourself open to things!"*you never know where they might lead."5interesting things. whatever that ends up being.">dishonesty. assholes. RMXP. other shit that doesn't work."ok there. happy now?"hif there's one thing that i can say with certainty it's that i don't know how to talk about myself."9yeah that's right ame!!!! i'm doing this too!!!!!!!!"...ahem"Kso none of this would've happened if i didn't get involved with reborn"8and that wouldn't've happened if it wasn't for ame."}ame will tell you about how making reborn kinda happened on accident- one thing led to another thing and now we're here."{that's kinda true of my presence in the community, too. i never had any expectations of things going the way they did."bbut i'm here! and, in hindsight, moving in with ame was probably the best decision i've made."�she's great. really cares about the community. really dedicated to making things for people to enjoy. really wants the best for the people around her.")she's my best friend and i love her."Cyeah i bet THATS not something you expect to see in a fangame."%lol fangames are just edgy trash"7yeah well this one got the developer a girlfriend!"8...though idk how true that'll be for other people."ame cray."AMÉ: O-oh?"Uh, hi there!"DDidn't expect to come back into this world like this, but okay!"*Don't worry, I'm still dead in canon."uWell, I was looking forward to putting in a secret room like this for so long and now I barely know what to say."WIn spite of that, I tend to talk a lot, so I'll probably say too much here anyway."uI know whenever I finish a game I liked, I always have a ton of questions about the development and its creator."7I want to know like "how did this game happen????""}So I'll try and pre-empt some of that with the answers I wished maybe I'd have access too if I were just finishing this."lTbh, that's most of how I approach the game; I just try to make something I'd enjoy playing for myself.";Anyway, feel free to ask about anything in particular."4AMÉ: Did you want to ask about something else?"eWhat'll it be? \ch[62,-1,Myself, Community ,League,Game,Leaders,Team,Future,Lessons,Fight ,Cass]"?AMÉ: Oh, sure, I can get over myself long enough to talk."So firstly, let's get this straight-- aside from existing in this particular room, I don't love having a self-insert character."�When I made the game based on the online league, we were pretty much exclusively using existing characters from the community though,"tAnd as the community leader and one running the online league, I was the closest thing to a "Professor" we had."�I didn't ever expect the game to go beyond the community, so then when it did, I'm like okay, I am sick of having a damn self-insert in this entire-ass game."oA lot of people kept expecting me to be the surprise villain or surprise champion or something, and like--"
No!!!"5I want to exist frankly as little as possible!!!"2And, well, you know how I fixed that problem."_Outside of myself as a character though, like, I'm just a girl who likes making videogame."tI got started with private lessons when I was 9, Game Maker when I was 10, and found RPG Maker when I was 11..."Y(To all you aspiring game devs out there, if 11-year- old me can do it, so can you.)"C...And I definitely tunnel-visioned on making games back then."hI didn't finish any of them, but I did spend several years on an isekai aRPG called Second Reality."�That's the only real prior experience I have here, and classically, I will want to perish if I think about that project too much."OStill, that experience helped me make this happen, so I'm grateful for it."vI went to school for psychology, but that was just a backup until any of my creative pursuits became sustainable."=I was originally writing a novel when Reborn took off..."DThe "Living Angel" thing in the circus was a reference to that."3But I abandoned the project to focus on games."aThanks to the community's support, I've been able to work on this full time for a while now."Tysm everyone!!! <33333"VI hope that the project has been able to live up to your expectations in the end,"ABut it definitely exceeded my own, so either way, I'm happy."8I hope I can keep doing this for a long time still."BAlthough I won't be making Pokémon games anymore after this,"(let me out.......)"\Maybe this won't be the last time you find me in a room like this at the end of a game!"@AMÉ: So, Reborn was a community long before it was a game."NMy dad taught me the basics of HTML, PHP, MySQL, etc when I was 10 or so,"(Thanks Dad!)">So I was running my own website by the time I was twelve."nWhen Diamond and Pearl came out a few years later, everyone wanted to try out the hot new WiFi functions,"�So I gathered a handful of people from various internet communities I was in, and my own website, and set up a subdomain on my site for us to try WiFi!"_That Pokémon-oriented subdomain ended up outliving the main site by a significant margin."=Even though there were only like, a dozen of us there..."<It was very lively and a lot of fun during the summers!"qIt didn't have a proper name or anything, so it just kinda got called PokéPlace in lack of anything better."KBut then, once school started, we all got busy and the place died too."k...And then when summer rolled around again, everyone was back battling and trading, so it was reborn!"lThis happened several years in a row, being dead during the school year, and then busy in the summer..."S...Which is why Reborn got its name! Because the site was Reborn every summer!"_...Well, it skipped a year. We all kind of moved on towards the end of 4th gen's lifespan."�I decided to bring it back the next year under its own site properly, and so we launched the current version of the site in May of 2010."PBy that time the League was a thing, but that's a separate dialogue option."jThe League ended up attracting a lot of people though, so we grew wayyy more than I ever expected to,"-And then the game attracted even more..."And here we all are today!"NMy life really wouldn't be anywhere near the same without this community,"[And although I've never been a fan of other big sites and places (too many people?!?!)"iI'm very grateful to everyone who's stuck around, contributed, just popped into chat briefly, etc..."YAnd I hope that those of you further away from us will consider dropping by someday!"uPlus, everyone whose support has kept me going through that alternate evolution of Eevee when you give it money,"3Really, like, makes my life awesome, you know?"%Thank you so much everyone <3333"eAMÉ: So, this game was based on the online Reborn League challenge we hosted for several years."/But how did that league itself come about?"BOriginally, it was a challenge to my best friend at the time."lWe met through the RPG Maker community, and enjoyed playing difficulty hacks like Emerald 386 together."�He and I often said things like, "Wouldn't it be awesome if you could fight Gym Leaders that actually put up as much of a fight as real people?""gSo when I was 14 or so, I came up with a list of badge names, images, and pun names for each type,"JAnd you basically know all of those already. I think I kept them all."FI started making that challenge for him around the time I was 15."WTerra was the first Leader I worked on, but she was no more than a name back then."�I remember spending a lot of time EV Training Gliscor and Flygon in actual Pearl, and I was going to create a team for each type that way."�...I didn't get farther than Gliscor and Flygon before my friend and I had a falling out, and we didn't really speak much after that."?The challenge died, and I also quit making games entirely."mA few years later, I found that image with all the badges and Leader names, and decided to try it again."qReborn had already existed as a community by then, and subsequently died (for good, even over the summer)..."iBut I still hung out with most of the people involved in a small little community called Monkey Pro."bMaybe they would be interested in the Gym Leader challenge I'd started for my friend instead?"�I also knew the Shoddy Battle simulator was a thing by then, so I was able to convince one of Monkey Pro's members, Hyperlisk, to host a private server for us."+Terra was once again the first Leader."WMy concept for her this time was "a girl who's personality is like an earthquake"."~I made Trainer Cards for each of them, and sprites that I worked on during class, or backstage from theatre rehearsals..."bI roleplayed the Leaders myself, and some of them didn't have much character, but it was fun."}So, it became a somewhat daily ritual for me to bark at some friends on MP, asking them if they'd like to do a Leader battle."<People seemed to really enjoy this "Monkey Pro League"."cThen I got kicked out of theatre, fell into depression, and stopped hosting it for months lmao"5In May of 2010, I decided to give it another go."�This time, I found the Pokémon Online simulator, which was way more friendly than Shoddy Battle, and another MP member hosted a server for us."You would know him as Nyu!"GI also made the current iteration of the site to go along with it."\This League began like the last, with me asking my friends if they wanted to Do A Fight"�...But what I didn't expect was for random-users to drop in from the greater Pokémon Online space and decide "Hey, this looks interesting!"">In this way, the league and community grew quite rapidly!"IAnd so, we hosted it nearly every weekday evening for several years."YIt quickly got too much for me to handle alone, so eventually I had to ask for help.":We used to do three battles per challenger per night,"DAnd then I had to limit it to just one as we got more and more,"bAnd then sometimes even at one battle per challenger, we'd still be up until two or three AM."\Managing that, team registrations and trainer cards really was a full time job already."But it was a lot of fun!"�My favorite part was how, when everyone was waiting for their own turn, the challengers would all pile into spectate each match."fThere was a lot of wild cheering for either side, fifteen people to a very small chat log room..."TAnd people would chat with and get interested in the Leaders' personal stories."|Many of the events in game are a reference to those online stories, such as Amaria losing her memory, and Luna disappearing."dShortly after sixth gen released, we made the difficult decision to retire the League for good."tThe bottom line is that I wasn't able to keep up with both running it and developing the game at the same time."�There were some other factors, like Pokémon Showdown becoming popular, and I wasn't entirely thrilled with the quality of recent matches and events."SBut even those things were just obstacles because the game was taking my time."]I hope everyone who was able to participate in the League has some fun memories from it!"7I know they were some of my favorite times ever <3"RAMÉ: When the League was at its peak, a few different users had the idea of,"7What if we made a game based on the Reborn League?"eThe first few fledgling passes at it from community members disappeared as quickly as they came.">For my part, I didn't pay the wayward attempts much mind."zI knew that trying to do that for all 18 Leaders would be an enormous undertaking that obviously no one would finish."2Also, I tried romhacking in the distant past."�I wanted to make, basically, Fire Red 386 since there wasn't a good difficulty + all availability game for Kanto like there was for Hoenn at the time."<Somehow I broke evolution by changing a Trainers' team."5Decided pretty quickly romhacking wasn't for me."{However, there was an ongoing thread of discussion over the months about "What would Reborn look like if it were a region?""eOne time in the PO server's earliest days, I signed off for the night as the sole admin and mod."PI'm not exactly clear what happened-- maybe a spammer or something came on?">Anyway, I wasn't there to deal with it, and havoc ensued."�One of the users on at the time, Will, then made an entire lore about how The City of Reborn Fell Into Chaos Because The Great Leader Ame Wasn't There."�He then started drawing +Infinitas, a comic about the leaders of Reborn facing off against the villainous Team Meteor, based on that premise...".I liked the idea of a ruined city region."WIt felt more fresh compared to the lush, vapid environments of every other region."MTo be honest, I also just like working with the concept of giant cities?",I find it likely this won't be my last."jAnyway, one of those times people were talking about The Region, I started hand-drawing a map for it."4Did it on and off, took me two years to finish."gI had a lot of fun, due to old habits, thinking about "What might this be like if it were a game?""4But I had no intention to actually make it one."Then, in 2012 a Reborn member by the name of STK Patrick posted once again about making a game based on the online league."OHe noted that a game called Pokémon Raptor had a working Pokémon engine."2I was like, "huh, weird, how does that work?""*He was like "oh it uses RPG Maker XP""0I was like "okay hold the goddamn phone rq,"fbecause i spent the better part of my teenage years tooling around on Rm2k3 and RMXP on the side."#This is suddenly up my alley.""cPulled a "yo imma let you finish but--" on him (because that was an in-vogue meme at the time)"-And made the first episode in two weeks."�I'm... not really sure how I managed that in two weeks other than that the episode kinda sucked at the time, and I didn't do anything else."ZAnyway, I pretty much just worked on the game during every class until I graduated..."�And the character assets already existed from the League, and I asked Will to give me some Team Meteor characters (Sirius and Solaris) for villains."�The community had some fun roleplaying events VS Team Meteor on the server, and another user, Ice, had contributed the characters of Taka and ZEL."CAce came later, and everyone else came from the League itself."AWhen I first started, I figured I'd get bored of it quickly."LMaybe drop the project after a couple months like most of my past ones.""...You can see how that went."�Because I thought I'd get bored, I didn't bother to figure out where the game was actually going until Heather first showed up in Malchous."EThen I'm like, oh, maybe I should like make a plan for anything."�I figured out a story based around fitting in all of the existing league characters, and four macguffins to help tie them together."�Originally I expected this to only be an in-community game, but then people started telling their friends about it and joining because of it..."nOver time I pivoted to make the game more accessible to anyone, even those who hadn't been in the League."fSo, I continued as the sole developer, and released episodes every 2-5 months at a steady pace..."IAnd I hit a wall around E14 (ending with Terra, released late 2014)."}I started wanting to focus on making the game Better as opposed to just More, which increased development time exponentially."aSuddenly releases took half a year to a year and a half, rather than just a few months each."I wasn't ready for that."mI blamed myself for taking too long, and went from doing almost nothing else to -actually- nothing else."gI pushed myself very hard to be perfectly productive, always trying to get E15 out faster because,"[Like E14 (Terra) to E15 (Ciel) is not a lot of content, why is it taking so long??????"FIt took around a year in the end with all the other improvements."aI also began to develop chronic pain in my hands, which I was determined not to let stop me."LEventually I physically couldn't click the mouse, and I had to ease up."yWhen I stepped back, I realized that the stress of pushing myself to work constantly was what was causing that pain."XUnlearning that is an ongoing process, and I still feel the pain from time to time."1Right now, as I'm saying this, for instance."}But at least I have it mostly under control, and I've learned to pace myself better, take breaks, play nice with a team, etc."�I still have some recurring of psychic damage from the amount it's taken to complete a passion project that I started on a whim...":I wonder how many other games I'll have time to make?"\But, I'm trying to learn to be proud of the amount of time and energy we spent on this."BNot many games get the full attention and scope they deserve."NAnd honestly, of all things? I'm not sure a Pokémon fangame deserved it."Still, here we are.">Ten years working on one project is nothing to sneeze at."I hope it shows?"4AMÉ: So, here's the story from my perspective."~I started running the online league by myself, blahblahblah, you can read about all of that in the other dialogue option.">Originally, I was just roleplaying the Leader characters."cLogistically, that meant I just signed on a second account and acted like them, nothing fancy."YWhen I was doing this challenge just for friends, there was no confusion about that."iIn fact, one time my IRL friend, Saya, decided to do a league battle during a rehearsal lunch break."aI fought as Hardy, who, at the time, played singles stall rather than doubles hyper offense.")Hardy's Shuckle vs their Empoleon..."!The battle took 200 turns..."-...We got yelled at for being very late."tAnyway, the point is, for the original challengers of the League, they knew exactly who was behind the leaders."3We were just across the table from each other."MI never expected there to be any doubt that they were just me all along."�Then, in the early days of the PO server, a user named Mashew joined at random and became interested in the league and its characters."/Only, he didn't realize they weren't real."BThere was no question of it, he just accepted that they were."This surprised me."sHe seemed to be having a lot of fun and getting personally invested in their stories, so I didn't correct him."pAfter all, it was way more fun to add some character, some drama, and play out a bit of conflict with them."NWhen others started joining after him, they seemed to believe it all too."�One example was Savage, who you might recall from the story in Lapis. That was a real thing that really happened in the League for some reason."dEven the people who originally knew that I was just roleplaying implicitly began to play along."%They seemed to get very into it."OI wondered if everyone, including Saya, had just forgotten that it was me."RMonths passed like this, and it was hard to keep up with all the challengers.":I ran 17 different monotypes, 5 nights a week, alone.">On average, I think there were 20-30 challengers a night."Hundreds over time."It was... difficult."wI invented the "sorry Luna disappeared arc" one night as an excuse to not have to play her when I wasn't up to it."\Other nights when I was just super stressed out and not feeling it, I pushed on anyway."kPlaying Terra and trying to capture her hyperness online, while crying about something or other IRL..."That was just the worst."ASaya happened to show up at my house on one of those nights."fI found out, she didn't forget it was me playing it, she was just going along with everyone else."bAnd everyone seemed to have a lot of fun accepting the different characters at surface level."AIt felt nice to not be entirely alone in keeping the secret."cIn Febuary of 2011, I realized that hosting the League by myself was absolutely unsustainable.",The volume of challengers was too high."6There was just too much for one person to handle."�I confided in our co-admin, Ikaru, who joined us in the fall of the year prior, after the Leaders' had already been accepted as a force of nature."�He was very invested in Titania, and finding out that the character who was so motivated by the notion of living up to truth, was herself a lie, hurt him."qI'm very grateful for his forgiveness, and that he stuck around to support the league and game despite that."qIkaru and Saya became my first co-hosts of the league, and joined me in hosting and roleplaying the leaders."]Even splitting them to a third between us, we barely kept up with the challenger volume."MAlso, it was stressful for them to have to keep up with every night too."pWe swapped out League Hosts over the next few years, being joined by Mashew, Ash, Hark, and several others,"ZAll of whom I'm very grateful to for helping manage the disaster traffic I'd amassed."GIn general, it was never one player to one specific Leader though."gI could barely keep the three or four of us in place each night, let alone a full roster of 17-18."VThere were two exceptions, being that for much of Season 2, I only played Amaria,"RAnd for a while we had one line leader by the name of Tenshi, who played Lin."�I was never terribly enthused with his capacity for roleplaying, but he was an excellent battler who swept through the League without batting an eye.";However, he eventually decided to leave the community,"[And he did so by posting a sudden resignation announcement in which he basically said,"MThe Leaders are all fake and being played by us, and I'm sick of it, bye"3I thought, okay, that's it, jig's up, go home."xGoing to be a lot less interesting entertaining my crowd of hundreds when they know it's just us in different hats."+I was surprised by what happened next."zObviously there were the handful of people who knew, and the handful of people who Thought So but didn't Know-know..."/But the general tone of the community was,"wIt's more fun to accept them as real, so let's just let the new folk keep believing that so they can enjoy it too."uThe game began to be a thing at some point after that, and the League stopped being a thing at some point later,"{But this was always still meant to be a community game, so it seemed like everyone implicitly accepted the same thing.";More fun to let the new players think it was all real."�I decided I'd keep it up until the game finished, but I really expected that to be, like, six years ago or so as opposed to only just now."PI've been tired of that all forever, but sunken cost is one hell of a drug."TRecently, there's been a lot of people who are morally concerned about it too--"�About whether or not it was okay for us to show things like Corey and Kiki, given their respective fates (which were story points in the online league too)"QAnd whether we got the express consent of the Leaders to be featured here..."C...And while those are fair concerns, they don't really apply."7They were all just fictional characters all along."=To some this will be disappointing; to others, a relief."!For myself, it's the latter."XI'm grateful to have this out in the open again so I can talk more freely about it."[I hope that everyone will forgive me for keeping up the facade for more than a decade."I understand if not."4Maybe let the new players have their fun still?"Maybe not."It's in your hands now."TAME: So like I said in the other dialogue options, I started this game alone..."CReally never was great at the whole working with others thing?"�I was like, weirdly afraid if I let someone else access the game's files, they'd just delete everything and run screeching into the night like some kind of gremlin."DObviously, that's ridiculous and most people just want to help."�I first started working with a team directly when The Amount Of Things That Needed To Be Done escalated in 2013 after the E13 (Charlotte) release."�Realistically, my standards just rose, but I needed help, so I started working with two good friends, Autumn and Blind Guardian (or Dan)."}You can thank Autumn for a lot of the animations in the game, especially the over the top ones like many of the Z-Moves!"�Dan helped shore up the bleeding scripts, and first encouraged me to try implementing the Field Effect system. He also made it so fields changed visually!"1But at first, they just helped with testing."wWe packed into a call, Autumn would play through the game with some ridiculous team probably involving a Castform,"}Dan would fix script errors, and I would do whatever else it was that needed doing and also probably stress out a little bit."It was a lot of fun!"HI was sad when that groove came to an end, but I still needed help."fThe early versions of Essentials were incomplete, and subsequent generations made that gap worse."dDespite running a website, I was still a fledging programmer, and I couldn't fix it all myself."BI got some help from someone I met in a game called Guhorden!"[I feel like of everyone who's helped out on development, I know the least about him..."YBut he offered his services where they were much needed, and I appreciated it a lot."TThe next to offer was Kurotsune, near the end of E14 when they were very drunk."sI had never talked to this person, and I was still pretty distrustful of Why Would This Rando Want To Help Me?".Which in retrospect was completely silly."�Kuro became an invaluable mentor to me both in terms of good programming habits (sorry about the indentation!!!) and organizing a team."They undertook the initiative to get a few more hands in to help finish the rest of the new-gen additions to the battle system."7Notably from that, we picked up Mike and Marcello!"]I felt bad because the process of development seemed to age Mike a half-decade at least,"And, like, same."mBut it seems he's back at it with his own work now so maybe that'll be a project worth checking out, ne?"�And Marcello went from being someone who I knew was helping out with the game but had never spoken to, to being one of my best friends. So that's neat!"?You can thank him for online existing in its current form!"kI followed suit, getting together a team to help out with all the missing animations around that time.">Smeargle and MDE were the main two I picked up from that!"WI'm pretty sure the M in MDE stood for "machine" because man, he cranked them out."VI think he still holds the title for having made the most animations in the game."WHe was very reliable and patient while I asked him for revisions eight times over!"�Meanwhile our resident Smeargletail has done quite a lot on his own too, and tends to hit them out of the park with a lot of care and energy!"YHe also made all the slick Legendary overworld animations you might see in postgame."MWe picked up one more animator down the line after MDE moved on, Vulpes!"�She seems to be the shy type, but she came with experience, and pretty much every animation she's done has been a banger out the gate."hOthers who've helped along the way include Azery and Lia, who we brought on for general bug-fixing."There was a lot of it..."|Kanaya and another friend of mine, I'd asked to help out with small tasks like filling in cliffs around the entire desert..."`Seriously, it took two of them two weeks of working on it reliably to get all of that done."7Not to mention the other areas they helped with..."zMuch appreciation to them for trudging through all of that despite me kind of giving them the short end of the stick."|Ikaru's another person who's helped out with filling in my ridiculous maps, along with just general handling of bug reports."lHe's also usually the first person I test with, watching his every playthrough and judging his actions!"Y...And getting trolled when he decides to spam Itemfinder everywhere until I behave."�Jan's just kind of here these days, but originally we had a trade where I helped him out with learning to sprite better in return for him tackling a few sprites for Reborn." Cass joined us late in E18."0Originally she was going to be an animator!"-She did Leafage and no other animations."zBut she more than made up for it in ways I already basically gushed about in another section, so I'll spare her here."DShe did suggest we take on a certain Toothpastefairy, or Perry!"�He happened to be working on some mods anyway so we picked him up to help out and he's just been fantastic for the whole tail end of the ride."�I'm very grateful for him helping us out with programming reliably, and also being totally down to enable whatever bullshit Cass or I get up to."qHe's done a lot of quality-of-life improvements for y'all especially, such as that quick TM view in the bag!"9Other late-joining stars include The Legendary Crim."WYou might know of her from her work on literally every other fangame in existence."KIt's been a huge help to have a second spriter and mapper on the team."Even though she was originally just learning both when I asked her to help with Starlight, she learns fast and caught up quick."iThere's no way we could've made some of the postgame content as gorgeous as it has been without her."3Last but not least, we also acquired an Azzie!"oFans might know her from her Tourmaline Travels story, and if not, they might be interested in reading it!"^She's helped out with a lot of the sundry postgame dialogue, especially in the Nightclub."eIf I had to do it all myself I probably would've gone insane and run into the hills screaming..."...Is that everyone?"I think so..."8Gosh, I've written too much already. Let's be done."NBut please appreciate everyone who's helped us make it to this point, ne?"%AME: So, no more Pokémon games."Sorry, not sorry."I am Tired and Done."-Also, there's the whole copyright thing."{Nintendo, please, we can all just walk away from this peacefully, I don't want anything more to do with it, I swear..."LI know a lot of people will probably be disappointed by it, but like..."qY'all gotta remember, even though I've been here for a decade and change, my start is not in Pokémon games."<I've wanted to make a tactical RPG since I was like 12.""Finally gonna go do that now."VIt's called Starlight Divide, and-- obligatory plug-- we have a demo out already!".Wait, I can just take you to the website!"Wanna give it a look?"(AMÉ: Hell yeah, okay, here you go."thank you ily"8AMÉ: okay that's understandable maybe another time"tRegardless, for those of you who already tried the demo (or even who will go on to try it)-- Thank you so much."BIt means a lot to me that you're willing to give it a chance!"pThere's still a lot of work to do on that too, but I'm eagerly looking forward to the opportunity to do so."NThere's a lot of side projects and other games I want to make too, but..."2I guess we'll just have to see how things go?"`My curse is that I come up with ideas way quicker than I can ever dream of developing them."
Alas."JI hope you'll stick around to see what comes from our next endeavors!"�AMÉ: This might've been unclear, but to be clear this section is just sort of advice/lessons I've learned in the realm of game development."nThere's a handful of things I wish I'd done differently, and so I hope others can learn from my mistakes."7If you're not interested, just hold X or whatever.")Let's start with something positive."OThe lesser-known phrase continues "But better than being a master of one.""&Ultimately, I think that is true."wEspecially as an indie dev starting out, it's important to be willing to handle all parts of the project yourself."�I pride myself on being able to do it all-- music, writing, programming (eventually...), spriting, mapping, animation, sfx, etc..."�The flexibility to do all of that has been a great asset in terms of having confidence in knowing that I could finish this game no matter what."�If you're just starting out, it'll also go a long way to helping you work with team members in a way that works for them, which itself helps build trust."...So that's great,"However,"NI think I've caused myself a lot of problems by relying on that too much."xGood to have the option, but it's equally important to be open to accepting help and letting others take the wheel."�Having explored so many different avenues of development, I quite clearly see what I need to do and practice in order to improve at each of them,"}But because I am doing so many things at once, I will not be able to pursue those paths to the ends of quality I'd like."Frustrating."�It also means I'm prone to taking on too much work myself and overwhelming myself, where I see other teams function better when the lead just"=Doesn't Worry About It because it's #NotTheirDepartment."Pros and cons, I guess."OI wish I'd navigated that a bit better and learned to lean on others more."`Speaking of working with others, we only started using git in the last year of development."pNo one told me about it before, and if they had, we couldn't work it meaningfully without exported scripts."mBut if you're on a team, I can't stress how critical it will be to let them access the project directly."Save yourself.":It's intimidating to learn at first, but so worth it."/Frankly, that goes for programming itself."qI didn't touch the scripts in Reborn for years and then I was like 'oh this is just rpg maker eventing lmao'" Eventing also intimidating?"4Again, if 11-year-old me can do it, so can you."Okay, what else?"}Pretty sure every single indie dev advice article will tell you this too, but I sure didn't listen, so I'm repeating it."sDon't make a giant sprawling epic with 18 badges and every legendary in postgame for your first major project.":...It was my second major project, so I'm vindicated."]...But probably just don't do it, like seriously, small goals are best, I p r o m i s e."[It's very easy to underestimate how long everything will take if you're doing it well."/Never doing a game this long again, i s2g."Probablement."HOkay, I phrased that a little too new-age-spiritually, but, like..."_Now that I'm on the other side of a ten year long project, I'm a lot Better at everything,"SAnd yet there are still things I feel like I could learn from my younger self."jOne of those things is to let myself rest when I don't feel like working, rather than forcing myself."PI talked a bit about the consequences of this in another dialogue option..."LBut I very much grew up admiring people with an unhealthy work ethic..."QThe kind of people who like work until they literally pass out or get sick--"^I felt like by not living up to the same standard, or by taking breaks, I was being lazy."No, that's stupid."[There's something to be said for the programming addage of "work smarter, not harder,""But more importantly..."nMany people are hard on themselves for "being lazy" or "procrastinating" but we are humans who need rest."rListening to yourself when you don't want to work, or when you need to relax, and choosing to trust yourself,"HThat's a necessary habit if you want to be in it for the long term.">Seriously, I don't want anyone to go through what I have."TListen, I know this sounds hokey, but I -promise- this is tangible real advice."HI just said that working harder and forcing yourself is bad, right?"KSo what's the trick to get good at something if you're not feeling it?"OIt's still to do it a lot, but the hack there is to -want- to do it a lot."dIf you're having fun, you're going to want to do it a lot, and you'll naturally get good at it."	See?"@And especially with long-haul development projects, like..."`You either find a way to make it fun for yourself, or it's miserable and drags out forever."+I really can't stress this one enough."3Okay, go out there and make some vidya, y'all.")AMÉ: Oh, so you've chosen violence."All right, here we go."4Good show! It's no wonder you made it this far!"AMÉ: Impressive work!"BBut then, you've made it this far, so who could be surprised?"(Here, let's throw in a BP for that."!That puts you at \v[593] BP."AMÉ: That's okay."�I think I put this in game somewhere, but as I always told the challengers in the online league, you learn more from losses than wins."?This is simply an extra learning opportunity just for you!")Let me heal up your team real quick."AMÉ: All better!"MBy the way, quick shout-out to the Crim for making my transition sprite."|I didn't want to, because I was like 'boo hoo spriting myself is so egotistical lmao whiiineeee' so she covered for me."0Also thanks to Cass for making my dev team,"/And, well, actually, everyone's dev teams,"RAnd while we're at it, pretty much the majority of the post-game teams too???"Girl's crazy."Love her."Okay, carry on."+AMÉ: Oh, sure, we can go back to her."DBut first I'm gonna use the opportunity to talk shit about her."9And by 'talk shit' I mean tell everyone she's great."�Cass joined us around the release of E18, ended up moving in with me, and has generally just done a lot of like, holding me together."nSo you have her to thank for me being able to complete the entire postgame without going literally crazy."�In addition to that, she also got MKXP support going for us back before it was a common thing, which meant less lag and Mac and Linux versions,"~And she broke open the scripts so we could use git like a functional team, made god knows however other many utilities for us,"AOptimized everything, recoded half the battle system and AI,"4All the goddamn teams, the battle tower sets..."T...And probably a lot of other smaller things that neither of us will remember."LThe point is I owe her a lot and I'm very grateful for all of her help."Okay, back to her now."Don't tell her I said this"uwu"DA sinister energy emerges from the generic graphic on the wall."It could be anything..."Do you dare?"i miss techie johnathan"fThe team's terrifying test train-er defeated, a sense of peace overcame you and healed your team.")Suddenly, everything was okay again."EWhatever had happened must have just been a terrible delusion..."-You tried not to let it derail your day."&did the team forget to delete me?"3You tried not to let it get you too off track."So what do you wanna do?"#So you wanna fight? Cool beans"Nice job"$SMEARGLE: Want to take some BP?"You have \v[593] BP now."SMEARGLE: Uh... oops."I'll fix your team."[Just to warn you I have a tendency to ramble and talk too much so here's your warning."[This stuff has also been rewritten a few times even though I kept calling it finished."%So what do you wanna talk about?"nHey my real name is Sam, and my main task to do was work on animations at the end of 2015 along with MDE."ZAlthough, in about the last year of development, I've also gotten to make two quests,"bwith one of those having a new trainer class and two original characters for zeraora's quest."�My friend Crim did touch ups so go give her a hug for me and give my other friend Azzie a hug for helping check my grammar and tightening up words."�Along with that stuff, I did some other tasks too, like the ferris wheel, giant dragon statue, overworld animations,screen overlay animations,ect."�Though my motivation has been off and on, Ame has been super patient with me through the years, honestly more than she probably should have."zDoesn't help that my diet consists of 1 meal and 2 pops a day, and almost no exercise which leaves me sleeping a lot."�Actually, that patience was really needed when I was having a mental breakdown in 2018, when I was juggling way too many things at once."�It was mostly real life related stuff that ended up leading to a few months of doing egg icons which were low effort but, kept me from being complacent."�Needless to say I'm very grateful for the chances Ame has given me to try to branch out in terms of creativity, and letting me take breaks for self care."kHopefully in the future there will be even more branching out, like trying my hand at music composing."OI'll probably stick around for future projects, or until Ame kicks me out."QHere's hoping my motivation and diet choices get better on the next project."�So I'm truly grateful for being in the right place and right time to be in the animation project. Some person on youtube did like a top 10 fangames video, I think?"3I just remember them being female and British."~Anyways, it was back in 2014, so it got lost in the thousands of top 10 pokemon fangame videos that have since been made."mI kind of wish I remembered the name so I could thank her for bringing me into this wonderful community.">As for what Reborn means to me, it's like a family to me."QEveryone in the dev team especially feel like the closest people in my life."~I'm an introvert so there's not a huge amount of friends outside of online, and it probably doesn't help that I talk too much."fSmeargle is named after the main character of one of my favorite books, "The Never Ending Story"."sIt's a name I tend to put into any game that lets me choose a name, either that or Rhiannon, my favorite song."The rest are named after Greek gods because of how interesting Greek myths are, even only knowing a fraction of the myths."..."VULPES: ...Oh, hi!"2Sorry, I was working on some animation stuff."6But I, uh... got a bit too caught up in it again."Did you want anything?"VULPES: Oh, sure!"&Which team did you want to fight?"?Oh, you won't get a BP for the animation team, by the way."RSince it's significantly easier to beat than the others, it wouldn't be fair."So which will it be?"Right!">Though if you'll humor me, I have a quick question first."+Which of these feels more vast to you?"*Which field did you want to fight on?"Okay, got it!"Sweetpea, if you would?"Not bad!"VULPES: Nice job!",Hope you enjoyed seeing the animations!"&VULPES: Hey, you did pretty well."'I'm sure you'll beat me next time!")And I hope you liked the animations!"Here's some BP."You have \v[593] now."(Oh, and about my question before..."@That was just our way of deciding what field we'd fight on."I know, it's a bit much."LBut Sweetpea here likes seeing people being surprised by her illusions,"?And what kind of trainer would I be if I didn't spoil her?"HBut now she's had her fun, so I can just ask straight up next time."Anything else?"PVULPES: Sure, if you want, though I'm not sure what to talk about honestly."<VULPES: So, I guess I should introduce myself properly."Hi, I'm Vulpes!"eI've been existing in Reborn's general vicinity since 2015, and I joined the team in early 2018."GI'm not really a people person though, so I've mostly just lurked."#I've also studied game design!"VI barely remember most of the course, but that was my first experience animating."WAnd I loved that part more than anything else we covered, so here I am, animating!"But word of advice?"IJust look up a syllabus and teach yourself, it's easier and cheaper."WThe only reason to even look at a course is to see what goes into game production."Anyway."RGetting involved in Reborn has taught me a lot, and it's been really fun too!"=And here's hoping any future projects are even more fun!"2So I started helping out with Reborn in 2018."ZI was checking a forum thread and Ame mentioned she was looking for another animator.":I really wanted to help with the game, since, well..."TReborn is probably the only reason I'm still interested in Pokémon in general."bI'd been a fan since I was five, maybe earlier, so Pokémon was a pretty big part of my life."cBut I started losing interest between BW2 and XY, and drifted away from the franchise by ORAS."EI don't know exactly why, but Reborn brought that interest back."oAnd I get extremely sentimental over everything, so having such a big part of my life revived like that..."It meant a lot."JAnyway, as I was saying, I really wanted to help out because of that.">But I was also convinced I would be a burden on the team."7I almost talked myself out of applying altogether." But I'm very glad I didn't."RThat choice is probably in the top three decisions I've ever made in my life."/Even so, it took a bit of getting used to."bAll my animation experience at the time was in 3D, and the technical stuff didn't carry over."RIt wound up with me thinking stuff like "Oh, a spiral will be easy to make!","'And then it would take me a month."0As opposed to like an hour in a 3D program."?Fun fact that is definitely not linked to this in any way:"YMy least favorite Pokémon is Shiinotic, and my least favorite move is Strength Sap."SBut I got better, and eventually even started using 3D to improve my 2D stuff."7Have you seen the Genesis Supernova animation yet?"hI made all the unique graphics for that by making a 3D reference pose to get the perspective right."g(I mostly just mentioned it because it's my favorite animation I've made and you should watch it.)"Actually, you know what?"Give me one... second..."There!"BI have a team on hand now with some of the animations I made!"DCan't have all of them because I made a fair number of Z-Moves,"SBut this is all I did for the game for like four years, I want to show it off."7But I've been working on other stuff recently too."TI also started helping with the code once we hit testing for the final episode!"lI had a little experience before that, but it was in a language that went out of use before I was born."So not exactly helpful."RBut then the animation editor started not letting you change things properly."2So I checked the code because why not, right?";And I saw a thing and said "hey is this breaking it?","PAnd Cass and Perry said "yeah that's it also you wanna help with the code","BAnd I said "sure sorry if I suck at first" and that was that."7And to this day I'm still messing up basic syntax."WI'm being dramatic, it's been two months at most, of course I'm not brilliant yet."0But I'm fine with that, baby steps and all."UAnd hey, you're using the password that was the first bit of code I implemented!"So I can't suck that bad!"@... Well, the first bit of code players will see, at least."XI made some changes to the animation editor first, but you probably won't see that."*VULPES: "But Vulpes," I hear you ask."KWhy do you have this option when you said you weren't a people person?"1Assuming you read the first option, that is."NThe answer is I just want an excuse to get a bunch of stuff off my chest."8And everyone here helped me deal with it, so there."`This is going to get kind of heavy, so here's a chance to back out if you're not up for it."5So, it might seem obvious from my other answers,"FBut I had pretty bad anxiety since even before I joined the team."@Probably with some moderate depression mixed in for flavor."ZI think it's been about five years, but thinking back I showed symptoms much earlier.">It wasn't exactly conductive to having a functional life."nFor most of the time I've been on the team, Reborn's been the only real anchor I've had to functionality."7Without the others, I'd have been a lot worse off."aAnd even now, when I'm starting to get better, they're helping me a lot just by being there.";With most people, I always felt pressured in some way."QEither by how I "should" act around them, or from the expectations they had."EIt'd be a lie to say I never felt like that around the others..."8But it was a lot less often than with other people."fAnd even when I did feel like that, after the first couple of months I could deal with it easier."nI wasn't able to actually talk very often, but at the same time I didn't feel guilty or "wrong" for that."`When the whole world tells you "socialise this, network that", even when it's impossible..."fHaving a space to exist with others, without having to worry about that stuff, was a big comfort."JAnd it's taken a while, plus some other help, but I'm not as bad now."LI'm able to talk to them without constantly panicking and overthinking."fEven if I'd started recovering without them around, I wouldn't be making nearly as much progress."`Instead of having two or three people I'm comfortable existing around, I have about twelve."GThere's only so many things you'll have in common with one person."LBut with different people, there's going to be different commonalities."6And it makes it that much easier to talk to them."TAnd maybe after that, eventually, you'll feel comfortable calling them friends."'And for everyone else on the team?"-I think I've finally reached that point."@So really, I owe the others my emotional health and sanity.">And also my existence outside of being the local cryptid.")Still plan on being that IRL though.".Give me a dog or cat over humans any day."0And hey, if any of this resonates with you?"DKnow that you're probably underestimating yourself as a person."/More people care about you than you think,"5And you're much less of a burden than you think."1I got caught up in those thoughts a lot too."But your brain is lying."=Even if you can't believe me right now, keep it in mind."-And I hope some day you will be able to."VULPES: Sure."Take care of yourself."$Okay, anything else you wanted?"*Anything else you want to talk about?"VULPES: Okay, see you!"CRIM: ...Oh, hi!",...Gosh, I never know what to say here."AUh, I guess I can just start with-- welcome to the dev room!"AIt's still kind of a trip for me to see myself in this room,"RFor a game that I've been playing and/or involved in for nearly half my life?"+But I'm immensely grateful regardless!"#I could gush a whole lot more,":But I'll save that for when I'm actually prompted to!"0Apologies in advance, I tend to talk a lot!"J...Anyways, hi! I'm Crimson, or Crim! But I usually go by the latter."It's lovely to meet you!"XCRIM: Hi, welcome back again! I hope you've been enjoying the rest of the dev room!"'And your adventure too, of course!"$Did you want to talk some more?"%...Or are you back for a battle?"What can I do for you?"/CRIM: Oh, you want to stay and chat a bit?"XJust as a heads-up, I never know what to say to these unless specifically prompted."0But I will talk your ear off if invited to!"EWhat's up? \ch[62,-1,Reborn,Game Involvement, Myself,Nevermind!]"-CRIM: Oh, you want to talk about Reborn?"Okay! Buckle up."OI ended up joining the team in early December of 2020, when I'd asked Ame,"DHey, so since we released Starlight, you want help with Reborn?"+And she was like, "Sure! Come aboard.""}I was over the moon. I already had a lot of love for the game-- I've got a massive soft spot for intricate storytelling."iThe characters, the story, the maps, the music, the world, all of it was just a pure serotonin rush."ZQuick commercial break: You should check out Starlight Divide, too! No bias, promise."VThere's a lot of love poured into that game already, and it's only a demo so far!";But to go back to your regularly scheduled emoposting,"mI was pretty starstruck about getting to work on a game I'd been playing for like, seven or eight years.""Honestly, I still kind of am!"9And as a bonus, it came with a bunch of cool people!"�Some of my closest friends are sitting right here in this room with me, or are people I've met through this game, and I'll always be forever grateful for that."/Both the community and its people, well..."`With the risk of sounding cheesy as heck, Reborn's probably-- definitely-- changed my life."|I was in a bit of a rough place before I'd first joined Starlight, and, well, both it and Reborn really helped me with that."`I really needed a change of scenery-- and Reborn gave me an outlet where that could happen."vI think some people kind of see me as "Oh, you're that person who's working on something dev-related constantly?""6Or, "Wait, how many fangames do you work on now?""SOr, "Hey, you've been on Aseprite for 4 days straight, do you need some help?""And like, true!"QBut it really just brings me the most massive amount of pure joy to work on."+And here we are, at the end of it all,"[Call me emotional, but I've definitely cried a few times while writing this whole bit."yI love this community, this game, and my friends dearly, and I'm grateful that they've stuck with me through it all."RIf I might be a little self-indulgent and quote my favorite Reborn character,"*What a happy ending I've fallen into."gCRIM: ...Whew, that was a lot. Sorry about that! Thanks for sticking around and listening, though."/I hope you enjoy the game as much as I do~"5Is there anything else you'd like to talk about?"GCRIM: Oh, you're curious about what I do for the game? Sure thing!"}So if you've been reading these in order, I mentioned before that I was originally pulled onto Reborn after Starlight's demo."hI was originally just a wee smol spriter on Starlight-- I just did the character overworld sprites."dWhen approaching Ame about Reborn, I was like, "Well, hey, I can offer support for spritework!""GOh, by the way, I'm also really interested in learning how to map."0And it kind of just... spiraled from there."UHonestly, at this point I'm struggling to remember what happened in what order--"�One of my first projects was when Ame asked me and Sam (that Smeargle over there!) about character backsprites for Mix 'n Match."nI got overexcited, and I think I ended up smashing out over twenty backsprites in like, less than a week."�I had a lot of fun coming up with poses that I thought would be fitting for each character! I also redid quite a few old backsprites as well."<By this point, minus those that already existed in E18,"LI think I've made most of the backsprites for the different characters?"�Spritework has been a pretty big part of my job here, mainly because it's what I'm comfiest with, but I dove into a lot of different categories!"�For this next section, I'll only mention certain things if you've completed their quest, as to not spoil anyone for something you might not have seen yet!"#So come back later and say hi!"#So for Celebi, to start with--"nTaube, Elena, and Shelly, along with the different maps in Celebi, were really my first big solo project."oI conceptualized, designed, and sprited all three of them, and I'm really proud of how they've turned out!"rFor Darkrai, PULSE Hypno and Camerupt were also mine in both design and sprites, along with the quest's maps!"SI know those two have been PULSE fights that people have been dying for, so...",I hope they've lived up to expectation!"1...So, standing here at the end of it all..."�There's a lot of different things for the different quests I've done, and I'd probably be here for several years if I tried to list it all."WNeoteric Isle, Zina's design and sprites, PULSE Arceus and Mime's overworlds, too!"9I remapped Apophyll Cave and Route 3's cave network!"AAnd all of the Pokémon Centers you see throughout the game!"�Oh, the Shaymin and Tao trio quests were also mine! Those two I'm particularly proud of, and I hope people enjoyed them as well!"{Anna's Dreamsick sprites are also a favorite-- they were sketched and done from scratch, and I'm really proud of them!";I hope they made for a fun and climactic final battle!"8Thanks for sticking through all the way to the end!"5CRIM: ...Okay, we're back from the conditionals?"+Basically, I've been all over the map."�I redid a huge chunk of Pokémon battler sprites-- mainly Gen 6 and 7-- and cleaned up a <i>lot</i> of NPC battle sprites-- a few main characters, too!"aI did a few move animations, including a Z-Move-- Psychic Fangs was my first ever animation!"�Jumped into writing dialogue near the end, too-- I helped with writing a little for the Nightclub and the Elite Four, as well as other random bits of dialogue here and there."<A bit of teambuilding, eventing, and puzzle design too!"AYou could say I'm probably somewhat of a jack of all trades?"Or an ace in the hole!"
Hehe."/Or at least I like to consider myself one!"Speaking of--"�If you've been around me for approximately ten seconds in the past year, you'll know that I am physically incapable of shutting up about Ace."VThey're one of the things ingame that mean the most to me, and I love them a lot."`If you're reading this from a save that's pre-E19 and haven't seen them, then....... oops!!")And you should go play early game!!!"iSame as with a few other characters, I designed and then sprited them, and I'm dearly proud of them."�I've probably said this about twenty times in this category alone, but I hope that others enjoy their presence ingame as much as I do!"CRIM: ...Okay! Uh."That was a lot!"�Honestly, it's a bit comical writing it all out like this, but it actually really means a lot to me that I've been able to do so many different things."FI count myself really lucky to be able to try so many new things."�I'm hugely grateful to Ame not just for trusting me with handing me all these different things to do, but also just the opportunity to do them at all."�She and Cass have been a huge support in both personal life and dev, have helped me try things out of my comfort zone-- and been patient with me if I screwed up said things, too!"DI think that about covers it for things I've done for the game!"EBut like, if you want an exhaustive list of <i>everything</i>..."Hit me up sometime!"WCRIM: Okay, I know I just said that I don't know what to say to these, but like..."9I <i>really</i> don't know how to talk about myself."/Let me at least introduce myself properly."Uh... hi!"I'm Crim!"eAs of the time of writing this, I'm in my last quarter of college, and I'm in my early twenties."RIf you've seen me around the server, you might know me better as, let's see--".That person who speaks in 50% cat emotes."-Or uses way too many exclamation points!"9I'm a Communications major, with a minor in Theater."8I've been around the community since... early 2019?"SEven then, I only really became active when joining Starlight dev in mid 2020."`Before that though, I'd still been playing Reborn! I started in E6! So about... 2013? 2014?"dI regret that I hadn't been able to find the community-- not just the game-- sooner than I did,"*But better late than never, you know?"�I've got a whole category dedicated to Reborn, so assuming you're reading these in order, you've already read about my experience with it!"6But as for what it really means to me personally?"jI'm going to take a leaf out of Vulpes' book, and just roll out the yellow caution tape really quick."dIt's currently 4:34 AM, so I'm a little more emotional than normal-- which is saying something."WSo if you're not up for it, please take the opportunity to back out if you'd like!"CRIM: Alrighty."|So this is probably evident either from the rest of my dialogue-- or if you've spent more than a few minutes around me,"HBut I've had a pretty severe case of anxiety-- for a long time now."I hold myself as a person and my work to a really high standard, and tend to overthink and spiral over this to an extreme."�This was especially prevalent when working on Reborn-- I'd freeze up at the thought of even starting something, out of fear I'd mess it up."OOr couldn't live up to some arbitrary expectation that I'd set for myself."1It was the sort of thinking that was like..."aThis is really going to be in Reborn? This is the big leagues now, it <i>has</i> to be good."ZSo I'd get extremely hung up on the tiniest of details and paralyze myself over them."�It was the same with interaction-- I struggled with feeling as if I couldn't meet a standard of simply existing in a space without feeling as if I was intruding or in the way."rI tend to worry about others over myself often, and want to make sure people are comfortable and happy, so..."3It was kind of a constant presence in my head."\Honestly, I'd be lying to myself if I said it wasn't a problem I'm still fighting with."cBut Reborn itself, especially the dev server and the friends within it-- has really helped me."mIt was a comfort to have a space where I could just be, without getting caught up in intrusive thoughts.")Baby steps, but we're getting there."KI certainly wouldn't be making the same progress as I am without them."EA friend sent me a song once-- one of its lyrics goes like this:"GLife is not the things that we do, it's who we're doing them with."And... yeah."bLike, Reborn's been an unforgettable experience to work on-- wouldn't trade it for the world."PBut everyone on the team has really made that journey all the more special."*Ame, for inviting me on this journey,"HAnd everyone else in this room with me, and even those who aren't--"8It really wouldn't have been the same without them,"4And I'm proud to call all of them dear friends."NCRIM: And well, if any of this happens to be relatable to anyone reading?"WKnow that you're not alone, and you deserve to give yourself a little more credit.":People care for you and love you more than you think."fIf you're struggling with doing the things that you want to do-- it's okay to give yourself time."PSurround yourself with people that see you as the joy you are to be around,"BAnd treat you with the same kindness and love as you deserve."8Of course, it's not something that comes overnight.";I know I get caught up in those kinds of thoughts too."kBut I hope that someday-- if that day isn't today-- you'll be able to see just how brightly you shine."3...Would you like to talk about anything else?"CRIM: Of course.""Please take care of yourself!""I hope you have a lovely day~",Or night, whenever you're reading this!"%CRIM: Oh? You're approaching me?"+Okay, but I'm more prepared this time!">I'll have you know, I'm still kind of awful at this game!"That has not changed!"(...But you know how I can fix that?"With a big heckin' sword!"Let's go!!"2Aww, shoot. I'll be sure to ace it next time~""CRIM: Okay, sorry, um, heck--" That wasn't in the cards--?"(I'm proud of you though, great job!":Here, I'll fix up your team and you can have some BP."+...And, hey, as a gift from me to you!"Just this once!"Here's a few extra BP!"As a treat."8You've come this far, and honestly, you deserve it!"*That brings you to... \v[593] BP now!";CRIM: ...Oh. I wasn't expecting to actually win there."'That's okay though, you did great!"Let me fix up your team."(You've definitely got it next time!"Oh, and by the way?"#I hope that my Vulpix got you!"CRIM: Okay!"2Fair warning, I'm kind of awful at this game!"\But when you're allowed to give a team of just your favorite Pokémon a little... help?"Even I can stand a chance!"...Hopefully."Bring it!" CRIM: Alrighty, no problem!"/I hope you enjoy the rest of the dev room~"#And the rest of the game, too!"5I'm glad that you were able to make it this far."All the way to the end!"_I hope you've been able to make as many fond memories from this game as I've been able to."$Some days, they're all we have."5You've still got some great things ahead of you!"ZI hope you have-- or are able to make-- as many fond memories from this game as I do."rAUTUMN: Oh, hi there! Welcome to the Dev Room! This is uhh.. I guess where we all just kinda relax and chill?"yIt's rough out there in this great wide region, though I suppose we have you to thank for fixing that up a bit, huh?"So! What can I do for you?"fA battle? All right, I'll have you know I competed in a tournament against everyone in this room!"I placed..."Dead last."So I grabbed a cool sword!"Maybe another time, then?"�AUTUMN: Okay fine! Here, I was saving these for another Explosion TM from Sinnoh that I've heard lowers the opposing Pokémon's defense..."$But, I guess you can have them."#That'll put you at \v[593] BP."<AUTUMN: Oof, I didn't expect I'd actually win, haha...."jHonestly I'm not the greatest at battling. Just pretty good at finding funny ways to cheese the game."|We're actually about to have a tournament in this room to see who's actually the best! I just hope I don't come last..."<Hopefully this will be good practice! Don't hold back!!"{I have a strict rule to never talk about myself unless prompted, and while I understand that you clicked the chat button..."0You're just gonna have to be more specific!"aUm, please? \ch[62,-1,Who are you?,What do you do?,What does Reborn mean to you?,Nevermind.]"CAUTUMN: Well, as you may have already read, my name is Autumn!"[Though, if you're an older member of the community, you might know me better as Inuki."jYeah, that Inuki. Of Porygon2 bridge fame. Alas, that was a few genders and plenty of life lived ago."qOutside of that... Who am I? Heck if I know, but here! I'll give you 5 fun facts instead of a proper answer!"`Fact 1: You see that dude sitting a tile away from me? His positioning isn't a coincidence!"THe's been my best friend for literally more than half of my life! (I'm 27 btw.)"�The butterfly effect is silly to think about. Stepping on a butterfly just makes you rude, it's highly improbable anything will come of it."[But meeting him? That's the event that really kicked off every other event in my life."SAnswering who I am is literally impossible without mentioning his involvement."II love you, fam. Thanks for all your help in paving the road I walk."2Fact 2: Mega Diancie is my favorite Pokémon!"WFact 3: Once, while programming something involving field effects way back when...".Like, a few episodes after they came out."{I forgot that case statements existed and instead created a nested if statement that contained no less than 30 "end"s."#All lined up at the end of it.".Fact 3.5: I was a computer science major."	Was."UFact 4: My appearance here is based on my Dungeons and Dragons character: Deneb!"�She's currently an Archfey warlock who gained the favor of a bunch of fae butterflies, eventually revealed to be her father's old swarm!"vHe was kind of a jerk and maybe so are they? Being a jerk seems to be a trait of that side of the family, though."....Anyway....."XThe tiny child on the couch closer to the back is the DM of that campaign actually!"kI've used it a lot to get comfortable with referring to myself with different pronouns over the years."xBut more importantly it's a really good story! It's been a blast to cooperatively write it with them every session!"PFact 5: I find it very likely that I have a fairly severe case of the ADHD."~This isn't anything particularly groundbreaking, and by the time the game releases this question will have been answered."YWe'll see if I remember to come back and fix this, or if it stays like this forever.":Phew, okay! Is there anything else you wanted to ask?"#All right, a different prompt!"3Gotcha, please enjoy the rest of the dev room!"?Precious little, compared to everyone else in this room..."�The more interesting answer is that I'm one of the move animators. I make the funny pictures move when you click buttons in battle."~I word it like this because I do not create the funny pictures that do the moving. I have no real artistic ability whatsoever."yI don't have the ability to visualize images in my head. I can't see what something will look like without doing it."KI have very strong opinions on how I want the moves I animate to feel."mUnfortunately this makes me remarkably unproductive when I can't put that feeling to paper, so to speak."gThat mixed with my terrible work ethic definitely led me to be the least productive member by far."�When I do finally make something though, I try to put my whole heart into it! I hope that shows, especially during Full Power Z-Moves!"6Anyway, is there anything else you wanted to ask?"|So if you're reading these in order, you may notice that I seemed pretty bummed about my relative lack of contribution."NPerhaps that's just a natural reaction, a way anybody like me might feel."iBut I feel that way because I absolutely love this game, and, at least my memories of the community."�So back in the day, right? My best friend and I were scrolling through Pokémon Online servers, trying to find an enjoyable place."KAs you may be aware of, not all communities are welcoming to everyone."QIt just so happens that my favorite anime is called "Katekyo Hitman Reborn!""USo when I came across a server with Reborn in its name, monkey brain went click."8What a marvelous coincidence that turned out to be."oA few years pass, Ame starts making a cool game, I play it as you do. I don't really think anything of it."nThe details are blurry, but my first act as a "Dev" was filling in the pages of the Field Effect Library."[Basically cooking up 100 pots of copypasta and draping the noodles into digital books."kIt was a good time, I enjoyed feeling helpful! Eventually I simply became a general purpose assistant."`Were there a thing to do that wasn't particularly complicated, I would be the one to do it!"tLike making a bunch of cliffs, remaking Route 2 three times, calculating how much soup could fit in a mountain."OAme, Dan, and I were in a Skype call regularly. It was a really good time!"|Eventually the animation:tm: project started cause the animations that came with essentials were, how you say... weirdchamp."pI remember Ame had already made a few that were really sick but then her hand decided to be a bit dramatic."#So she showed me how to do it!"So I started doing it!"jAnd now here I am! Incredibly grateful for the opportunity that Ame has given me to work on her game."UAnd incredibly grateful for the home her community has been for the past........"Very long time."5I hope it's a significantly longer time to come."<AUTUMN: Oh, okay! Enjoy the rest of the dev room, then!"kAUTUMN: Oh,\| right,\| yeah,\| sure,\| of course.\| Hey, before you go, what's your favorite Pokémon?"9AUTUMN: 3...\| 2...\| 1...\| Andddd...\.\.\. Bang.\|"-No idea what you put in that text box.\|"*But it's removed from the game now.\|"$I hope being rude was worth it.">:["AJAN: Hi! Hello! Bet you didn't think you'd see me down here?"AI mean, yeah, technically this isn't <i>really</i> my world."7Well, technically I've been to this world first..."$Um... Forget about all of that!"JAN: So, what do you need?"8JAN: Oh... Yeah, we do that in this world don't we?"WBattling? Um, admittedly I'm not the best at that. I'm still an intern, after all!"But I'll do my best!">:C"JAN: Fuck."+Okay, okay... You win fair and square."EI'll have my revenge on you yet. Maybe not in this world, but..."ASomewhere, someplace, the cycle of suffering will never end."`We'll play forever and ever and ever and ever until we get the ending we're satisfied with."Karma's a bitch."=JAN: All right, enough of that. You have \v[593] BP now.";JAN: This is just the lemonade stand all over again..."=JAN: You wanna chat? Sure! What do you wanna chat about?"JAN: Yeah. That's my lore."4Right now I'm a senior at Axis High University."EI'm required to take up an internship job before I can graduate."BBut between you and me... None of that really matters anyway."NIt's a way to "tie up loose ends" and justify my existence in this world."That's one of the rules, right? If there's no justification for my existence then I'll just disappear into little bitty pixels."EYou look confused? I think I have that effect on people a lot..."5Well, don't try to think about it too much, yes?""JAN: Ooh, you were listening!"6Okay, so that's half truth. I am from this world!"2In fact, it's where I was born. Conceptually."YBut eventually, after some time I was able to leave using the process of "blooming".";I bloomed! After that I left and created my own world."Technically..."AIt wasn't all me. I have friends who came with me and stuff."EHey, what's that look for? You act as if I'm talking nonsense...">All of this makes sense, trust me. I wouldn't lie to you."mJAN: Admittedly, I stole this option from Cass because I think a lot of what she says applies to me too."WBut I think it's sort of an understatement to say that Reborn has changed my life."EI was sort of aimless and without purpose before I found Reborn."oThen I saw how much work Ame put into this world and I decided I wanted to try and apply myself similarly."KThat's how I was able to "bloom" and create the world of Rejuvenation."tThat bloom wasn't exactly pretty... A lot of my early attempts were met with some backlash and stuff like that."7It was my first time creating a new world, jeez..."TI had no idea creating an entirely new line of existence would be so much work."EIt took a lot of time, but I think I got the hang of things now.">I guess you could say I owe everything to Ame and Reborn."My internship is ending..."XJAN: That answer changes a lot. At first it was Dusclops, then it was Chandelure..."FRight now as of uh... January 23rd 2022 at 10:23 pm it's Claydol."IJAN: Have you been to Aegir Cave? You've definitely been to Iolia..."?Well, those two areas are what pop into my mind right now."1I really hope I'm not forgetting anything..."JAN: Cya."IKARU: Oh, uh, sorry."gI sometimes find myself looking back on everything that brought me here, and I space out a little.".It's just a lot to think about, you know?"\Every choice I've made, however small, nudging me a little in one direction or another."WLike a visual novel, but, you know, for real, and without the relationship points."v... Or maybe with them! Just don't try Blue Moon Ice Cream on real people as a shortcut. It takes more than that."Anyway, I'm Ikaru. I do the little stuff that people COULD do themselves, when their time is better spent on things I can't do."jI also play new versions of the game before most people, when they're the most broken, so that's fun."bThere's a chance you're not here to listen to my musing though, so I'll leave that up to you."RIKARU: Hi again. Want to talk for a bit? Or maybe you're just here to battle?"eIKARU: Sure thing. I told Ame that I would try not to write too much, but, once I get into it..."gWell, Ikaru from the future that has finished writing these is here to warn you, there's... a lot."mWhat sounds most interesting? \ch[62,-1,Pre- Reborn,Early Reborn and League,Game Involvement,Reflection]"5The olden times, huh. Sure. So, full disclosure:"�I'm just going to pretend that I don't know that Autumn over there will have said the exact same things that I'm going to say here at one point or another.""Fun fact for the class first:"�Before I started going by Ikaru, I had a different alias, well over like, 13 years ago now. And I know, that's not a very fun fact by itself, but..."FSay, have you ever fought the Grand Hall trainers on a Wednesday?"ESpecifically, the one with the Xatu and (Mega-)Mawile from hell?"xThe one who says some cryptic "you don't know who I am" stuff? Psychic Silva? Yeah, that's me. Or, well, it WAS me."�But hold on, before you start accusing me of stealing your childhood crush's first kiss or something out of some war-flashback-esque anger,"xI didn't make those teams, it was just stuff I liked that needed to be seen in-game... somewhere. Sorry, not sorry!"�That aside: my earliest internet days in middle school were spent on the Serebii forums, writing a really bad Pokemon fanfiction, which,"Hopefully,"pWill never see the light of day again. If you know, you know, and if you don't, well, it's better that way."�So like I said, this was in middle school. I had a few friends on the forums, kind of, but not many of them stuck around long term because of course not."�There was one, though, that I knew irl too, and- well, actually, "stuck around" isn't a good phrase for him either, more like he..."^... suddenly reappeared in Reborn, out of thin air in the left field like 10 years later?"�And that by itself is wild to me, like, I live by the phrase "timing is everything" and all our choices yada yada I said that already,"�But the degree to which we were completely different people than we were back then is staggering. We weren't even THAT close, but,"bIf you happen to be reading this, shoutout to you, friend. I'm glad we both made it this far."�So, next came the Marriland forums. I put myself out there a bit more, and wrote less (read: wrote no) fanfiction. I dabbled a little in competitive Pokemon."hThis was 4th gen, and I was just starting to be less uptight about "super broken" overused Pokemon."�(And, like, good for me because I was missing out on so many cool things in favor of... *checks notes* ... Swords Dance Quick Attack Zangoose.)"�On a fateful July afternoon in 2007, I was scrolling the "wi-fi battles" subforum and the thread I chose to respond to was the start of everything."EThe thread starter was someone who... Ah, what were her words..."JA few genders and plenty of life lived later, is now known as Autumn."ZThe green one a single tile away from here, yeah. That placement is very intentional."�We became real good friends using our Nintendo DS wi-fi, even when she had to hide the fact that she was friends with strangers online from her mom."And, like, fair."Eventually she invited me to her own forum for her friends, which, when I joined, had a staggering two (2) active members."�We hung out there all the time, doing whatever we wanted with whatever nonsense topics and stuff because it was pretty much just the two of us."�She invited more and more people and we had a fun little group that did battling, roleplaying, art, children's card games, you name it."}One of the people she invited was her friend Wolfie, and if you know me well enough, you already know the significance there."�If you don't, just know that she's a blessing. A past version of me might argue that I don't deserve her, and that past version of me is wrong,"5Though I do my best to be worth it all the same."�It is no small exaggeration to say that those two are the single (uh, double?) most important people in my life and I would not be where I am now without them."zI love them both dearly and I'm glad that they've stuck around through everything. I couldn't ask for better friends."@...Whew. Sorry, I'm sure you weren't expecting all of that.""Thanks for listening, though."&Want to talk about anything else?"+My early Reborn experience, huh? Sure."JWould you believe me joining this community was entirely an accident?"9Ah, well, maybe a better term is "misunderstanding.""�You see, Autumn and I are fans of the anime "Katekyo Hitman Reborn!" and when we first made the switch from NetBattle to Pokemon Online,"All the way back in 2010,"ZWe saw a server that was named "Reborn Server" and we didn't think too hard about it."4YOOOOOO it's Reborn we said, joining instantly."$Best mistake we made that year."yThe League was already a thing when we joined, though the server was still a tiny baby compared to what we have now."�I signed up pretty instantly for funsies with a team that was... questionable. I remember my first battle was actually pretty significant."�Not for me though, for Hardy. Titania was newly revealed and he said that if he won his next battle, he would go challenge her next."dYanno, as he does, trying to prove Rock-types can still hold up to the all-powerful Steel-type."gAnd I was the unlucky sucker that thought shit was sweet, with a pretty weak team, and got Rocked."	Heh."�Then I made a better team and fought Corey, and to say he was a stark contrast to my last opponent is an understatement. Both in character and difficulty."\Cal was next, and I got slapped, then I rematched Hardy and won. Rematched Cal and won."�Next was Florinia. And boy did she beat me up for a long while. A battle between us was the 666th log, fun fact. Eventually I fought Heather instead,"6Who, by the way, was an entry leader at the time,"�And won first try. And let me tell you, I was the ONLY one who did. The fact that she's part of the Elite Four in this game is not coincidence."�Her rank shot up real shortly after that, and first of all, my trainer card looked real funny with all the empty space between her badge and the rest."gAnd man, the relief I felt knowing I didn't have to fight her again after she stepped it up, haha."VI interacted with the leaders pretty often, and some had more to say than others."eBy far my favorite group was none other than the OTS gang; Titania, Florinia, Amaria, and Julia."gI built up a bit of a reputation as a knight in not-so- shining armor, no points for guessing why."\The interactions I had with Titania and Amaria were like, the talk of the whole league."And then there was El."�Let's just say I'm glad I never have to fight him again. My team had Dragon Dance Dragonite as a win condition and it backfired every time."&Can't stand Ditto anymore hahaha."}I sure gave it to him in the X-League though. Resorted to a Chilan Berry on my Darkrai to survive Arceus and put it to sleep."]I got really into everything and it was a blast. I was the second one to win the league!"lHave you done the spirit hunting quest in Victory Road? If you did, then you saw my team at some point."�If you ask me if I regret it, knowing what I know now... Nah, definitely not. I feel like my own character developed as much as any of the leaders' did."�Nowadays I'm a lot more relaxed, I think, but there's always a little bit of Titania chilling under the surface for whenever I need her to come out."$... Not that it needs to. Much."�Anyway, I'd say the League was definitely one of the highlights of my experience. Hopefully you enjoyed the little trip down memory lane."-My involvement with the game, huh? Sure."�Well, like I said when I introduced myself, I mostly do a lot of small, boring stuff that other people can definitely do themselves."{Difference between them and me is I don't know how to do all that much, so the really cool stuff is best left to them."ZFull transparency, this event is like the only eventing I've done in the entire game."�Uh, well, unless you count scattering hidden items in the new city and the Chrysolia Spring. But that was just copying and pasting events, really."�Speaking of the spring, though, I filled in all the walls there once Ame laid down the outline. I did that for a few maps, actually."?A couple of the mountains in the desert were my doing too."ZAnd let's see... There's also the Tanzan Depths, the maps in the cave in Tanzan Cove."�That was also the one time I had a little fun and left something funny that no one will see unless they open up the map in RMXP or something."�I think my favorite niche talent is the power to find double spaces in text. When I first joined the dev server, I made my name "melee marth player,""3Because my attention to spacing is IMMACULATE."jTo be clear, when I say "double space" I mean the difference between "this phrase" and "this phrase.""�I can also tell when Pokemon names have a space before them, when the nicknaming window puts one there automatically for... some reason."�Outside of actual work on the game, I also play the game! The wild west versions where maybe everything works and maybe it doesn't!"�During my testing of E19, my Palkia was named "no." and my Dialga was named "yes!" because I had a 2 hour struggle with Palkia and then Dialga was like,"cOkay, I'll get in the frame 1 Quick Ball I guess, and Dialga was the one I wanted more anyway!"(Hopefully it's easier for you guys."�Aside from that, I try to keep reported bugs listed in our Official(tm) Cat(tm) Reporting Spreadsheet so that it's at least organized."3Honestly, huge shoutout to everyone else here."vThe difference in that spreadsheet when everything that's "Done" is hidden compared to how much has been on it..."�It's like night and day. The bugs- ah, cats, never stop, but looking back on everything that didn't work before that does now is insane.";Remember to show your appreciation for everyone, okay?"ZReflection... Well, I'm no Serra, but I sure do think about this kind of thing a lot."nI like music a lot, which isn't particularly unique or anything, but it plays into a lot of my character."qIn places like your generic "About Me"s and, like, status messages and all that, I quote songs all the time."RIf we're friends on Final Fantasy XIV, my search info is always a song quote."DThere's a few lyrical quotes here and there even in this event."�The placeholder dialogue Ame left here for my pre- battle message was a joke about that, since it's so ingrained into my personality haha."�My biggest inspiration is the Japanese musician Aimer. I really love the celestial themes and late night vibes in her earlier music."kIt was a tweet from her in 2018 that really motivated me to get up and finish my college registration."�She said "I wonder if some of you started a new life today" among other things, and I read that and thought "yeah, okay." So I did!"kMy college major was always astronomy, but discovering someone like her really solidified my interest.":My favorite song is, perhaps unsurprisingly, Polaris."�It's sad, but at the same time, motivational. And it's always- ... well, usually, the melancholy stuff that hits me the hardest."uI say "usually," because it's not my FAVORITE song, but LIGHTS's "Timing Is Everything" is, like, my life motto."cThe chorus of the song says "There I was, none the wiser, both of us, different trajectories,""PWho'd have thought we'd be right here, in this spot, timing is everything.""4And it just makes me think. Despite everything,"AThe hundreds of thousands of years that humans have existed,"<You and I are here in the same place, at the same time."IUh, well, same "place" and same "time," but don't sweat the details."�Everything we are is just a huge combination of wacky coincidences, or, like, such small choices. If I hadn't met Autumn in 2007, I wouldn't be here now."BIf I hadn't signed up for the League, I wouldn't be here now."XIf Ame hadn't succumbed to her whims and made a game, none of us would be here now." But we are. Isn't it great?"^I, for one, am glad you're here and hopefully enjoying yourself. Stick around, won't you?")IKARU: Ah. To the death it is, then."... Just kidding!"OYou've been through a lot to get where you are now, haven't you, Champion?"7Did you get what you wanted out of your adventure?"GI'm glad to hear it. I hope the same is true of your next journey."CWell, there's not always some deeper meaning, and that's okay."VHere you stand, at the end of a journey 10 years in the making. You've done well."]With your quest said and done, how about a little something with no stakes to wind down?":And yet, there's even more out there waiting for you."]When we're finished here, make sure you see things all the way through for me, will you?"6And when that's done, tell me your favorite part!"-(Bonus points if it's this interaction!)"IKARU: Round two, huh?"'You'll touch the stars in no time."KI did my Adrienn impression already, but the sentiment is still there."Just a little higher..."*Morning waits on the edge of a dream."HIKARU: I expect no less from someone who's come as far as you have."1Here's some Battle Points for your troubles."rAnd hey, you know what, there's only two people here that I don't outrank, and they can't tell me what to do."{Here's one (1) more, just this once. You've come so far, and frankly, these battles are a little stacked against you, haha."1That brings you to... \v[593] points, is it?"wIKARU: Well, teams of just our favorites weren't really going to stand up to endgame players without some... help."aI'll get your squad all fixed up, and if you have any complaints, I'm innocent; Cass did it!"IKARU: Alright."8Hey, if you ever get lost, just look up at the sky."8If you can see the stars, they'll show you the way."1Your next meeting is just around the corner.";MARCELLO: Hi there, I'm Marcello, I work on this game."QDo not believe the sprite I have been given for the purposes of bullying me,"0I am not, in fact, a child with green hair."So, what's up?"7MARCELLO: I'm pretty terrible at Pokémon, myself."UBut turns out, when you can just cheat and make your team utter unfair bullshit?"3Even I can come up with something pretty good."Bring it on!"#MARCELLO: Good job, have a BP!"x...I feel like these dev fights are probably way too difficult to reward just 3 BP, but that's just how things are."You've got \v[593] BP now."7MARCELLO: Hey, don't worry, we all lose sometimes."-If I can offer some constructive advice."&That thing you did in our battle?"CWhere you let all your mons' HP go to zero before my mons' HP?"#Yeah, don't do that next time."Should help you win.".MARCELLO: You want to know more about me?"(Well sure, if you insist. Ask away!"MARCELLO: I'm Marcello!"ESome random British guy that tripped and fell onto the Dev Team."hOnce upon a time, I was the newest member of the team, I felt like a kid compared to everyone else.">(Speaking of, despite the sprite, I'm not a kid. I'm 25.)"W(Ame, who is SHORTER THAN ME, liked to tease me about my height once upon a time.)"�(I have no idea about the exact joke origins, it was forever ago but hey I ended up with a child's sprite, we all have to live with this now.)"Anyway, tangent aside."/That time I was the 'new kid' on the team?"Was seven years ago."KI have worked on this game my entire adult life, which is crazy to me."SAnd with any luck, I can continue working to make games with Ame and the team,"(For the rest of my adult life, too."!Did you want to ask me more?"All right, see you around.",MARCELLO: Oh, well I'm a mathematician."?...But I assume you mean with regards to this game, right?"7Well, when I first started it was as a programmer!"gI knew nothing about that kind of thing though, but I learnt on the job and fixed a bunch of bugs."nAnd all in all wrote lots and lots of code that Cass or Perry or myself would eventually have to rewrite." Because it sucked real bad.":But I like to think I got pretty good over the years."$I got the online stuff working!"&I fixed numerous persistent bugs!"dWhen we completely rewrote the AI, I was the one that programmed that (though Ame designed it)."EAll these big things I've done have something in common, though."sIn the last year or so, Cass or Perry have completely redone my work in these areas and made them much better."And I couldn't be happier!"xI like to think I provided a good starting point, and seeing some incredibly talented team members improve on that,"7To make stuff that seems to work pretty damn well!"{I find that very cool, and I can't help but be proud of myself and even more proud of this amazing team I'm a part of."(But programming isn't all I can do!"TThis last year of development, I had to step back for a bit because of illness.",(Don't worry, reader, all is well now.)"_And when I got back I was out of practice, not to mention that Cass and Perry are so cool,"MThere wasn't too much even left to do on the programming side of things."2But turns out this nerd quite enjoys writing."QAnd I like to think I'm pretty good at it-- something which Ame agrees with!"KSo for the last segment of development I was writing dialogue instead!"PMy biggest contribution is the Celebi Quest, if you've played that already."3That was designed, evented, and written by me!"P(Lots of thanks to Crim and Ame for the graphical assets ur both great. <3)"-I even made all the battle teams for it!"gBut I've also done other bits throughout postgame, small bits in other quests, among other things."uI'm sure I could tell you more about the other things I worked on specifically, but that would take long enough,"4We'll just say that's a story for another time."xRegardless, writing for the game and seeing the other developers (and hopefully players like you) enjoy my writing,"&Has given me huge amounts of joy!"[I'm so excited that everyone can finally play the game and see the work I put into it!"6I think that pretty much covers my contributions!"MARCELLO: I mean, so much."SEven before I was a developer, I've met so many cool people in this community."^Most of my closest friends are either on this dev team, or were met because of this game."iCall me a big nerd if you want, but I also got really into Dungeons and Dragons thanks to this game."|At this point I've been DMing a campaign for two years whose players have almost exclusively been people I know from Reborn."jShoutout to Ame and Autumn who are both players in the game and are deeply chaotic in their doing so."XAnd have taken it upon themselves to ensure none of my plans ever come to fruition."xBut also my other players who aren't on the team, and people who played in the group in the past but don't anymore?"yKnow that I deeply love and appreciate you all, these last two years have been infinitely better because of you all."And I owe that to Reborn.".I like to think I owe so very much to it."dSo many of the people in this room are some of my best friends, and they're all just wonderful!"bPlus, being in such a supportive community around such great people for the last seven years,":I feel like has shaped me into the person I am today."And I like that person!"lSo I couldn't be more grateful to have been a part of all this, and treasure the friendships I've made."pHere's to the next seven years of my time knowing and working with Ame being just as rewarding as the last."GMARCELLO: I feel deeply unqualified to give advice about anything."But I'll try my best!"JIf you struggle to do the things you want to, don't beat yourself up."�I've spent a lot of time on this team going back and forth between incredibly rapid productivity and paralyzing indecision and inaction."�But I made it, and things got a lot better when I stopped beating myself up every time I felt like I wasn't doing 'good enough'."!I'm sure you'll make it too.";But more than anything, my number one piece of advice?"-Just surround yourself with good people."aPeople you like, people you respect, people you admire, and people you wish to be more like."UIt was entirely accidental, but that's what I did when I joined the Reborn team."bAnd I think, more than anything, that is what lead me to all the best parts of my life today."gI've grown into a person I like, I have wonderful friends, and most importantly of all, I'm happy."GAnd I feel like I owe all of that to the wonderful friends I have."1...Yeah, sorry, if you were hoping for like,".Fangame dev specific advice or something,"
Oops."LBut this is what you get from me, and I hope somebody finds it helpful!"mA notebook with "Noir a blanc" written on the cover is on the desk. The last written page is bookmarked."
Lire?"December 18th, 2021"XIt's been a while, hasn't it? Progress has been kind of slow lately, regrettably..."aBut I'm still further along than I would have ever been without your accidental inspiration."2When I go outside at night, in total silence,"[My surroundings lit by nothing more than a few street lights, the moon, and the stars,"3I think of you and your music, and I remember.",You may never know it, but that's okay."uAs long as it motivates me, it doesn't really matter. And maybe someday, I might be able to thank you properly.""PERRY: Hey, hey!" Look who finally showed up."So, what you wanna do?"MPERRY: I can't decide between singles or doubles. So I'll let you choose"ZOh, fun fact! I made the function that temporarily sets your pokémons levels to 100."[But it doesn't set the opponents pokémon to lvl 100, we just have the teams that way.": )"*That's what I expect from our protag!"%PERRY: Nice one! Here's some BP."That puts you at \v[593]."+I hope the AI didn't misplay too hard.">PERRY: Oof, did the lvl 101 thing mess you up that badly?"8PERRY: Sure, I'll think up something to talk about."]Anything specific you want to talk about? \ch[62,-1,Reborn,Game dev, Me, Ramblings, Nah]"/PERRY: Man, there's so much to talk about."/Starting with my introduction to the game."eIt started by watching someone play through the game on Youtube, pkmnRob I think their name was.";Thought it was neat so decided to check it out myself."[I played a few hacked ROMs before, but this was my first time playing on the computer."kAnd then I got my ass handed to me in true Reborn fashion. The one pokémon strat didn't work anymore."EAfter that I just kept on playing, basically no-living the game."POne of the things I love about the game is just how multidimensional it is."nIt's not only about the story, or the battling. It has puzzles, beautiful maps, many sidequests and more."ZAnd I think the game has made me a bit of a better person. Not that I was bad before."MBut I think I came out of it a bit more compassionate and understanding."tI ended up hanging around and checking up on the game every once in a while, playing the updates that came out."6And then Cass made a post about the battle tower."kA person in the comments asked if there would also be a battle factory, a gamemode I enjoy myself too."dCass responded that she'd think it cool, but it would be too much effort to make it worthwhile."+My ego showed up, and went like: "Bet""�It's a miracle, but somehow I actually managed to get it to work.Part of it is the coding language, Ruby. It's pretty easy to pick up, not a lot of foreknowledge required."}So when I almost finished the battle factory I showed it off in the patreon server. Was planning to release it as a mod."kCass said she wanted it in the main game, so I polished it up a bit and sent everything needed for it."nHelped with a few other things, and a while later she asked me if I actually wanted to help out as a dev."*I really have a lot to thank her for."XAfter entering the team I met a lot of awesome people, which are here in this room."(And it has been an awesome journey."-PERRY: But what is it I did in the game?"LIf you're reading in order you know that Cass asked me on the dev team."^That's because all the bugs that had been found after e18 was released had been compiled."_And it was a long list. So to help Marchello, and Azery at the time, out I was brought on."�Like 10 days later I found a way to test where the code takes longest to run. 2 days after that e18.4 was released and optimization galore was a fact."�Cass ran with it way further than I could take it, but I've been making sure things don't crash after she had sledgehammered them."SSo most of the work I've done has just been bugfixing and fixin up after Cass."9But of course, there are also new things I've added!"fThe battle factory, a lot of AI rewrite, online doubles, new field notes, are just a few of them."�It's hard to remember them all, since about 90% of them are just small QoL things. Like the game staying in the same place and speedup persisting when resetting."wThat's about it, really. Most of the work i do isn't visible, since it's not a new thing but fixing the old thing."UPERRY: Hi, I'm Perry or toothpastefairy which isn't really a name I use anymore."1Living that good life at the ripe age of 23."NAnd a masters student studying Applied Physics living in the Netherlands."�Probably addicted to playing chess, since the amount of times I stopped writing all this dialogue and played a quick game online has hit the double digits."jThere's a good chance this is the first time you hear of me, I'm not involved in the community a lot."TSometimes I wish I was, but it's just not something that comes naturally to me."�Meeting new communities and friend groups is always scary, and if the circumstances are not up for it you won't get many words out of me."hI'm sure you have felt like that too a few times, like when going to a new school or maybe a party."|Especially starting a conversation. You'll catch me dead before I talk about myself unprovoked. Unless you're counting this."qBut mostly i don't sweat that stuff too much, it's not who I am to do that and in the end I can accept that."9Anyhow, another thing about me is that I love music!"}High chance that if I'm alone at home, I'm with my headphones on. Not that I have a particularly refined taste in music."\I'm pretty sure that it is as close to basic as you can get, but I enjoy it nontheless."zLike the e4 and champion battle tracks. Absolute bangers, those two. Deffo give them a listen if you haven't already."vOther than that my view of myself seems to oscillate between thinking I'm great and being disappointed in myself."GWhere on some days I hype myself up and feel great about who I am."rAnd other days I feel helpless in trying to live my life in a healthy way and be a person I'm proud of being."dChecking in on my friends, not wasting away a day doing things I won't remember two days later.",And I've been getting better at it too!"0So there, life. I'm getting the hang of it."�PERRY: And what a mistake to select this option. So this is just gonna be my random thoughts, a stream of conciousness if you're familiar with the term."EI do love this game dearly, having had a huge impact on my life."xHelping out on it is an amazing feeling, where for the first time I feel like I'm contributing to something bigger."HAnd the fact that it feels productive working on this too, amazing."vI'm just about the last one writing my dialogue, so I have the advantage of knowing what everybody else has said."]And Vulpes was really able to nail down how I feel about contributing to Reborn as well."cI'm not too good a writer, so I'll gladly point to others when they better express how I feel."�And we do have a lot of talented writers in this room here. That should be no surprise to you, most of them contributed to the story of Reborn which we love so much."IOne of my favorite parts was walking around in the desert with Taka."�Did you know that Taka has the most dialogue in the game? Or at least, the text "TAKA:" appears 1.5x more than any other "CHARACTER:" in the game."AAzzie wrote a really sweet fic about it as well, go read it!"kYeah I'm still in love with the game. But now I appreciate the work the others put in it all the more."|It's funny, since I don't even game that much anymore. I think that in the last 5 years I've played a total of 3 games."qGot sucked in the world of fanfiction instead I guess. If only at school those counted as books you've read."lBut anyway, you're probably holding the X button down to skip this dialogue so I'll end your suffering."Have fun out there!"PERRY: Cool, see ya."0Talk to the others too, they're very sweet!"AZZIE: Hi there!"Thanks for stopping by!"(I hope you've been enjoying Reborn!"\This game means so much to so many people, I'm really glad you stuck it out to the end."QThere's some pretty great stuff still ahead of you, I'll tell you that much."@Was there something in particular you'd like to talk about?"+AZZIE: I do like talking about Reborn!"USo compared to most people in this room, my history with Reborn is pretty short."XIn 2017-ish, I found out about the game through a friend of mine tweeting about it."�He posted a picture of the inside of Sweet Kiss Candy shop, I mistook it for a Pokecentre, and immediately decided I had to play this game."�Of course, then I actually started playing, and... Well, let's just say Julia kicked my butt so badly I put the game down and forgot about it."For a couple years."uIn February of 2019, I decided to try it again, and-- while I wasn't much better-- I at least had more patience."aI ended up falling completely in love with the game. The characters, the music, the world..."4It made me, and continues to make me, so happy."@Reborn actually ended up reigniting my passion for writing."7More than that, I fell in love with the community!"tI made some incredible friends, some of whom are in this room with me, and I wouldn't trade them for the world."YIn late 2020, I messaged Ame, asking if she needed any help with last-minute things."]A while later, she decided she could use some help with the Nightclub, and so here I am!"iAll the Trainers you can battle in the Battle Pavillion, their little dialogues, were my department!"�I also worked on some of the characters' chatter while hanging out in the club itself-- so go say hi to folks, if you haven't already!"xThis game and community mean so much to me, and I'll always be grateful for how kind and wonderful everyone's been."AZZIE: Oh! Okay, uh, hi!"I'm Azzie."ZI'm a Canadian gal, and at the time this is being published, I'm in my late twenties."~Apart from Reborn (and sundry other fangames, and Pokemon in general) I'm also a musician, animal lover, and storyteller."�I'm so passionate about stories, in all their forms. How they can bring people together, heal people, bring joy and catharsis...":Definitely one of my favourite things to think about."AZZIE: Okay!"
Welp!"AZZIE: That was fun!"&Here, have some BP for your time!" You'll have \v[593] BP now!"1AZZIE: That's okay, you'll get it next time!"KYRA: Prrawr?"QYou find yourself compelled by forces beyond your comprehension to pet Kyra."Allow yourself to pet her?"Kyra hisses and attacks!"*angry cat noises*";You pet Kyra, careful to avoid The Forbidden Zone(tm)."Your hand is bleeding."Kyra looks satisfied."VThis Zorua is repeating the same move over and over, occasionally holding a pose."?Maybe she's helping her trainer with animation references."Oui"Non"Eau Fraîche - $200"Soda Cool- $300"Limonade - $350"Annuler"	Fite"Ame"	Chat"Combattre"	Talk"What do you do" How did you get into reborn"Team Names"	Nope"Developer team"Animation team"Durée"Espace"Fairytale"Starlight"You"Azurine Island"The others"	Rien"Listen"Not now"Battle"Cancel (Derogatory)"You're an intern?"Not from this world?"Reborn's meaning."	Plus"Favorite Pokemon?"Favorite Reborn Location?"	Rien"Who are you?"What do you do?"What Reborn means to you?"Any advice?"Simple"Double"
Azzie"Let's just battle!"Non, merci.;[V"By entering this room you hereby acknowledge that anything you see, hear, observe, experience, or vividly imagine as if it were unmistakably more real than the mutual delusion it must have been in these premises is not and cannot legally be held accountable for being canon.")A note below a row of broken clocks:" How to make peace with time"!Graveyard of Past Developers"Kanaya,"/I still hope you're doing well out there.""DYou might never know how much of everything you've done for me,">As much as I'll try to find the words to express as such.">Maybe I'll never be able to do so fully, and that's okay."QBut I hope that one day I'm able to return the favor and thank you properly."(Wait for me in the starlight, too?""Missed connections:"KOn the release day of Pokémon Gold and Silver, back in the year 2000,"bYou were just about to check out from the retail store with the last physical copy of Silver."HA kid appeared in line behind you, also looking for Silver version."OYou gave the kid your copy, and stepped out of line to get it another day."!You specified one condition:"IThat if they were ever in your position, they should pay it forward."_...Well, that never happened, and digital distribution is a thing so I doubt it ever will."9Hopefully you'll accept this game as payment enough?"Thanks for that.""T.D.R.,"/Well it took me a few years, but I did it."8If you happen to see this, maybe say 'hi' sometime."Max mark?""starrynight,"8If you're still out there and kicking, let us know.":You disappeared so suddenly we were kind of worried.""
Riku," I wish it had gone better.""AA collection of notes for what looks to be a future project."Starlight Divide"�If you look carefully, you can see the notes for a half dozen other prospective future projects hidden and scattered behind them."#None of them are intelligible."VIf only whoever wrote them ever had either enough time or the sense to chill out."The Archivist"Kurotsune"You feel a presence..."Face it head on?"Fantastic! Bye."1You suddenly felt as if you had gained a BP."*You felt that you now had \v[593] BP."Dan"I'm tilted."
Azery"What A Great Battle..."Lia"	oosp"	Mike"May he yet find Redemption"Kids these days..."MDE"*Just a friendly Dedenne here to help!"Kanaya"...Tch."Guhorden"BWe should probably have made space for a few more tombstones?"<I mean, it's not like these people are actually gone..."But some others as well--"Dashie"Aeodyn"starrynight"HThat's without a 'k' people, don't get confused with the other one!"0Not that she hasn't been super helpful too."Also Koyo!"HOh yeah, the summoning thing had a thing for her too, or whatever.""!!!"NTo those of you resting here, and those of you still actively by my side,"oThanks so much for helping me on this stupid over- ambitious project that I started on a whim forever ago."TThere's a lot of mistakes I made and things I wish I could've done differently,".And also while we're at it, water is wet."MStill, it means a lot to me to have had the help and made it to the end."Thank you <3""9To all the former staff of the online Reborn League,"IThanks for being a part of the bullshit that kicked all of this off."II know it's been years, and your respective mileages varied with it,"�But at the end of it all, I'm still grateful for all your help in setting up memories for the few dozen people packed into the server each evening."<Not to mention the however-many-more seeing this now..."&Smile for the camera, won't you?""<It's a vending machine.\nWhich drink would you like? \G""\GA Fresh Water dropped down!"/\GBonus! Another Fresh Water dropped down."(\GYou have no room left in the bag."#\GYou don't have enough money."\GA Soda Pop dropped down!",\GBonus! Another Soda Pop dropped down."\GA Lemonade dropped down!",\GBonus! Another Lemonade dropped down."CASS: yo"?it is SO nice to be able to ignore grammar rules for once."rules are the worst."so what are you in for"CASS: k, put 'em up"great, you did it." CASS: have a bp or whatever"$you have \v[593] now, have fun."CASS: ok, buddy."!CASS: you wanna talk to ame?"sure, hold on."okay, sure!"Dfull disclosure, i really have no idea what to talk about here."{i'm writing this on new year's eve so you're just going to be getting whatever stray thoughts come into my head today."5take your pick. \ch[62,-1,who u,devving,lessons]"Ftake your pick. \ch[62,-1,who u,devving,lessons, likes, dislikes]"Mtake your pick. \ch[62,-1,who u, devving, lessons, likes, dislikes, ame]"im cass",look, i never know what to say to this."5here, i'll add some more options to the chatbox."ah yes."!back when i was a smol child"at the wee age of 21"7i hit up ame and was like "hey you want some help""/and ame was like "yeah do some animations""Li had played reborn twice and liked it enough to come back to it later."Ji like helping out with things that have potential and need the help." but god i hated animations."�the animation editor worked in a legal sense. if you consulted the dictionary definition of "functional" you would likely deduce that the editor qualified as such."(but working with it was a bad time."i made one animation.":now i genuinely don't remember what i did after that."nlife was rough. i ended up clicking with ame really well and moved in with her at the end of that summer."7i did a lot of uncategorizable dev work for a bit."�i think the most notable thing i did was filesize reduction. e17 was the largest episode of reborn and i'm doing my best to keep it that way."tafter that i got into teambuilding. most of the nightclub content was done by me. it's why i have an NPC there."Lit would've been... about three years ago by the time this is released."ki've gotten a bit better at teambuilding since then! just in case some of the teams seem a bit crusty."�later that year we put out e18.2. that was technically my first release! it was just a small update to the AI to put out some fixes."Vafter that was when i started putting effort into getting the game to run better."hbefore this, i had some minor experience with scripting. i generally didn't like working with code."Sthen perry showed up with a script that evaluated the performance of the code.""i took that and went to town."Uregular readers of my devblog posts will recall the optimization o'clock series."�i spent an absolute shitload of time combing through the scripts, running the profiler, making changes, re-running the profiler, noting differences, making changes, re-rerunning the profiler..."Aas weird as it may sound, it was a life-changing experience."�i think i'm probably known more generally as a coder these days. which is weird! if you told me before my optimization binge that my primary role on the team was going to be as a scripter, I'd have laughed really hard before tossing you out of my office."(metaphorical office)"@it got me to realize that, hey, maybe coding wasn't so bad!"#and now i'm really good at it!"?hell, the optimization binge practically changed fangames."bif this isn't your first fangame, you've probably felt the impact of this without knowing it."nthe biggest effect was probably that it kicked off a series of events that led to making MKXP mainstream."8i don't know if you happened to use the old engine."it sucked."@it ran badly for everyone no matter what hardware you used."3it was in desperate, dire need of improvement."Fif you've never experienced it then i consider that a good thing."Bit also opened up the development of the main fangame engine."_you've probably experienced something based on my code modifications without realizing it."+and, well, i guess now we're at today!"3i help out with a number of different games..."%i've made a fuckload of teams..."destroyed the code..."and now here we are!"wso if you're playing this game, or rejuv, or some other game, and noticing that it's running smooth like butter..."i'm glad i could help!"+look at you picking the cheesy option."Ahopefully you also picked them in order so this has context!"'man i'm bad at talking about this."reborn's changed my life.".....god that's SO cheesy."/i think it's making me lactose intolerant."Oi said that i was in a bad place when i first got involved in development."Ci could really use a change of environment, change of scenery."reborn's where i got that."`it kinda got off to a rocky start. i was in a social circle that was... not the healthiest."Hbut then i got out of that. made new friends, worked on new things."%i've come a long way since then!"*people don't take fangames seriously."i get it."7but that doesn't mean that they aren't meaningful."�i've met a lot of cool people, i've worked on a project that other people enjoy, i've acquired a lot of new skills, and i've (hopefully!) helped out other people in the process."=i don't want to say that there's a "lesson" from this..."&but keep yourself open to things!"*you never know where they might lead."5interesting things. whatever that ends up being.">dishonesty. assholes. RMXP. other shit that doesn't work."ok there. happy now?"hif there's one thing that i can say with certainty it's that i don't know how to talk about myself."9yeah that's right ame!!!! i'm doing this too!!!!!!!!"...ahem"Kso none of this would've happened if i didn't get involved with reborn"8and that wouldn't've happened if it wasn't for ame."}ame will tell you about how making reborn kinda happened on accident- one thing led to another thing and now we're here."{that's kinda true of my presence in the community, too. i never had any expectations of things going the way they did."bbut i'm here! and, in hindsight, moving in with ame was probably the best decision i've made."�she's great. really cares about the community. really dedicated to making things for people to enjoy. really wants the best for the people around her.")she's my best friend and i love her."Cyeah i bet THATS not something you expect to see in a fangame."%lol fangames are just edgy trash"7yeah well this one got the developer a girlfriend!"8...though idk how true that'll be for other people."ame cray."AME: O-oh?"Uh, hi there!"DDidn't expect to come back into this world like this, but okay!"*Don't worry, I'm still dead in canon."uWell, I was looking forward to putting in a secret room like this for so long and now I barely know what to say."WIn spite of that, I tend to talk a lot, so I'll probably say too much here anyway."uI know whenever I finish a game I liked, I always have a ton of questions about the development and its creator."7I want to know like "how did this game happen????""}So I'll try and pre-empt some of that with the answers I wished maybe I'd have access too if I were just finishing this."lTbh, that's most of how I approach the game; I just try to make something I'd enjoy playing for myself.";Anyway, feel free to ask about anything in particular."3AME: Did you want to ask about something else?"eWhat'll it be? \ch[62,-1,Myself, Community ,League,Game,Leaders,Team,Future,Lessons,Fight ,Cass]">AME: Oh, sure, I can get over myself long enough to talk."So firstly, let's get this straight-- aside from existing in this particular room, I don't love having a self-insert character."�When I made the game based on the online league, we were pretty much exclusively using existing characters from the community though,"tAnd as the community leader and one running the online league, I was the closest thing to a "Professor" we had."�I didn't ever expect the game to go beyond the community, so then when it did, I'm like okay, I am sick of having a damn self-insert in this entire-ass game."oA lot of people kept expecting me to be the surprise villain or surprise champion or something, and like--"
No!!!"5I want to exist frankly as little as possible!!!"2And, well, you know how I fixed that problem."_Outside of myself as a character though, like, I'm just a girl who likes making videogame."tI got started with private lessons when I was 9, Game Maker when I was 10, and found RPG Maker when I was 11..."Y(To all you aspiring game devs out there, if 11-year- old me can do it, so can you.)"C...And I definitely tunnel-visioned on making games back then."hI didn't finish any of them, but I did spend several years on an isekai aRPG called Second Reality."�That's the only real prior experience I have here, and classically, I will want to perish if I think about that project too much."OStill, that experience helped me make this happen, so I'm grateful for it."vI went to school for psychology, but that was just a backup until any of my creative pursuits became sustainable."=I was originally writing a novel when Reborn took off..."DThe "Living Angel" thing in the circus was a reference to that."3But I abandoned the project to focus on games."aThanks to the community's support, I've been able to work on this full time for a while now."Tysm everyone!!! <33333"VI hope that the project has been able to live up to your expectations in the end,"ABut it definitely exceeded my own, so either way, I'm happy."8I hope I can keep doing this for a long time still."BAlthough I won't be making Pokémon games anymore after this,"(let me out.......)"\Maybe this won't be the last time you find me in a room like this at the end of a game!"?AME: So, Reborn was a community long before it was a game."NMy dad taught me the basics of HTML, PHP, MySQL, etc when I was 10 or so,"(Thanks Dad!)">So I was running my own website by the time I was twelve."nWhen Diamond and Pearl came out a few years later, everyone wanted to try out the hot new WiFi functions,"�So I gathered a handful of people from various internet communities I was in, and my own website, and set up a subdomain on my site for us to try WiFi!"_That Pokémon-oriented subdomain ended up outliving the main site by a significant margin."=Even though there were only like, a dozen of us there..."<It was very lively and a lot of fun during the summers!"qIt didn't have a proper name or anything, so it just kinda got called PokéPlace in lack of anything better."KBut then, once school started, we all got busy and the place died too."k...And then when summer rolled around again, everyone was back battling and trading, so it was reborn!"lThis happened several years in a row, being dead during the school year, and then busy in the summer..."S...Which is why Reborn got its name! Because the site was Reborn every summer!"_...Well, it skipped a year. We all kind of moved on towards the end of 4th gen's lifespan."�I decided to bring it back the next year under its own site properly, and so we launched the current version of the site in May of 2010."PBy that time the League was a thing, but that's a separate dialogue option."jThe League ended up attracting a lot of people though, so we grew wayyy more than I ever expected to,"-And then the game attracted even more..."And here we all are today!"NMy life really wouldn't be anywhere near the same without this community,"[And although I've never been a fan of other big sites and places (too many people?!?!)"iI'm very grateful to everyone who's stuck around, contributed, just popped into chat briefly, etc..."YAnd I hope that those of you further away from us will consider dropping by someday!"uPlus, everyone whose support has kept me going through that alternate evolution of Eevee when you give it money,"3Really, like, makes my life awesome, you know?"%Thank you so much everyone <3333"dAME: So, this game was based on the online Reborn League challenge we hosted for several years."/But how did that league itself come about?"BOriginally, it was a challenge to my best friend at the time."lWe met through the RPG Maker community, and enjoyed playing difficulty hacks like Emerald 386 together."�He and I often said things like, "Wouldn't it be awesome if you could fight Gym Leaders that actually put up as much of a fight as real people?""gSo when I was 14 or so, I came up with a list of badge names, images, and pun names for each type,"JAnd you basically know all of those already. I think I kept them all."FI started making that challenge for him around the time I was 15."WTerra was the first Leader I worked on, but she was no more than a name back then."�I remember spending a lot of time EV Training Gliscor and Flygon in actual Pearl, and I was going to create a team for each type that way."�...I didn't get farther than Gliscor and Flygon before my friend and I had a falling out, and we didn't really speak much after that."?The challenge died, and I also quit making games entirely."mA few years later, I found that image with all the badges and Leader names, and decided to try it again."qReborn had already existed as a community by then, and subsequently died (for good, even over the summer)..."iBut I still hung out with most of the people involved in a small little community called Monkey Pro."bMaybe they would be interested in the Gym Leader challenge I'd started for my friend instead?"�I also knew the Shoddy Battle simulator was a thing by then, so I was able to convince one of Monkey Pro's members, Hyperlisk, to host a private server for us."+Terra was once again the first Leader."WMy concept for her this time was "a girl who's personality is like an earthquake"."~I made Trainer Cards for each of them, and sprites that I worked on during class, or backstage from theatre rehearsals..."bI roleplayed the Leaders myself, and some of them didn't have much character, but it was fun."}So, it became a somewhat daily ritual for me to bark at some friends on MP, asking them if they'd like to do a Leader battle."<People seemed to really enjoy this "Monkey Pro League"."cThen I got kicked out of theatre, fell into depression, and stopped hosting it for months lmao"5In May of 2010, I decided to give it another go."�This time, I found the Pokémon Online simulator, which was way more friendly than Shoddy Battle, and another MP member hosted a server for us."You would know him as Nyu!"GI also made the current iteration of the site to go along with it."\This League began like the last, with me asking my friends if they wanted to Do A Fight"�...But what I didn't expect was for random-users to drop in from the greater Pokémon Online space and decide "Hey, this looks interesting!"">In this way, the league and community grew quite rapidly!"IAnd so, we hosted it nearly every weekday evening for several years."YIt quickly got too much for me to handle alone, so eventually I had to ask for help.":We used to do three battles per challenger per night,"DAnd then I had to limit it to just one as we got more and more,"bAnd then sometimes even at one battle per challenger, we'd still be up until two or three AM."\Managing that, team registrations and trainer cards really was a full time job already."But it was a lot of fun!"�My favorite part was how, when everyone was waiting for their own turn, the challengers would all pile into spectate each match."fThere was a lot of wild cheering for either side, fifteen people to a very small chat log room..."TAnd people would chat with and get interested in the Leaders' personal stories."|Many of the events in game are a reference to those online stories, such as Amaria losing her memory, and Luna disappearing."dShortly after sixth gen released, we made the difficult decision to retire the League for good."tThe bottom line is that I wasn't able to keep up with both running it and developing the game at the same time."�There were some other factors, like Pokémon Showdown becoming popular, and I wasn't entirely thrilled with the quality of recent matches and events."SBut even those things were just obstacles because the game was taking my time."]I hope everyone who was able to participate in the League has some fun memories from it!"7I know they were some of my favorite times ever <3"QAME: When the League was at its peak, a few different users had the idea of,"7What if we made a game based on the Reborn League?"eThe first few fledgling passes at it from community members disappeared as quickly as they came.">For my part, I didn't pay the wayward attempts much mind."zI knew that trying to do that for all 18 Leaders would be an enormous undertaking that obviously no one would finish."2Also, I tried romhacking in the distant past."�I wanted to make, basically, Fire Red 386 since there wasn't a good difficulty + all availability game for Kanto like there was for Hoenn at the time."<Somehow I broke evolution by changing a Trainers' team."5Decided pretty quickly romhacking wasn't for me."{However, there was an ongoing thread of discussion over the months about "What would Reborn look like if it were a region?""eOne time in the PO server's earliest days, I signed off for the night as the sole admin and mod."PI'm not exactly clear what happened-- maybe a spammer or something came on?">Anyway, I wasn't there to deal with it, and havoc ensued."�One of the users on at the time, Will, then made an entire lore about how The City of Reborn Fell Into Chaos Because The Great Leader Ame Wasn't There."�He then started drawing +Infinitas, a comic about the leaders of Reborn facing off against the villainous Team Meteor, based on that premise...".I liked the idea of a ruined city region."WIt felt more fresh compared to the lush, vapid environments of every other region."MTo be honest, I also just like working with the concept of giant cities?",I find it likely this won't be my last."jAnyway, one of those times people were talking about The Region, I started hand-drawing a map for it."4Did it on and off, took me two years to finish."gI had a lot of fun, due to old habits, thinking about "What might this be like if it were a game?""4But I had no intention to actually make it one."Then, in 2012 a Reborn member by the name of STK Patrick posted once again about making a game based on the online league."OHe noted that a game called Pokémon Raptor had a working Pokémon engine."2I was like, "huh, weird, how does that work?""*He was like "oh it uses RPG Maker XP""0I was like "okay hold the goddamn phone rq,"fbecause i spent the better part of my teenage years tooling around on Rm2k3 and RMXP on the side."#This is suddenly up my alley.""cPulled a "yo imma let you finish but--" on him (because that was an in-vogue meme at the time)"-And made the first episode in two weeks."�I'm... not really sure how I managed that in two weeks other than that the episode kinda sucked at the time, and I didn't do anything else."ZAnyway, I pretty much just worked on the game during every class until I graduated..."�And the character assets already existed from the League, and I asked Will to give me some Team Meteor characters (Sirius and Solaris) for villains."�The community had some fun roleplaying events VS Team Meteor on the server, and another user, Ice, had contributed the characters of Taka and ZEL."CAce came later, and everyone else came from the League itself."AWhen I first started, I figured I'd get bored of it quickly."LMaybe drop the project after a couple months like most of my past ones.""...You can see how that went."�Because I thought I'd get bored, I didn't bother to figure out where the game was actually going until Heather first showed up in Malchous."EThen I'm like, oh, maybe I should like make a plan for anything."�I figured out a story based around fitting in all of the existing league characters, and four macguffins to help tie them together."�Originally I expected this to only be an in-community game, but then people started telling their friends about it and joining because of it..."nOver time I pivoted to make the game more accessible to anyone, even those who hadn't been in the League."fSo, I continued as the sole developer, and released episodes every 2-5 months at a steady pace..."IAnd I hit a wall around E14 (ending with Terra, released late 2014)."}I started wanting to focus on making the game Better as opposed to just More, which increased development time exponentially."aSuddenly releases took half a year to a year and a half, rather than just a few months each."I wasn't ready for that."mI blamed myself for taking too long, and went from doing almost nothing else to -actually- nothing else."gI pushed myself very hard to be perfectly productive, always trying to get E15 out faster because,"[Like E14 (Terra) to E15 (Ciel) is not a lot of content, why is it taking so long??????"FIt took around a year in the end with all the other improvements."aI also began to develop chronic pain in my hands, which I was determined not to let stop me."LEventually I physically couldn't click the mouse, and I had to ease up."yWhen I stepped back, I realized that the stress of pushing myself to work constantly was what was causing that pain."XUnlearning that is an ongoing process, and I still feel the pain from time to time."1Right now, as I'm saying this, for instance."}But at least I have it mostly under control, and I've learned to pace myself better, take breaks, play nice with a team, etc."�I still have some recurring of psychic damage from the amount it's taken to complete a passion project that I started on a whim...":I wonder how many other games I'll have time to make?"\But, I'm trying to learn to be proud of the amount of time and energy we spent on this."BNot many games get the full attention and scope they deserve."NAnd honestly, of all things? I'm not sure a Pokémon fangame deserved it."Still, here we are.">Ten years working on one project is nothing to sneeze at."I hope it shows?"3AME: So, here's the story from my perspective."~I started running the online league by myself, blahblahblah, you can read about all of that in the other dialogue option.">Originally, I was just roleplaying the Leader characters."cLogistically, that meant I just signed on a second account and acted like them, nothing fancy."YWhen I was doing this challenge just for friends, there was no confusion about that."iIn fact, one time my IRL friend, Saya, decided to do a league battle during a rehearsal lunch break."aI fought as Hardy, who, at the time, played singles stall rather than doubles hyper offense.")Hardy's Shuckle vs their Empoleon..."!The battle took 200 turns..."-...We got yelled at for being very late."tAnyway, the point is, for the original challengers of the League, they knew exactly who was behind the leaders."3We were just across the table from each other."MI never expected there to be any doubt that they were just me all along."�Then, in the early days of the PO server, a user named Mashew joined at random and became interested in the league and its characters."/Only, he didn't realize they weren't real."BThere was no question of it, he just accepted that they were."This surprised me."sHe seemed to be having a lot of fun and getting personally invested in their stories, so I didn't correct him."pAfter all, it was way more fun to add some character, some drama, and play out a bit of conflict with them."NWhen others started joining after him, they seemed to believe it all too."�One example was Savage, who you might recall from the story in Lapis. That was a real thing that really happened in the League for some reason."dEven the people who originally knew that I was just roleplaying implicitly began to play along."%They seemed to get very into it."OI wondered if everyone, including Saya, had just forgotten that it was me."RMonths passed like this, and it was hard to keep up with all the challengers.":I ran 17 different monotypes, 5 nights a week, alone.">On average, I think there were 20-30 challengers a night."Hundreds over time."It was... difficult."wI invented the "sorry Luna disappeared arc" one night as an excuse to not have to play her when I wasn't up to it."\Other nights when I was just super stressed out and not feeling it, I pushed on anyway."kPlaying Terra and trying to capture her hyperness online, while crying about something or other IRL..."That was just the worst."ASaya happened to show up at my house on one of those nights."fI found out, she didn't forget it was me playing it, she was just going along with everyone else."bAnd everyone seemed to have a lot of fun accepting the different characters at surface level."AIt felt nice to not be entirely alone in keeping the secret."cIn Febuary of 2011, I realized that hosting the League by myself was absolutely unsustainable.",The volume of challengers was too high."6There was just too much for one person to handle."�I confided in our co-admin, Ikaru, who joined us in the fall of the year prior, after the Leaders' had already been accepted as a force of nature."�He was very invested in Titania, and finding out that the character who was so motivated by the notion of living up to truth, was herself a lie, hurt him."qI'm very grateful for his forgiveness, and that he stuck around to support the league and game despite that."qIkaru and Saya became my first co-hosts of the league, and joined me in hosting and roleplaying the leaders."]Even splitting them to a third between us, we barely kept up with the challenger volume."MAlso, it was stressful for them to have to keep up with every night too."pWe swapped out League Hosts over the next few years, being joined by Mashew, Ash, Hark, and several others,"ZAll of whom I'm very grateful to for helping manage the disaster traffic I'd amassed."GIn general, it was never one player to one specific Leader though."gI could barely keep the three or four of us in place each night, let alone a full roster of 17-18."VThere were two exceptions, being that for much of Season 2, I only played Amaria,"RAnd for a while we had one line leader by the name of Tenshi, who played Lin."�I was never terribly enthused with his capacity for roleplaying, but he was an excellent battler who swept through the League without batting an eye.";However, he eventually decided to leave the community,"[And he did so by posting a sudden resignation announcement in which he basically said,"MThe Leaders are all fake and being played by us, and I'm sick of it, bye"3I thought, okay, that's it, jig's up, go home."xGoing to be a lot less interesting entertaining my crowd of hundreds when they know it's just us in different hats."+I was surprised by what happened next."zObviously there were the handful of people who knew, and the handful of people who Thought So but didn't Know-know..."/But the general tone of the community was,"wIt's more fun to accept them as real, so let's just let the new folk keep believing that so they can enjoy it too."uThe game began to be a thing at some point after that, and the League stopped being a thing at some point later,"{But this was always still meant to be a community game, so it seemed like everyone implicitly accepted the same thing.";More fun to let the new players think it was all real."�I decided I'd keep it up until the game finished, but I really expected that to be, like, six years ago or so as opposed to only just now."PI've been tired of that all forever, but sunken cost is one hell of a drug."TRecently, there's been a lot of people who are morally concerned about it too--"�About whether or not it was okay for us to show things like Corey and Kiki, given their respective fates (which were story points in the online league too)"QAnd whether we got the express consent of the Leaders to be featured here..."C...And while those are fair concerns, they don't really apply."7They were all just fictional characters all along."=To some this will be disappointing; to others, a relief."!For myself, it's the latter."XI'm grateful to have this out in the open again so I can talk more freely about it."[I hope that everyone will forgive me for keeping up the facade for more than a decade."I understand if not."4Maybe let the new players have their fun still?"Maybe not."It's in your hands now."TAME: So like I said in the other dialogue options, I started this game alone..."CReally never was great at the whole working with others thing?"�I was like, weirdly afraid if I let someone else access the game's files, they'd just delete everything and run screeching into the night like some kind of gremlin."DObviously, that's ridiculous and most people just want to help."�I first started working with a team directly when The Amount Of Things That Needed To Be Done escalated in 2013 after the E13 (Charlotte) release."�Realistically, my standards just rose, but I needed help, so I started working with two good friends, Autumn and Blind Guardian (or Dan)."}You can thank Autumn for a lot of the animations in the game, especially the over the top ones like many of the Z-Moves!"�Dan helped shore up the bleeding scripts, and first encouraged me to try implementing the Field Effect system. He also made it so fields changed visually!"1But at first, they just helped with testing."wWe packed into a call, Autumn would play through the game with some ridiculous team probably involving a Castform,"}Dan would fix script errors, and I would do whatever else it was that needed doing and also probably stress out a little bit."It was a lot of fun!"HI was sad when that groove came to an end, but I still needed help."fThe early versions of Essentials were incomplete, and subsequent generations made that gap worse."dDespite running a website, I was still a fledging programmer, and I couldn't fix it all myself."BI got some help from someone I met in a game called Guhorden!"[I feel like of everyone who's helped out on development, I know the least about him..."YBut he offered his services where they were much needed, and I appreciated it a lot."TThe next to offer was Kurotsune, near the end of E14 when they were very drunk."sI had never talked to this person, and I was still pretty distrustful of Why Would This Rando Want To Help Me?".Which in retrospect was completely silly."�Kuro became an invaluable mentor to me both in terms of good programming habits (sorry about the indentation!!!) and organizing a team."They undertook the initiative to get a few more hands in to help finish the rest of the new-gen additions to the battle system."7Notably from that, we picked up Mike and Marcello!"]I felt bad because the process of development seemed to age Mike a half-decade at least,"And, like, same."mBut it seems he's back at it with his own work now so maybe that'll be a project worth checking out, ne?"�And Marcello went from being someone who I knew was helping out with the game but had never spoken to, to being one of my best friends. So that's neat!"?You can thank him for online existing in its current form!"kI followed suit, getting together a team to help out with all the missing animations around that time.">Smeargle and MDE were the main two I picked up from that!"WI'm pretty sure the M in MDE stood for "machine" because man, he cranked them out."VI think he still holds the title for having made the most animations in the game."WHe was very reliable and patient while I asked him for revisions eight times over!"�Meanwhile our resident Smeargletail has done quite a lot on his own too, and tends to hit them out of the park with a lot of care and energy!"YHe also made all the slick Legendary overworld animations you might see in postgame."MWe picked up one more animator down the line after MDE moved on, Vulpes!"�She seems to be the shy type, but she came with experience, and pretty much every animation she's done has been a banger out the gate."hOthers who've helped along the way include Azery and Lia, who we brought on for general bug-fixing."There was a lot of it..."|Kanaya and another friend of mine, I'd asked to help out with small tasks like filling in cliffs around the entire desert..."`Seriously, it took two of them two weeks of working on it reliably to get all of that done."7Not to mention the other areas they helped with..."zMuch appreciation to them for trudging through all of that despite me kind of giving them the short end of the stick."|Ikaru's another person who's helped out with filling in my ridiculous maps, along with just general handling of bug reports."lHe's also usually the first person I test with, watching his every playthrough and judging his actions!"Y...And getting trolled when he decides to spam Itemfinder everywhere until I behave."�Jan's just kind of here these days, but originally we had a trade where I helped him out with learning to sprite better in return for him tackling a few sprites for Reborn." Cass joined us late in E18."0Originally she was going to be an animator!"-She did Leafage and no other animations."zBut she more than made up for it in ways I already basically gushed about in another section, so I'll spare her here."DShe did suggest we take on a certain Toothpastefairy, or Perry!"�He happened to be working on some mods anyway so we picked him up to help out and he's just been fantastic for the whole tail end of the ride."�I'm very grateful for him helping us out with programming reliably, and also being totally down to enable whatever bullshit Cass or I get up to."qHe's done a lot of quality-of-life improvements for y'all especially, such as that quick TM view in the bag!"9Other late-joining stars include The Legendary Crim."WYou might know of her from her work on literally every other fangame in existence."KIt's been a huge help to have a second spriter and mapper on the team."Even though she was originally just learning both when I asked her to help with Starlight, she learns fast and caught up quick."iThere's no way we could've made some of the postgame content as gorgeous as it has been without her."3Last but not least, we also acquired an Azzie!"oFans might know her from her Tourmaline Travels story, and if not, they might be interested in reading it!"^She's helped out with a lot of the sundry postgame dialogue, especially in the Nightclub."eIf I had to do it all myself I probably would've gone insane and run into the hills screaming..."...Is that everyone?"I think so..."8Gosh, I've written too much already. Let's be done."NBut please appreciate everyone who's helped us make it to this point, ne?"%AME: So, no more Pokémon games."Sorry, not sorry."I am Tired and Done."-Also, there's the whole copyright thing."{Nintendo, please, we can all just walk away from this peacefully, I don't want anything more to do with it, I swear..."LI know a lot of people will probably be disappointed by it, but like..."qY'all gotta remember, even though I've been here for a decade and change, my start is not in Pokémon games."<I've wanted to make a tactical RPG since I was like 12.""Finally gonna go do that now."VIt's called Starlight Divide, and-- obligatory plug-- we have a demo out already!".Wait, I can just take you to the website!"Wanna give it a look?"'AME: Hell yeah, okay, here you go."thank you ily"7AME: okay that's understandable maybe another time"tRegardless, for those of you who already tried the demo (or even who will go on to try it)-- Thank you so much."BIt means a lot to me that you're willing to give it a chance!"pThere's still a lot of work to do on that too, but I'm eagerly looking forward to the opportunity to do so."NThere's a lot of side projects and other games I want to make too, but..."2I guess we'll just have to see how things go?"`My curse is that I come up with ideas way quicker than I can ever dream of developing them."
Alas."JI hope you'll stick around to see what comes from our next endeavors!"�AME: This might've been unclear, but to be clear this section is just sort of advice/lessons I've learned in the realm of game development."nThere's a handful of things I wish I'd done differently, and so I hope others can learn from my mistakes."7If you're not interested, just hold X or whatever.")Let's start with something positive."OThe lesser-known phrase continues "But better than being a master of one.""&Ultimately, I think that is true."wEspecially as an indie dev starting out, it's important to be willing to handle all parts of the project yourself."�I pride myself on being able to do it all-- music, writing, programming (eventually...), spriting, mapping, animation, sfx, etc..."�The flexibility to do all of that has been a great asset in terms of having confidence in knowing that I could finish this game no matter what."�If you're just starting out, it'll also go a long way to helping you work with team members in a way that works for them, which itself helps build trust."...So that's great,"However,"NI think I've caused myself a lot of problems by relying on that too much."xGood to have the option, but it's equally important to be open to accepting help and letting others take the wheel."�Having explored so many different avenues of development, I quite clearly see what I need to do and practice in order to improve at each of them,"}But because I am doing so many things at once, I will not be able to pursue those paths to the ends of quality I'd like."Frustrating."�It also means I'm prone to taking on too much work myself and overwhelming myself, where I see other teams function better when the lead just"=Doesn't Worry About It because it's #NotTheirDepartment."Pros and cons, I guess."OI wish I'd navigated that a bit better and learned to lean on others more."`Speaking of working with others, we only started using git in the last year of development."pNo one told me about it before, and if they had, we couldn't work it meaningfully without exported scripts."mBut if you're on a team, I can't stress how critical it will be to let them access the project directly."Save yourself.":It's intimidating to learn at first, but so worth it."/Frankly, that goes for programming itself."qI didn't touch the scripts in Reborn for years and then I was like 'oh this is just rpg maker eventing lmao'" Eventing also intimidating?"4Again, if 11-year-old me can do it, so can you."Okay, what else?"}Pretty sure every single indie dev advice article will tell you this too, but I sure didn't listen, so I'm repeating it."sDon't make a giant sprawling epic with 18 badges and every legendary in postgame for your first major project.":...It was my second major project, so I'm vindicated."]...But probably just don't do it, like seriously, small goals are best, I p r o m i s e."[It's very easy to underestimate how long everything will take if you're doing it well."/Never doing a game this long again, i s2g."probably."HOkay, I phrased that a little too new-age-spiritually, but, like..."_Now that I'm on the other side of a ten year long project, I'm a lot Better at everything,"SAnd yet there are still things I feel like I could learn from my younger self."jOne of those things is to let myself rest when I don't feel like working, rather than forcing myself."PI talked a bit about the consequences of this in another dialogue option..."LBut I very much grew up admiring people with an unhealthy work ethic..."QThe kind of people who like work until they literally pass out or get sick--"^I felt like by not living up to the same standard, or by taking breaks, I was being lazy."No, that's stupid."[There's something to be said for the programming addage of "work smarter, not harder,""But more importantly..."nMany people are hard on themselves for "being lazy" or "procrastinating" but we are humans who need rest."rListening to yourself when you don't want to work, or when you need to relax, and choosing to trust yourself,"HThat's a necessary habit if you want to be in it for the long term.">Seriously, I don't want anyone to go through what I have."TListen, I know this sounds hokey, but I -promise- this is tangible real advice."HI just said that working harder and forcing yourself is bad, right?"KSo what's the trick to get good at something if you're not feeling it?"OIt's still to do it a lot, but the hack there is to -want- to do it a lot."dIf you're having fun, you're going to want to do it a lot, and you'll naturally get good at it."	See?"@And especially with long-haul development projects, like..."`You either find a way to make it fun for yourself, or it's miserable and drags out forever."+I really can't stress this one enough."3Okay, go out there and make some vidya, y'all."(AME: Oh, so you've chosen violence."All right, here we go."4Good show! It's no wonder you made it this far!"AME: Impressive work!"BBut then, you've made it this far, so who could be surprised?"(Here, let's throw in a BP for that."!That puts you at \v[593] BP."AME: That's okay."�I think I put this in game somewhere, but as I always told the challengers in the online league, you learn more from losses than wins."?This is simply an extra learning opportunity just for you!")Let me heal up your team real quick."AME: All better!"MBy the way, quick shout-out to the Crim for making my transition sprite."|I didn't want to, because I was like 'boo hoo spriting myself is so egotistical lmao whiiineeee' so she covered for me."0Also thanks to Cass for making my dev team,"/And, well, actually, everyone's dev teams,"RAnd while we're at it, pretty much the majority of the post-game teams too???"Girl's crazy."Love her."Okay, carry on."*AME: Oh, sure, we can go back to her."DBut first I'm gonna use the opportunity to talk shit about her."9And by 'talk shit' I mean tell everyone she's great."�Cass joined us around the release of E18, ended up moving in with me, and has generally just done a lot of like, holding me together."nSo you have her to thank for me being able to complete the entire postgame without going literally crazy."�In addition to that, she also got MKXP support going for us back before it was a common thing, which meant less lag and Mac and Linux versions,"~And she broke open the scripts so we could use git like a functional team, made god knows however other many utilities for us,"AOptimized everything, recoded half the battle system and AI,"4All the goddamn teams, the battle tower sets..."T...And probably a lot of other smaller things that neither of us will remember."LThe point is I owe her a lot and I'm very grateful for all of her help."Okay, back to her now."Don't tell her I said this"uwu"DA sinister energy emerges from the generic graphic on the wall."It could be anything..."Do you dare?"i miss techie johnathan"fThe team's terrifying test train-er defeated, a sense of peace overcame you and healed your team.")Suddenly, everything was okay again."EWhatever had happened must have just been a terrible delusion..."-You tried not to let it derail your day."&did the team forget to delete me?"3You tried not to let it get you too off track."So what do you wanna do?"#So you wanna fight? Cool beans"Nice job"$SMEARGLE: Want to take some BP?"You have \v[593] BP now."SMEARGLE: Uh... oops."I'll fix your team."[Just to warn you I have a tendency to ramble and talk too much so here's your warning."[This stuff has also been rewritten a few times even though I kept calling it finished."%So what do you wanna talk about?"nHey my real name is Sam, and my main task to do was work on animations at the end of 2015 along with MDE."ZAlthough, in about the last year of development, I've also gotten to make two quests,"bwith one of those having a new trainer class and two original characters for zeraora's quest."�My friend Crim did touch ups so go give her a hug for me and give my other friend Azzie a hug for helping check my grammar and tightening up words."�Along with that stuff, I did some other tasks too, like the ferris wheel, giant dragon statue, overworld animations,screen overlay animations,ect."�Though my motivation has been off and on, Ame has been super patient with me through the years, honestly more than she probably should have."zDoesn't help that my diet consists of 1 meal and 2 pops a day, and almost no exercise which leaves me sleeping a lot."�Actually, that patience was really needed when I was having a mental breakdown in 2018, when I was juggling way too many things at once."�It was mostly real life related stuff that ended up leading to a few months of doing egg icons which were low effort but, kept me from being complacent."�Needless to say I'm very grateful for the chances Ame has given me to try to branch out in terms of creativity, and letting me take breaks for self care."kHopefully in the future there will be even more branching out, like trying my hand at music composing."OI'll probably stick around for future projects, or until Ame kicks me out."QHere's hoping my motivation and diet choices get better on the next project."�So I'm truly grateful for being in the right place and right time to be in the animation project. Some person on youtube did like a top 10 fangames video, I think?"3I just remember them being female and British."~Anyways, it was back in 2014, so it got lost in the thousands of top 10 pokemon fangame videos that have since been made."mI kind of wish I remembered the name so I could thank her for bringing me into this wonderful community.">As for what Reborn means to me, it's like a family to me."QEveryone in the dev team especially feel like the closest people in my life."~I'm an introvert so there's not a huge amount of friends outside of online, and it probably doesn't help that I talk too much."fSmeargle is named after the main character of one of my favorite books, "The Never Ending Story"."sIt's a name I tend to put into any game that lets me choose a name, either that or Rhiannon, my favorite song."The rest are named after Greek gods because of how interesting Greek myths are, even only knowing a fraction of the myths."..."VULPES: ...Oh, hi!"2Sorry, I was working on some animation stuff."6But I, uh... got a bit too caught up in it again."Did you want anything?"VULPES: Oh, sure!"&Which team did you want to fight?"?Oh, you won't get a BP for the animation team, by the way."RSince it's significantly easier to beat than the others, it wouldn't be fair."So which will it be?"Right!">Though if you'll humor me, I have a quick question first."+Which of these feels more vast to you?"*Which field did you want to fight on?"Okay, got it!"Sweetpea, if you would?"Not bad!"VULPES: Nice job!",Hope you enjoyed seeing the animations!"&VULPES: Hey, you did pretty well."'I'm sure you'll beat me next time!")And I hope you liked the animations!"Here's some BP."You have \v[593] now."(Oh, and about my question before..."@That was just our way of deciding what field we'd fight on."I know, it's a bit much."LBut Sweetpea here likes seeing people being surprised by her illusions,"?And what kind of trainer would I be if I didn't spoil her?"HBut now she's had her fun, so I can just ask straight up next time."Anything else?"PVULPES: Sure, if you want, though I'm not sure what to talk about honestly."<VULPES: So, I guess I should introduce myself properly."Hi, I'm Vulpes!"eI've been existing in Reborn's general vicinity since 2015, and I joined the team in early 2018."GI'm not really a people person though, so I've mostly just lurked."#I've also studied game design!"VI barely remember most of the course, but that was my first experience animating."WAnd I loved that part more than anything else we covered, so here I am, animating!"But word of advice?"IJust look up a syllabus and teach yourself, it's easier and cheaper."WThe only reason to even look at a course is to see what goes into game production."Anyway."RGetting involved in Reborn has taught me a lot, and it's been really fun too!"=And here's hoping any future projects are even more fun!"2So I started helping out with Reborn in 2018."ZI was checking a forum thread and Ame mentioned she was looking for another animator.":I really wanted to help with the game, since, well..."TReborn is probably the only reason I'm still interested in Pokémon in general."bI'd been a fan since I was five, maybe earlier, so Pokémon was a pretty big part of my life."cBut I started losing interest between BW2 and XY, and drifted away from the franchise by ORAS."EI don't know exactly why, but Reborn brought that interest back."oAnd I get extremely sentimental over everything, so having such a big part of my life revived like that..."It meant a lot."JAnyway, as I was saying, I really wanted to help out because of that.">But I was also convinced I would be a burden on the team."7I almost talked myself out of applying altogether." But I'm very glad I didn't."RThat choice is probably in the top three decisions I've ever made in my life."/Even so, it took a bit of getting used to."bAll my animation experience at the time was in 3D, and the technical stuff didn't carry over."RIt wound up with me thinking stuff like "Oh, a spiral will be easy to make!","'And then it would take me a month."0As opposed to like an hour in a 3D program."?Fun fact that is definitely not linked to this in any way:"YMy least favorite Pokémon is Shiinotic, and my least favorite move is Strength Sap."SBut I got better, and eventually even started using 3D to improve my 2D stuff."7Have you seen the Genesis Supernova animation yet?"hI made all the unique graphics for that by making a 3D reference pose to get the perspective right."g(I mostly just mentioned it because it's my favorite animation I've made and you should watch it.)"Actually, you know what?"Give me one... second..."There!"BI have a team on hand now with some of the animations I made!"DCan't have all of them because I made a fair number of Z-Moves,"SBut this is all I did for the game for like four years, I want to show it off."7But I've been working on other stuff recently too."TI also started helping with the code once we hit testing for the final episode!"lI had a little experience before that, but it was in a language that went out of use before I was born."So not exactly helpful."RBut then the animation editor started not letting you change things properly."2So I checked the code because why not, right?";And I saw a thing and said "hey is this breaking it?","PAnd Cass and Perry said "yeah that's it also you wanna help with the code","BAnd I said "sure sorry if I suck at first" and that was that."7And to this day I'm still messing up basic syntax."WI'm being dramatic, it's been two months at most, of course I'm not brilliant yet."0But I'm fine with that, baby steps and all."UAnd hey, you're using the password that was the first bit of code I implemented!"So I can't suck that bad!"@... Well, the first bit of code players will see, at least."XI made some changes to the animation editor first, but you probably won't see that."*VULPES: "But Vulpes," I hear you ask."KWhy do you have this option when you said you weren't a people person?"1Assuming you read the first option, that is."NThe answer is I just want an excuse to get a bunch of stuff off my chest."8And everyone here helped me deal with it, so there."`This is going to get kind of heavy, so here's a chance to back out if you're not up for it."5So, it might seem obvious from my other answers,"FBut I had pretty bad anxiety since even before I joined the team."@Probably with some moderate depression mixed in for flavor."ZI think it's been about five years, but thinking back I showed symptoms much earlier.">It wasn't exactly conductive to having a functional life."nFor most of the time I've been on the team, Reborn's been the only real anchor I've had to functionality."7Without the others, I'd have been a lot worse off."aAnd even now, when I'm starting to get better, they're helping me a lot just by being there.";With most people, I always felt pressured in some way."QEither by how I "should" act around them, or from the expectations they had."EIt'd be a lie to say I never felt like that around the others..."8But it was a lot less often than with other people."fAnd even when I did feel like that, after the first couple of months I could deal with it easier."nI wasn't able to actually talk very often, but at the same time I didn't feel guilty or "wrong" for that."`When the whole world tells you "socialise this, network that", even when it's impossible..."fHaving a space to exist with others, without having to worry about that stuff, was a big comfort."JAnd it's taken a while, plus some other help, but I'm not as bad now."LI'm able to talk to them without constantly panicking and overthinking."fEven if I'd started recovering without them around, I wouldn't be making nearly as much progress."`Instead of having two or three people I'm comfortable existing around, I have about twelve."GThere's only so many things you'll have in common with one person."LBut with different people, there's going to be different commonalities."6And it makes it that much easier to talk to them."TAnd maybe after that, eventually, you'll feel comfortable calling them friends."'And for everyone else on the team?"-I think I've finally reached that point."@So really, I owe the others my emotional health and sanity.">And also my existence outside of being the local cryptid.")Still plan on being that IRL though.".Give me a dog or cat over humans any day."0And hey, if any of this resonates with you?"DKnow that you're probably underestimating yourself as a person."/More people care about you than you think,"5And you're much less of a burden than you think."1I got caught up in those thoughts a lot too."But your brain is lying."=Even if you can't believe me right now, keep it in mind."-And I hope some day you will be able to."VULPES: Sure."Take care of yourself."$Okay, anything else you wanted?"*Anything else you want to talk about?"VULPES: Okay, see you!"CRIM: ...Oh, hi!",...Gosh, I never know what to say here."AUh, I guess I can just start with-- welcome to the dev room!"AIt's still kind of a trip for me to see myself in this room,"RFor a game that I've been playing and/or involved in for nearly half my life?"+But I'm immensely grateful regardless!"#I could gush a whole lot more,":But I'll save that for when I'm actually prompted to!"0Apologies in advance, I tend to talk a lot!"J...Anyways, hi! I'm Crimson, or Crim! But I usually go by the latter."It's lovely to meet you!"XCRIM: Hi, welcome back again! I hope you've been enjoying the rest of the dev room!"'And your adventure too, of course!"$Did you want to talk some more?"%...Or are you back for a battle?"What can I do for you?"/CRIM: Oh, you want to stay and chat a bit?"XJust as a heads-up, I never know what to say to these unless specifically prompted."0But I will talk your ear off if invited to!"EWhat's up? \ch[62,-1,Reborn,Game Involvement, Myself,Nevermind!]"-CRIM: Oh, you want to talk about Reborn?"Okay! Buckle up."OI ended up joining the team in early December of 2020, when I'd asked Ame,"DHey, so since we released Starlight, you want help with Reborn?"+And she was like, "Sure! Come aboard.""}I was over the moon. I already had a lot of love for the game-- I've got a massive soft spot for intricate storytelling."iThe characters, the story, the maps, the music, the world, all of it was just a pure serotonin rush."ZQuick commercial break: You should check out Starlight Divide, too! No bias, promise."VThere's a lot of love poured into that game already, and it's only a demo so far!";But to go back to your regularly scheduled emoposting,"mI was pretty starstruck about getting to work on a game I'd been playing for like, seven or eight years.""Honestly, I still kind of am!"9And as a bonus, it came with a bunch of cool people!"�Some of my closest friends are sitting right here in this room with me, or are people I've met through this game, and I'll always be forever grateful for that."/Both the community and its people, well..."`With the risk of sounding cheesy as heck, Reborn's probably-- definitely-- changed my life."|I was in a bit of a rough place before I'd first joined Starlight, and, well, both it and Reborn really helped me with that."`I really needed a change of scenery-- and Reborn gave me an outlet where that could happen."vI think some people kind of see me as "Oh, you're that person who's working on something dev-related constantly?""6Or, "Wait, how many fangames do you work on now?""SOr, "Hey, you've been on Aseprite for 4 days straight, do you need some help?""And like, true!"QBut it really just brings me the most massive amount of pure joy to work on."+And here we are, at the end of it all,"[Call me emotional, but I've definitely cried a few times while writing this whole bit."yI love this community, this game, and my friends dearly, and I'm grateful that they've stuck with me through it all."RIf I might be a little self-indulgent and quote my favorite Reborn character,"*What a happy ending I've fallen into."gCRIM: ...Whew, that was a lot. Sorry about that! Thanks for sticking around and listening, though."/I hope you enjoy the game as much as I do~"5Is there anything else you'd like to talk about?"GCRIM: Oh, you're curious about what I do for the game? Sure thing!"}So if you've been reading these in order, I mentioned before that I was originally pulled onto Reborn after Starlight's demo."hI was originally just a wee smol spriter on Starlight-- I just did the character overworld sprites."dWhen approaching Ame about Reborn, I was like, "Well, hey, I can offer support for spritework!""GOh, by the way, I'm also really interested in learning how to map."0And it kind of just... spiraled from there."UHonestly, at this point I'm struggling to remember what happened in what order--"�One of my first projects was when Ame asked me and Sam (that Smeargle over there!) about character backsprites for Mix 'n Match."nI got overexcited, and I think I ended up smashing out over twenty backsprites in like, less than a week."�I had a lot of fun coming up with poses that I thought would be fitting for each character! I also redid quite a few old backsprites as well."<By this point, minus those that already existed in E18,"LI think I've made most of the backsprites for the different characters?"�Spritework has been a pretty big part of my job here, mainly because it's what I'm comfiest with, but I dove into a lot of different categories!"�For this next section, I'll only mention certain things if you've completed their quest, as to not spoil anyone for something you might not have seen yet!"#So come back later and say hi!"#So for Celebi, to start with--"nTaube, Elena, and Shelly, along with the different maps in Celebi, were really my first big solo project."oI conceptualized, designed, and sprited all three of them, and I'm really proud of how they've turned out!"rFor Darkrai, PULSE Hypno and Camerupt were also mine in both design and sprites, along with the quest's maps!"SI know those two have been PULSE fights that people have been dying for, so...",I hope they've lived up to expectation!"1...So, standing here at the end of it all..."�There's a lot of different things for the different quests I've done, and I'd probably be here for several years if I tried to list it all."WNeoteric Isle, Zina's design and sprites, PULSE Arceus and Mime's overworlds, too!"9I remapped Apophyll Cave and Route 3's cave network!"AAnd all of the Pokémon Centers you see throughout the game!"�Oh, the Shaymin and Tao trio quests were also mine! Those two I'm particularly proud of, and I hope people enjoyed them as well!"{Anna's Dreamsick sprites are also a favorite-- they were sketched and done from scratch, and I'm really proud of them!";I hope they made for a fun and climactic final battle!"8Thanks for sticking through all the way to the end!"5CRIM: ...Okay, we're back from the conditionals?"+Basically, I've been all over the map."�I redid a huge chunk of Pokémon battler sprites-- mainly Gen 6 and 7-- and cleaned up a <i>lot</i> of NPC battle sprites-- a few main characters, too!"aI did a few move animations, including a Z-Move-- Psychic Fangs was my first ever animation!"�Jumped into writing dialogue near the end, too-- I helped with writing a little for the Nightclub and the Elite Four, as well as other random bits of dialogue here and there."<A bit of teambuilding, eventing, and puzzle design too!"AYou could say I'm probably somewhat of a jack of all trades?"Or an ace in the hole!"
Hehe."/Or at least I like to consider myself one!"Speaking of--"�If you've been around me for approximately ten seconds in the past year, you'll know that I am physically incapable of shutting up about Ace."VThey're one of the things ingame that mean the most to me, and I love them a lot."`If you're reading this from a save that's pre-E19 and haven't seen them, then....... oops!!")And you should go play early game!!!"iSame as with a few other characters, I designed and then sprited them, and I'm dearly proud of them."�I've probably said this about twenty times in this category alone, but I hope that others enjoy their presence ingame as much as I do!"CRIM: ...Okay! Uh."That was a lot!"�Honestly, it's a bit comical writing it all out like this, but it actually really means a lot to me that I've been able to do so many different things."FI count myself really lucky to be able to try so many new things."�I'm hugely grateful to Ame not just for trusting me with handing me all these different things to do, but also just the opportunity to do them at all."�She and Cass have been a huge support in both personal life and dev, have helped me try things out of my comfort zone-- and been patient with me if I screwed up said things, too!"DI think that about covers it for things I've done for the game!"EBut like, if you want an exhaustive list of <i>everything</i>..."Hit me up sometime!"WCRIM: Okay, I know I just said that I don't know what to say to these, but like..."9I <i>really</i> don't know how to talk about myself."/Let me at least introduce myself properly."Uh... hi!"I'm Crim!"eAs of the time of writing this, I'm in my last quarter of college, and I'm in my early twenties."RIf you've seen me around the server, you might know me better as, let's see--".That person who speaks in 50% cat emotes."-Or uses way too many exclamation points!"9I'm a Communications major, with a minor in Theater."8I've been around the community since... early 2019?"SEven then, I only really became active when joining Starlight dev in mid 2020."`Before that though, I'd still been playing Reborn! I started in E6! So about... 2013? 2014?"dI regret that I hadn't been able to find the community-- not just the game-- sooner than I did,"*But better late than never, you know?"�I've got a whole category dedicated to Reborn, so assuming you're reading these in order, you've already read about my experience with it!"6But as for what it really means to me personally?"jI'm going to take a leaf out of Vulpes' book, and just roll out the yellow caution tape really quick."dIt's currently 4:34 AM, so I'm a little more emotional than normal-- which is saying something."WSo if you're not up for it, please take the opportunity to back out if you'd like!"CRIM: Alrighty."|So this is probably evident either from the rest of my dialogue-- or if you've spent more than a few minutes around me,"HBut I've had a pretty severe case of anxiety-- for a long time now."I hold myself as a person and my work to a really high standard, and tend to overthink and spiral over this to an extreme."�This was especially prevalent when working on Reborn-- I'd freeze up at the thought of even starting something, out of fear I'd mess it up."OOr couldn't live up to some arbitrary expectation that I'd set for myself."1It was the sort of thinking that was like..."aThis is really going to be in Reborn? This is the big leagues now, it <i>has</i> to be good."ZSo I'd get extremely hung up on the tiniest of details and paralyze myself over them."�It was the same with interaction-- I struggled with feeling as if I couldn't meet a standard of simply existing in a space without feeling as if I was intruding or in the way."rI tend to worry about others over myself often, and want to make sure people are comfortable and happy, so..."3It was kind of a constant presence in my head."\Honestly, I'd be lying to myself if I said it wasn't a problem I'm still fighting with."cBut Reborn itself, especially the dev server and the friends within it-- has really helped me."mIt was a comfort to have a space where I could just be, without getting caught up in intrusive thoughts.")Baby steps, but we're getting there."KI certainly wouldn't be making the same progress as I am without them."EA friend sent me a song once-- one of its lyrics goes like this:"GLife is not the things that we do, it's who we're doing them with."And... yeah."bLike, Reborn's been an unforgettable experience to work on-- wouldn't trade it for the world."PBut everyone on the team has really made that journey all the more special."*Ame, for inviting me on this journey,"HAnd everyone else in this room with me, and even those who aren't--"8It really wouldn't have been the same without them,"4And I'm proud to call all of them dear friends."NCRIM: And well, if any of this happens to be relatable to anyone reading?"WKnow that you're not alone, and you deserve to give yourself a little more credit.":People care for you and love you more than you think."fIf you're struggling with doing the things that you want to do-- it's okay to give yourself time."PSurround yourself with people that see you as the joy you are to be around,"BAnd treat you with the same kindness and love as you deserve."8Of course, it's not something that comes overnight.";I know I get caught up in those kinds of thoughts too."kBut I hope that someday-- if that day isn't today-- you'll be able to see just how brightly you shine."3...Would you like to talk about anything else?"CRIM: Of course.""Please take care of yourself!""I hope you have a lovely day~",Or night, whenever you're reading this!"%CRIM: Oh? You're approaching me?"+Okay, but I'm more prepared this time!">I'll have you know, I'm still kind of awful at this game!"That has not changed!"(...But you know how I can fix that?"With a big heckin' sword!"Let's go!!"2Aww, shoot. I'll be sure to ace it next time~""CRIM: Okay, sorry, um, heck--" That wasn't in the cards--?"(I'm proud of you though, great job!":Here, I'll fix up your team and you can have some BP."+...And, hey, as a gift from me to you!"Just this once!"Here's a few extra BP!"As a treat."8You've come this far, and honestly, you deserve it!"*That brings you to... \v[593] BP now!";CRIM: ...Oh. I wasn't expecting to actually win there."'That's okay though, you did great!"Let me fix up your team."(You've definitely got it next time!"Oh, and by the way?"#I hope that my Vulpix got you!"CRIM: Okay!"2Fair warning, I'm kind of awful at this game!"\But when you're allowed to give a team of just your favorite Pokémon a little... help?"Even I can stand a chance!"...Hopefully."Bring it!" CRIM: Alrighty, no problem!"/I hope you enjoy the rest of the dev room~"#And the rest of the game, too!"5I'm glad that you were able to make it this far."All the way to the end!"_I hope you've been able to make as many fond memories from this game as I've been able to."$Some days, they're all we have."5You've still got some great things ahead of you!"ZI hope you have-- or are able to make-- as many fond memories from this game as I do."rAUTUMN: Oh, hi there! Welcome to the Dev Room! This is uhh.. I guess where we all just kinda relax and chill?"yIt's rough out there in this great wide region, though I suppose we have you to thank for fixing that up a bit, huh?"So! What can I do for you?"fA battle? All right, I'll have you know I competed in a tournament against everyone in this room!"I placed..."Dead last."So I grabbed a cool sword!"Maybe another time, then?"�AUTUMN: Okay fine! Here, I was saving these for another Explosion TM from Sinnoh that I've heard lowers the opposing Pokémon's defense..."$But, I guess you can have them."#That'll put you at \v[593] BP."<AUTUMN: Oof, I didn't expect I'd actually win, haha...."jHonestly I'm not the greatest at battling. Just pretty good at finding funny ways to cheese the game."|We're actually about to have a tournament in this room to see who's actually the best! I just hope I don't come last..."<Hopefully this will be good practice! Don't hold back!!"{I have a strict rule to never talk about myself unless prompted, and while I understand that you clicked the chat button..."0You're just gonna have to be more specific!"aUm, please? \ch[62,-1,Who are you?,What do you do?,What does Reborn mean to you?,Nevermind.]"CAUTUMN: Well, as you may have already read, my name is Autumn!"[Though, if you're an older member of the community, you might know me better as Inuki."jYeah, that Inuki. Of Porygon2 bridge fame. Alas, that was a few genders and plenty of life lived ago."qOutside of that... Who am I? Heck if I know, but here! I'll give you 5 fun facts instead of a proper answer!"`Fact 1: You see that dude sitting a tile away from me? His positioning isn't a coincidence!"THe's been my best friend for literally more than half of my life! (I'm 27 btw.)"�The butterfly effect is silly to think about. Stepping on a butterfly just makes you rude, it's highly improbable anything will come of it."[But meeting him? That's the event that really kicked off every other event in my life."SAnswering who I am is literally impossible without mentioning his involvement."II love you, fam. Thanks for all your help in paving the road I walk."2Fact 2: Mega Diancie is my favorite Pokémon!"WFact 3: Once, while programming something involving field effects way back when...".Like, a few episodes after they came out."{I forgot that case statements existed and instead created a nested if statement that contained no less than 30 "end"s."#All lined up at the end of it.".Fact 3.5: I was a computer science major."	Was."UFact 4: My appearance here is based on my Dungeons and Dragons character: Deneb!"�She's currently an Archfey warlock who gained the favor of a bunch of fae butterflies, eventually revealed to be her father's old swarm!"vHe was kind of a jerk and maybe so are they? Being a jerk seems to be a trait of that side of the family, though."....Anyway....."XThe tiny child on the couch closer to the back is the DM of that campaign actually!"kI've used it a lot to get comfortable with referring to myself with different pronouns over the years."xBut more importantly it's a really good story! It's been a blast to cooperatively write it with them every session!"PFact 5: I find it very likely that I have a fairly severe case of the ADHD."~This isn't anything particularly groundbreaking, and by the time the game releases this question will have been answered."YWe'll see if I remember to come back and fix this, or if it stays like this forever.":Phew, okay! Is there anything else you wanted to ask?"#All right, a different prompt!"3Gotcha, please enjoy the rest of the dev room!"?Precious little, compared to everyone else in this room..."�The more interesting answer is that I'm one of the move animators. I make the funny pictures move when you click buttons in battle."~I word it like this because I do not create the funny pictures that do the moving. I have no real artistic ability whatsoever."yI don't have the ability to visualize images in my head. I can't see what something will look like without doing it."KI have very strong opinions on how I want the moves I animate to feel."mUnfortunately this makes me remarkably unproductive when I can't put that feeling to paper, so to speak."gThat mixed with my terrible work ethic definitely led me to be the least productive member by far."�When I do finally make something though, I try to put my whole heart into it! I hope that shows, especially during Full Power Z-Moves!"6Anyway, is there anything else you wanted to ask?"|So if you're reading these in order, you may notice that I seemed pretty bummed about my relative lack of contribution."NPerhaps that's just a natural reaction, a way anybody like me might feel."iBut I feel that way because I absolutely love this game, and, at least my memories of the community."�So back in the day, right? My best friend and I were scrolling through Pokémon Online servers, trying to find an enjoyable place."KAs you may be aware of, not all communities are welcoming to everyone."QIt just so happens that my favorite anime is called "Katekyo Hitman Reborn!""USo when I came across a server with Reborn in its name, monkey brain went click."8What a marvelous coincidence that turned out to be."oA few years pass, Ame starts making a cool game, I play it as you do. I don't really think anything of it."nThe details are blurry, but my first act as a "Dev" was filling in the pages of the Field Effect Library."[Basically cooking up 100 pots of copypasta and draping the noodles into digital books."kIt was a good time, I enjoyed feeling helpful! Eventually I simply became a general purpose assistant."`Were there a thing to do that wasn't particularly complicated, I would be the one to do it!"tLike making a bunch of cliffs, remaking Route 2 three times, calculating how much soup could fit in a mountain."OAme, Dan, and I were in a Skype call regularly. It was a really good time!"|Eventually the animation:tm: project started cause the animations that came with essentials were, how you say... weirdchamp."pI remember Ame had already made a few that were really sick but then her hand decided to be a bit dramatic."#So she showed me how to do it!"So I started doing it!"jAnd now here I am! Incredibly grateful for the opportunity that Ame has given me to work on her game."UAnd incredibly grateful for the home her community has been for the past........"Very long time."5I hope it's a significantly longer time to come."<AUTUMN: Oh, okay! Enjoy the rest of the dev room, then!"kAUTUMN: Oh,\| right,\| yeah,\| sure,\| of course.\| Hey, before you go, what's your favorite Pokémon?"9AUTUMN: 3...\| 2...\| 1...\| Andddd...\.\.\. Bang.\|"-No idea what you put in that text box.\|"*But it's removed from the game now.\|"$I hope being rude was worth it.">:["AJAN: Hi! Hello! Bet you didn't think you'd see me down here?"AI mean, yeah, technically this isn't <i>really</i> my world."7Well, technically I've been to this world first..."$Um... Forget about all of that!"JAN: So, what do you need?"8JAN: Oh... Yeah, we do that in this world don't we?"WBattling? Um, admittedly I'm not the best at that. I'm still an intern, after all!"But I'll do my best!">:C"JAN: Fuck."+Okay, okay... You win fair and square."EI'll have my revenge on you yet. Maybe not in this world, but..."ASomewhere, someplace, the cycle of suffering will never end."`We'll play forever and ever and ever and ever until we get the ending we're satisfied with."Karma's a bitch."=JAN: All right, enough of that. You have \v[593] BP now.";JAN: This is just the lemonade stand all over again..."=JAN: You wanna chat? Sure! What do you wanna chat about?"JAN: Yeah. That's my lore."4Right now I'm a senior at Axis High University."EI'm required to take up an internship job before I can graduate."BBut between you and me... None of that really matters anyway."NIt's a way to "tie up loose ends" and justify my existence in this world."That's one of the rules, right? If there's no justification for my existence then I'll just disappear into little bitty pixels."EYou look confused? I think I have that effect on people a lot..."5Well, don't try to think about it too much, yes?""JAN: Ooh, you were listening!"6Okay, so that's half truth. I am from this world!"2In fact, it's where I was born. Conceptually."YBut eventually, after some time I was able to leave using the process of "blooming".";I bloomed! After that I left and created my own world."Technically..."AIt wasn't all me. I have friends who came with me and stuff."EHey, what's that look for? You act as if I'm talking nonsense...">All of this makes sense, trust me. I wouldn't lie to you."mJAN: Admittedly, I stole this option from Cass because I think a lot of what she says applies to me too."WBut I think it's sort of an understatement to say that Reborn has changed my life."EI was sort of aimless and without purpose before I found Reborn."oThen I saw how much work Ame put into this world and I decided I wanted to try and apply myself similarly."KThat's how I was able to "bloom" and create the world of Rejuvenation."tThat bloom wasn't exactly pretty... A lot of my early attempts were met with some backlash and stuff like that."7It was my first time creating a new world, jeez..."TI had no idea creating an entirely new line of existence would be so much work."EIt took a lot of time, but I think I got the hang of things now.">I guess you could say I owe everything to Ame and Reborn."My internship is ending..."XJAN: That answer changes a lot. At first it was Dusclops, then it was Chandelure..."FRight now as of uh... January 23rd 2022 at 10:23 pm it's Claydol."IJAN: Have you been to Aegir Cave? You've definitely been to Iolia..."?Well, those two areas are what pop into my mind right now."1I really hope I'm not forgetting anything..."JAN: Cya."IKARU: Oh, uh, sorry."gI sometimes find myself looking back on everything that brought me here, and I space out a little.".It's just a lot to think about, you know?"\Every choice I've made, however small, nudging me a little in one direction or another."WLike a visual novel, but, you know, for real, and without the relationship points."v... Or maybe with them! Just don't try Blue Moon Ice Cream on real people as a shortcut. It takes more than that."Anyway, I'm Ikaru. I do the little stuff that people COULD do themselves, when their time is better spent on things I can't do."jI also play new versions of the game before most people, when they're the most broken, so that's fun."bThere's a chance you're not here to listen to my musing though, so I'll leave that up to you."RIKARU: Hi again. Want to talk for a bit? Or maybe you're just here to battle?"eIKARU: Sure thing. I told Ame that I would try not to write too much, but, once I get into it..."gWell, Ikaru from the future that has finished writing these is here to warn you, there's... a lot."mWhat sounds most interesting? \ch[62,-1,Pre- Reborn,Early Reborn and League,Game Involvement,Reflection]"5The olden times, huh. Sure. So, full disclosure:"�I'm just going to pretend that I don't know that Autumn over there will have said the exact same things that I'm going to say here at one point or another.""Fun fact for the class first:"�Before I started going by Ikaru, I had a different alias, well over like, 13 years ago now. And I know, that's not a very fun fact by itself, but..."FSay, have you ever fought the Grand Hall trainers on a Wednesday?"ESpecifically, the one with the Xatu and (Mega-)Mawile from hell?"xThe one who says some cryptic "you don't know who I am" stuff? Psychic Silva? Yeah, that's me. Or, well, it WAS me."�But hold on, before you start accusing me of stealing your childhood crush's first kiss or something out of some war-flashback-esque anger,"xI didn't make those teams, it was just stuff I liked that needed to be seen in-game... somewhere. Sorry, not sorry!"�That aside: my earliest internet days in middle school were spent on the Serebii forums, writing a really bad Pokemon fanfiction, which,"Hopefully,"pWill never see the light of day again. If you know, you know, and if you don't, well, it's better that way."�So like I said, this was in middle school. I had a few friends on the forums, kind of, but not many of them stuck around long term because of course not."�There was one, though, that I knew irl too, and- well, actually, "stuck around" isn't a good phrase for him either, more like he..."^... suddenly reappeared in Reborn, out of thin air in the left field like 10 years later?"�And that by itself is wild to me, like, I live by the phrase "timing is everything" and all our choices yada yada I said that already,"�But the degree to which we were completely different people than we were back then is staggering. We weren't even THAT close, but,"bIf you happen to be reading this, shoutout to you, friend. I'm glad we both made it this far."�So, next came the Marriland forums. I put myself out there a bit more, and wrote less (read: wrote no) fanfiction. I dabbled a little in competitive Pokemon."hThis was 4th gen, and I was just starting to be less uptight about "super broken" overused Pokemon."�(And, like, good for me because I was missing out on so many cool things in favor of... *checks notes* ... Swords Dance Quick Attack Zangoose.)"�On a fateful July afternoon in 2007, I was scrolling the "wi-fi battles" subforum and the thread I chose to respond to was the start of everything."EThe thread starter was someone who... Ah, what were her words..."JA few genders and plenty of life lived later, is now known as Autumn."ZThe green one a single tile away from here, yeah. That placement is very intentional."�We became real good friends using our Nintendo DS wi-fi, even when she had to hide the fact that she was friends with strangers online from her mom."And, like, fair."Eventually she invited me to her own forum for her friends, which, when I joined, had a staggering two (2) active members."�We hung out there all the time, doing whatever we wanted with whatever nonsense topics and stuff because it was pretty much just the two of us."�She invited more and more people and we had a fun little group that did battling, roleplaying, art, children's card games, you name it."}One of the people she invited was her friend Wolfie, and if you know me well enough, you already know the significance there."�If you don't, just know that she's a blessing. A past version of me might argue that I don't deserve her, and that past version of me is wrong,"5Though I do my best to be worth it all the same."�It is no small exaggeration to say that those two are the single (uh, double?) most important people in my life and I would not be where I am now without them."zI love them both dearly and I'm glad that they've stuck around through everything. I couldn't ask for better friends."@...Whew. Sorry, I'm sure you weren't expecting all of that.""Thanks for listening, though."&Want to talk about anything else?"+My early Reborn experience, huh? Sure."JWould you believe me joining this community was entirely an accident?"9Ah, well, maybe a better term is "misunderstanding.""�You see, Autumn and I are fans of the anime "Katekyo Hitman Reborn!" and when we first made the switch from NetBattle to Pokemon Online,"All the way back in 2010,"ZWe saw a server that was named "Reborn Server" and we didn't think too hard about it."4YOOOOOO it's Reborn we said, joining instantly."$Best mistake we made that year."yThe League was already a thing when we joined, though the server was still a tiny baby compared to what we have now."�I signed up pretty instantly for funsies with a team that was... questionable. I remember my first battle was actually pretty significant."�Not for me though, for Hardy. Titania was newly revealed and he said that if he won his next battle, he would go challenge her next."dYanno, as he does, trying to prove Rock-types can still hold up to the all-powerful Steel-type."gAnd I was the unlucky sucker that thought shit was sweet, with a pretty weak team, and got Rocked."	Heh."�Then I made a better team and fought Corey, and to say he was a stark contrast to my last opponent is an understatement. Both in character and difficulty."\Cal was next, and I got slapped, then I rematched Hardy and won. Rematched Cal and won."�Next was Florinia. And boy did she beat me up for a long while. A battle between us was the 666th log, fun fact. Eventually I fought Heather instead,"6Who, by the way, was an entry leader at the time,"�And won first try. And let me tell you, I was the ONLY one who did. The fact that she's part of the Elite Four in this game is not coincidence."�Her rank shot up real shortly after that, and first of all, my trainer card looked real funny with all the empty space between her badge and the rest."gAnd man, the relief I felt knowing I didn't have to fight her again after she stepped it up, haha."VI interacted with the leaders pretty often, and some had more to say than others."eBy far my favorite group was none other than the OTS gang; Titania, Florinia, Amaria, and Julia."gI built up a bit of a reputation as a knight in not-so- shining armor, no points for guessing why."\The interactions I had with Titania and Amaria were like, the talk of the whole league."And then there was El."�Let's just say I'm glad I never have to fight him again. My team had Dragon Dance Dragonite as a win condition and it backfired every time."&Can't stand Ditto anymore hahaha."}I sure gave it to him in the X-League though. Resorted to a Chilan Berry on my Darkrai to survive Arceus and put it to sleep."]I got really into everything and it was a blast. I was the second one to win the league!"lHave you done the spirit hunting quest in Victory Road? If you did, then you saw my team at some point."�If you ask me if I regret it, knowing what I know now... Nah, definitely not. I feel like my own character developed as much as any of the leaders' did."�Nowadays I'm a lot more relaxed, I think, but there's always a little bit of Titania chilling under the surface for whenever I need her to come out."$... Not that it needs to. Much."�Anyway, I'd say the League was definitely one of the highlights of my experience. Hopefully you enjoyed the little trip down memory lane."-My involvement with the game, huh? Sure."�Well, like I said when I introduced myself, I mostly do a lot of small, boring stuff that other people can definitely do themselves."{Difference between them and me is I don't know how to do all that much, so the really cool stuff is best left to them."ZFull transparency, this event is like the only eventing I've done in the entire game."�Uh, well, unless you count scattering hidden items in the new city and the Chrysolia Spring. But that was just copying and pasting events, really."�Speaking of the spring, though, I filled in all the walls there once Ame laid down the outline. I did that for a few maps, actually."?A couple of the mountains in the desert were my doing too."ZAnd let's see... There's also the Tanzan Depths, the maps in the cave in Tanzan Cove."�That was also the one time I had a little fun and left something funny that no one will see unless they open up the map in RMXP or something."�I think my favorite niche talent is the power to find double spaces in text. When I first joined the dev server, I made my name "melee marth player,""3Because my attention to spacing is IMMACULATE."jTo be clear, when I say "double space" I mean the difference between "this phrase" and "this phrase.""�I can also tell when Pokemon names have a space before them, when the nicknaming window puts one there automatically for... some reason."�Outside of actual work on the game, I also play the game! The wild west versions where maybe everything works and maybe it doesn't!"�During my testing of E19, my Palkia was named "no." and my Dialga was named "yes!" because I had a 2 hour struggle with Palkia and then Dialga was like,"cOkay, I'll get in the frame 1 Quick Ball I guess, and Dialga was the one I wanted more anyway!"(Hopefully it's easier for you guys."�Aside from that, I try to keep reported bugs listed in our Official(tm) Cat(tm) Reporting Spreadsheet so that it's at least organized."3Honestly, huge shoutout to everyone else here."vThe difference in that spreadsheet when everything that's "Done" is hidden compared to how much has been on it..."�It's like night and day. The bugs- ah, cats, never stop, but looking back on everything that didn't work before that does now is insane.";Remember to show your appreciation for everyone, okay?"ZReflection... Well, I'm no Serra, but I sure do think about this kind of thing a lot."nI like music a lot, which isn't particularly unique or anything, but it plays into a lot of my character."qIn places like your generic "About Me"s and, like, status messages and all that, I quote songs all the time."RIf we're friends on Final Fantasy XIV, my search info is always a song quote."DThere's a few lyrical quotes here and there even in this event."�The placeholder dialogue Ame left here for my pre- battle message was a joke about that, since it's so ingrained into my personality haha."�My biggest inspiration is the Japanese musician Aimer. I really love the celestial themes and late night vibes in her earlier music."kIt was a tweet from her in 2018 that really motivated me to get up and finish my college registration."�She said "I wonder if some of you started a new life today" among other things, and I read that and thought "yeah, okay." So I did!"kMy college major was always astronomy, but discovering someone like her really solidified my interest.":My favorite song is, perhaps unsurprisingly, Polaris."�It's sad, but at the same time, motivational. And it's always- ... well, usually, the melancholy stuff that hits me the hardest."uI say "usually," because it's not my FAVORITE song, but LIGHTS's "Timing Is Everything" is, like, my life motto."cThe chorus of the song says "There I was, none the wiser, both of us, different trajectories,""PWho'd have thought we'd be right here, in this spot, timing is everything.""4And it just makes me think. Despite everything,"AThe hundreds of thousands of years that humans have existed,"<You and I are here in the same place, at the same time."IUh, well, same "place" and same "time," but don't sweat the details."�Everything we are is just a huge combination of wacky coincidences, or, like, such small choices. If I hadn't met Autumn in 2007, I wouldn't be here now."BIf I hadn't signed up for the League, I wouldn't be here now."XIf Ame hadn't succumbed to her whims and made a game, none of us would be here now." But we are. Isn't it great?"^I, for one, am glad you're here and hopefully enjoying yourself. Stick around, won't you?")IKARU: Ah. To the death it is, then."... Just kidding!"OYou've been through a lot to get where you are now, haven't you, Champion?"7Did you get what you wanted out of your adventure?"GI'm glad to hear it. I hope the same is true of your next journey."CWell, there's not always some deeper meaning, and that's okay."VHere you stand, at the end of a journey 10 years in the making. You've done well."]With your quest said and done, how about a little something with no stakes to wind down?":And yet, there's even more out there waiting for you."]When we're finished here, make sure you see things all the way through for me, will you?"6And when that's done, tell me your favorite part!"-(Bonus points if it's this interaction!)"IKARU: Round two, huh?"'You'll touch the stars in no time."KI did my Adrienn impression already, but the sentiment is still there."Just a little higher..."*Morning waits on the edge of a dream."HIKARU: I expect no less from someone who's come as far as you have."1Here's some Battle Points for your troubles."rAnd hey, you know what, there's only two people here that I don't outrank, and they can't tell me what to do."{Here's one (1) more, just this once. You've come so far, and frankly, these battles are a little stacked against you, haha."1That brings you to... \v[593] points, is it?"wIKARU: Well, teams of just our favorites weren't really going to stand up to endgame players without some... help."aI'll get your squad all fixed up, and if you have any complaints, I'm innocent; Cass did it!"IKARU: Alright."8Hey, if you ever get lost, just look up at the sky."8If you can see the stars, they'll show you the way."1Your next meeting is just around the corner.";MARCELLO: Hi there, I'm Marcello, I work on this game."QDo not believe the sprite I have been given for the purposes of bullying me,"0I am not, in fact, a child with green hair."So, what's up?"7MARCELLO: I'm pretty terrible at Pokémon, myself."UBut turns out, when you can just cheat and make your team utter unfair bullshit?"3Even I can come up with something pretty good."Bring it on!"#MARCELLO: Good job, have a BP!"x...I feel like these dev fights are probably way too difficult to reward just 3 BP, but that's just how things are."You've got \v[593] BP now."7MARCELLO: Hey, don't worry, we all lose sometimes."-If I can offer some constructive advice."&That thing you did in our battle?"CWhere you let all your mons' HP go to zero before my mons' HP?"#Yeah, don't do that next time."Should help you win.".MARCELLO: You want to know more about me?"(Well sure, if you insist. Ask away!"MARCELLO: I'm Marcello!"ESome random British guy that tripped and fell onto the Dev Team."hOnce upon a time, I was the newest member of the team, I felt like a kid compared to everyone else.">(Speaking of, despite the sprite, I'm not a kid. I'm 25.)"W(Ame, who is SHORTER THAN ME, liked to tease me about my height once upon a time.)"�(I have no idea about the exact joke origins, it was forever ago but hey I ended up with a child's sprite, we all have to live with this now.)"Anyway, tangent aside."/That time I was the 'new kid' on the team?"Was seven years ago."KI have worked on this game my entire adult life, which is crazy to me."SAnd with any luck, I can continue working to make games with Ame and the team,"(For the rest of my adult life, too."!Did you want to ask me more?"All right, see you around.",MARCELLO: Oh, well I'm a mathematician."?...But I assume you mean with regards to this game, right?"7Well, when I first started it was as a programmer!"gI knew nothing about that kind of thing though, but I learnt on the job and fixed a bunch of bugs."nAnd all in all wrote lots and lots of code that Cass or Perry or myself would eventually have to rewrite." Because it sucked real bad.":But I like to think I got pretty good over the years."$I got the online stuff working!"&I fixed numerous persistent bugs!"dWhen we completely rewrote the AI, I was the one that programmed that (though Ame designed it)."EAll these big things I've done have something in common, though."sIn the last year or so, Cass or Perry have completely redone my work in these areas and made them much better."And I couldn't be happier!"xI like to think I provided a good starting point, and seeing some incredibly talented team members improve on that,"7To make stuff that seems to work pretty damn well!"{I find that very cool, and I can't help but be proud of myself and even more proud of this amazing team I'm a part of."(But programming isn't all I can do!"TThis last year of development, I had to step back for a bit because of illness.",(Don't worry, reader, all is well now.)"_And when I got back I was out of practice, not to mention that Cass and Perry are so cool,"MThere wasn't too much even left to do on the programming side of things."2But turns out this nerd quite enjoys writing."QAnd I like to think I'm pretty good at it-- something which Ame agrees with!"KSo for the last segment of development I was writing dialogue instead!"PMy biggest contribution is the Celebi Quest, if you've played that already."3That was designed, evented, and written by me!"P(Lots of thanks to Crim and Ame for the graphical assets ur both great. <3)"-I even made all the battle teams for it!"gBut I've also done other bits throughout postgame, small bits in other quests, among other things."uI'm sure I could tell you more about the other things I worked on specifically, but that would take long enough,"4We'll just say that's a story for another time."xRegardless, writing for the game and seeing the other developers (and hopefully players like you) enjoy my writing,"&Has given me huge amounts of joy!"[I'm so excited that everyone can finally play the game and see the work I put into it!"6I think that pretty much covers my contributions!"MARCELLO: I mean, so much."SEven before I was a developer, I've met so many cool people in this community."^Most of my closest friends are either on this dev team, or were met because of this game."iCall me a big nerd if you want, but I also got really into Dungeons and Dragons thanks to this game."|At this point I've been DMing a campaign for two years whose players have almost exclusively been people I know from Reborn."jShoutout to Ame and Autumn who are both players in the game and are deeply chaotic in their doing so."XAnd have taken it upon themselves to ensure none of my plans ever come to fruition."xBut also my other players who aren't on the team, and people who played in the group in the past but don't anymore?"yKnow that I deeply love and appreciate you all, these last two years have been infinitely better because of you all."And I owe that to Reborn.".I like to think I owe so very much to it."dSo many of the people in this room are some of my best friends, and they're all just wonderful!"bPlus, being in such a supportive community around such great people for the last seven years,":I feel like has shaped me into the person I am today."And I like that person!"lSo I couldn't be more grateful to have been a part of all this, and treasure the friendships I've made."pHere's to the next seven years of my time knowing and working with Ame being just as rewarding as the last."GMARCELLO: I feel deeply unqualified to give advice about anything."But I'll try my best!"JIf you struggle to do the things you want to, don't beat yourself up."�I've spent a lot of time on this team going back and forth between incredibly rapid productivity and paralyzing indecision and inaction."�But I made it, and things got a lot better when I stopped beating myself up every time I felt like I wasn't doing 'good enough'."!I'm sure you'll make it too.";But more than anything, my number one piece of advice?"-Just surround yourself with good people."aPeople you like, people you respect, people you admire, and people you wish to be more like."UIt was entirely accidental, but that's what I did when I joined the Reborn team."bAnd I think, more than anything, that is what lead me to all the best parts of my life today."gI've grown into a person I like, I have wonderful friends, and most importantly of all, I'm happy."GAnd I feel like I owe all of that to the wonderful friends I have."1...Yeah, sorry, if you were hoping for like,".Fangame dev specific advice or something,"
Oops."LBut this is what you get from me, and I hope somebody finds it helpful!"mA notebook with "Noir a blanc" written on the cover is on the desk. The last written page is bookmarked."
Read?"December 18th, 2021"XIt's been a while, hasn't it? Progress has been kind of slow lately, regrettably..."aBut I'm still further along than I would have ever been without your accidental inspiration."2When I go outside at night, in total silence,"[My surroundings lit by nothing more than a few street lights, the moon, and the stars,"3I think of you and your music, and I remember.",You may never know it, but that's okay."uAs long as it motivates me, it doesn't really matter. And maybe someday, I might be able to thank you properly.""PERRY: Hey, hey!" Look who finally showed up."So, what you wanna do?"MPERRY: I can't decide between singles or doubles. So I'll let you choose"ZOh, fun fact! I made the function that temporarily sets your pokémons levels to 100."[But it doesn't set the opponents pokémon to lvl 100, we just have the teams that way.": )"*That's what I expect from our protag!"%PERRY: Nice one! Here's some BP."That puts you at \v[593]."+I hope the AI didn't misplay too hard.">PERRY: Oof, did the lvl 101 thing mess you up that badly?"8PERRY: Sure, I'll think up something to talk about."]Anything specific you want to talk about? \ch[62,-1,Reborn,Game dev, Me, Ramblings, Nah]"/PERRY: Man, there's so much to talk about."/Starting with my introduction to the game."eIt started by watching someone play through the game on Youtube, pkmnRob I think their name was.";Thought it was neat so decided to check it out myself."[I played a few hacked ROMs before, but this was my first time playing on the computer."kAnd then I got my ass handed to me in true Reborn fashion. The one pokémon strat didn't work anymore."EAfter that I just kept on playing, basically no-living the game."POne of the things I love about the game is just how multidimensional it is."nIt's not only about the story, or the battling. It has puzzles, beautiful maps, many sidequests and more."ZAnd I think the game has made me a bit of a better person. Not that I was bad before."MBut I think I came out of it a bit more compassionate and understanding."tI ended up hanging around and checking up on the game every once in a while, playing the updates that came out."6And then Cass made a post about the battle tower."kA person in the comments asked if there would also be a battle factory, a gamemode I enjoy myself too."dCass responded that she'd think it cool, but it would be too much effort to make it worthwhile."+My ego showed up, and went like: "Bet""�It's a miracle, but somehow I actually managed to get it to work.Part of it is the coding language, Ruby. It's pretty easy to pick up, not a lot of foreknowledge required."}So when I almost finished the battle factory I showed it off in the patreon server. Was planning to release it as a mod."kCass said she wanted it in the main game, so I polished it up a bit and sent everything needed for it."nHelped with a few other things, and a while later she asked me if I actually wanted to help out as a dev."*I really have a lot to thank her for."XAfter entering the team I met a lot of awesome people, which are here in this room."(And it has been an awesome journey."-PERRY: But what is it I did in the game?"LIf you're reading in order you know that Cass asked me on the dev team."^That's because all the bugs that had been found after e18 was released had been compiled."_And it was a long list. So to help Marchello, and Azery at the time, out I was brought on."�Like 10 days later I found a way to test where the code takes longest to run. 2 days after that e18.4 was released and optimization galore was a fact."�Cass ran with it way further than I could take it, but I've been making sure things don't crash after she had sledgehammered them."SSo most of the work I've done has just been bugfixing and fixin up after Cass."9But of course, there are also new things I've added!"fThe battle factory, a lot of AI rewrite, online doubles, new field notes, are just a few of them."�It's hard to remember them all, since about 90% of them are just small QoL things. Like the game staying in the same place and speedup persisting when resetting."wThat's about it, really. Most of the work i do isn't visible, since it's not a new thing but fixing the old thing."UPERRY: Hi, I'm Perry or toothpastefairy which isn't really a name I use anymore."1Living that good life at the ripe age of 23."NAnd a masters student studying Applied Physics living in the Netherlands."�Probably addicted to playing chess, since the amount of times I stopped writing all this dialogue and played a quick game online has hit the double digits."jThere's a good chance this is the first time you hear of me, I'm not involved in the community a lot."TSometimes I wish I was, but it's just not something that comes naturally to me."�Meeting new communities and friend groups is always scary, and if the circumstances are not up for it you won't get many words out of me."hI'm sure you have felt like that too a few times, like when going to a new school or maybe a party."|Especially starting a conversation. You'll catch me dead before I talk about myself unprovoked. Unless you're counting this."qBut mostly i don't sweat that stuff too much, it's not who I am to do that and in the end I can accept that."9Anyhow, another thing about me is that I love music!"}High chance that if I'm alone at home, I'm with my headphones on. Not that I have a particularly refined taste in music."\I'm pretty sure that it is as close to basic as you can get, but I enjoy it nontheless."zLike the e4 and champion battle tracks. Absolute bangers, those two. Deffo give them a listen if you haven't already."vOther than that my view of myself seems to oscillate between thinking I'm great and being disappointed in myself."GWhere on some days I hype myself up and feel great about who I am."rAnd other days I feel helpless in trying to live my life in a healthy way and be a person I'm proud of being."dChecking in on my friends, not wasting away a day doing things I won't remember two days later.",And I've been getting better at it too!"0So there, life. I'm getting the hang of it."�PERRY: And what a mistake to select this option. So this is just gonna be my random thoughts, a stream of conciousness if you're familiar with the term."EI do love this game dearly, having had a huge impact on my life."xHelping out on it is an amazing feeling, where for the first time I feel like I'm contributing to something bigger."HAnd the fact that it feels productive working on this too, amazing."vI'm just about the last one writing my dialogue, so I have the advantage of knowing what everybody else has said."]And Vulpes was really able to nail down how I feel about contributing to Reborn as well."cI'm not too good a writer, so I'll gladly point to others when they better express how I feel."�And we do have a lot of talented writers in this room here. That should be no surprise to you, most of them contributed to the story of Reborn which we love so much."IOne of my favorite parts was walking around in the desert with Taka."�Did you know that Taka has the most dialogue in the game? Or at least, the text "TAKA:" appears 1.5x more than any other "CHARACTER:" in the game."AAzzie wrote a really sweet fic about it as well, go read it!"kYeah I'm still in love with the game. But now I appreciate the work the others put in it all the more."|It's funny, since I don't even game that much anymore. I think that in the last 5 years I've played a total of 3 games."qGot sucked in the world of fanfiction instead I guess. If only at school those counted as books you've read."lBut anyway, you're probably holding the X button down to skip this dialogue so I'll end your suffering."Have fun out there!"PERRY: Cool, see ya."0Talk to the others too, they're very sweet!"AZZIE: Hi there!"Thanks for stopping by!"(I hope you've been enjoying Reborn!"\This game means so much to so many people, I'm really glad you stuck it out to the end."QThere's some pretty great stuff still ahead of you, I'll tell you that much."@Was there something in particular you'd like to talk about?"+AZZIE: I do like talking about Reborn!"USo compared to most people in this room, my history with Reborn is pretty short."XIn 2017-ish, I found out about the game through a friend of mine tweeting about it."�He posted a picture of the inside of Sweet Kiss Candy shop, I mistook it for a Pokecentre, and immediately decided I had to play this game."�Of course, then I actually started playing, and... Well, let's just say Julia kicked my butt so badly I put the game down and forgot about it."For a couple years."uIn February of 2019, I decided to try it again, and-- while I wasn't much better-- I at least had more patience."aI ended up falling completely in love with the game. The characters, the music, the world..."4It made me, and continues to make me, so happy."@Reborn actually ended up reigniting my passion for writing."7More than that, I fell in love with the community!"tI made some incredible friends, some of whom are in this room with me, and I wouldn't trade them for the world."YIn late 2020, I messaged Ame, asking if she needed any help with last-minute things."]A while later, she decided she could use some help with the Nightclub, and so here I am!"iAll the Trainers you can battle in the Battle Pavillion, their little dialogues, were my department!"�I also worked on some of the characters' chatter while hanging out in the club itself-- so go say hi to folks, if you haven't already!"xThis game and community mean so much to me, and I'll always be grateful for how kind and wonderful everyone's been."AZZIE: Oh! Okay, uh, hi!"I'm Azzie."ZI'm a Canadian gal, and at the time this is being published, I'm in my late twenties."~Apart from Reborn (and sundry other fangames, and Pokemon in general) I'm also a musician, animal lover, and storyteller."�I'm so passionate about stories, in all their forms. How they can bring people together, heal people, bring joy and catharsis...":Definitely one of my favourite things to think about."AZZIE: Okay!"
